{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves","id":592622,"title":"Norse and Nerves","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-16T08:01:17-07:00","id":592622,"title":"Norse and Nerves","content":"Hello all,<br /> <br /> I am an inexperienced ST who's trying to resurrect my first Scion game by request of the players. Not sure why it petered out in the first place, but I suspect it had something to do with long drives and a bit of chaos in life. Since I've never made it past Hero-level in a Scion game, I'm writing this chronicle to both entertain and to be open to advice.<br /> <br /> Here's a part of the setting, I'll update the rest when I have more time.<br /> <br /> Taking place in New York City, a Band of four were created on the same night when their divine parents performed a Visitation. Lad Gould is the son of Baldur and one of NYC's finest. Noble and talkative, he received a pet wolf and a sword that can be transformed into a bracer, while granting him the purviews Guardian and Sun. Katya is the daughter of Hel and a mortician. Supposedly a cynic, she now has access to the Death &amp; Magic boons through a leather belt, while wielding a scythe. Her pet isn't much of a pet. A Gambian Rat she has dubbed 'Janah', the large rodent can speak to her and her alone. Vjun is the son of Vidar and a hunter. Reluctantly away from his preferred domain of woods and solitude, he has a chestplate that gives him frost armor with the cost of a legend point, along with vambraces to channel Justice. Finally, he has a ferret. No, it can't talk. Yes, it is smarter than the average ferret. But, in Vidar's eyes, it's an insult gift to show his displeasure at Vjun's hiding away from society. Lastly, Jamie 'Moriarty', criminal consultant and daughter of Loki. Mischevious, she now has five tattoos with the runes for Fire, Frost, Magic, Chaos, and Illusion. But her preferred weapon is a Remington who has seen gleeful use lately.<br /> <br /> Their current quest is to find Thor's belt. During a raid, the Son of Odin went missing when the dust settled. While the Aesir can't find him, a prophecy has hinted at it being somewhere in the Big Apple. With the giants keeping pressure on Asgard, none of the gods can be away for too long. Thus, Odin has made arrangements for these scions to receive their Visitation so that they may find the Belt in their stead. <br /> <br /> And that's where our players are pretty much. The only clue they have is that there is a crime wave and a dose of supernatural activity going on in Hell's Kitchen. In addition to that, bodies have been going missing lately, noticed by Katya. Jamie checked with one of her contacts, and, while not too much info, she now has a job to deliver five stiffs for 10 grand each to one of the piers. Today, (after getting the party back together) they'll hopefully be headed into Hell's Kitchen to get to the bottom of this.<br /> <br /> As far as the overall setting, most of the other pantheons have been destroyed, along with their respective titans. There may be a god here and a legendary being there, but it's mostly left to the Norse now. This means Ragnorak will likely not be a localized event. <br /> <br /> I've only introduced one houserule so far. For major events that add to their legends, I give out legend experience points, which can only be used to raise legend. <br /> <br /> That's all of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6942,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","user":"simison","date":". 07-16-2015, 12:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T08:45:35-07:00","id":594795,"title":"","content":"Okay, we had our first new session last Thursday.<br /> <br /> <br /> It was a mess.<br /> <br /> Perhaps reading through John Scion's Resource's archived blogs wasn't as practical as coming up with more plot or making sure I had the combat rules memorized. The session started with individual segments. My goal for this session was to get everyone back on their bikes. That meant trying to get them into character, while re-uniting the party. To help them get into character, I thought giving each of them a little sidequest might help. <br /> <br /> Vjun, after fruitlessly wandering around Central Park asking for hobos for info, ran into Gridny, the forest maiden/nymph of Central Park. After noticing the rose in her hair was actually growing out of her scalp, Vjun divined (pun not intended?) her supernatural nature. After a terse beginning, things relaxed, and they came up with a deal. If Vjun dealt with vandals for her, she would provide any kind of aid. The conversation ended with Gridny warning Vjun that she had sensed titanspawn at the edge of her park, near Hell's Kitchen. <br /> <br /> Jamie got a call from a former-thug-now-mob-boss named Moran. He needed a letter delivered to a judge living in Hell's Kitchen and was asking for a favor of Jamie since he was the one who helped her move from simple thief to criminal consultant. She accepted. <br /> <br /> Katya had a less pleasant surprise. As she was finishing up a day's work in the morgue, Jessica, a murdered young woman, started haunting her, demanding that Katya avenge her. While Katya agreed, the specter has continued to follow her until the deed is done.<br /> <br /> By far the worst one, Lad was called into his superior's office, who had heard of his inquiries into the crime of Hell's Kitchen. The LT, eager for more help with the new crime wave, assigned Lad to the neighborhood. Not a bad premise, but I didn't actually give anything for Lad to do. I had intended for random encounters to happen, while he was in Hell's Kitchen, but nothing happened this session.<br /> <br /> So, as you can see, not only was I trying to give the characters things to do, but I was trying to get them to go together. <br /> <br /> It didn't work out that way. It half-worked. Vjun and Katya met up, ready to move into Hell's Kitchen. Jamie, however, had the actual link to the main story. First, she called Katya and tried to get the bodies that way without explaining what she was up to. Katya refused. Well, that was one easy way removed. The exchanged happened, while I was in the other room with Vjun's player. Otherwise, I would've had Janah straighten it out.<br /> <br /> Let me pause and explain Janah, since none of my players will probably come around these parts. From a strictly mechanics view, Janah is a two-dot creature, the second dot granting him E.Intelligence. To explain this, I've decided that Janah is actually a failed Son of Hel who's been rewarded (or condemned) to have his soul stuck in a rat, and be Hel's connection to her daughter. Janah is bitter about the experience, but that was compounded by Katya's attitude toward him. The two now have a very antagonistic relationship, though Janah won't abandon her, much as he wants to. Now, back to the story.<br /> <br /> Denied access, Jamie goes through her contacts. None of her Underworld contacts can supply her because most of the floating corpses have already been bought. So, she turns to the nearby university's storage of cadavers. Although the professor in charge is corrupt, she's not willing to see how much he actually wants. Instead, she calls Lad and tricks him into securing the bodies for her (getting her 6 bodies instead of the 5 the original deal asks for). The Son of Baldur arrives at the university, in-person and in uniform. The professor, fearful that the city's hero cop has shown up at his door, immediately caves when Lad asks for the bodies for 'police work'. <br /> <br /> That's fine with me, but not the next step. After procuring a van to transport the bodies, Jamie tries to go to the exchange site...alone. Lad is suspicious enough to insist on traveling with her. But no one attempts to bring the other half of the Band. So, when Lad calls the other two to say they're going to be later, Janah warns Katya that they need to be there as well. After some finagling, the Band reunites at the Pier where Jamie is supposed to drop off the bodies. The meeting site is within a small maze of shipping containers. Vjun and Katya had arrived first and had been waiting long enough to realize the area was being patrolled. Instead of bringing the Band with her, in case of danger, Jamie takes the bodies in alone.<br /> *sigh*<br /> <br /> To be fair, I wasn't dead set on a fight breaking out, but I was ready for it. What happens is Jamie goes in and makes the deal with no issue, even getting a hesitant invite to a new titan cult along with the $60k for the bodies.She considers it, but makes no decision since she can just come back with another batch of cadavers. <br /> <br /> (Now, if I had been quicker on my feet, the moment I knew combat wasn't going to break out, I should've had something happen with the other three. Definitely should have been something related to crime to give some kind of detail to Lad's side quest. Alas.)<br /> <br /> She returns, and the four agree to have supper at a nearby diner. But Jamie needs to stop at a bank alone...<br /> <br /> Out of curiosity, anybody else have this much trouble keeping the Band together? Or is this a secondary skill of Loki's kids?<br /> <br /> Lad insists, but the other two go ahead. The bank stop is simple. Not trusting the money, Jamie deposits the cash into a safety deposit box that only she and Lad knows about. It's at this point, I decide something needs to happen to Vjun and Katya. In hindsight, throwing in a frost giant might've been overkill since I didn't know how they would react to it. What was supposed to be another quick peek at the supernatural, turned into something else. After ordering their food, Vjun and Katya are waiting when a frost giant walks in to grab a quick order. He walks out before Jamie and Lad get there. Like I said, I was just trying to give them a taste and thought it'd end right there. <br /> <br /> Nope.<br /> <br /> Instead, they immediately try to devise a way to track the frost giant before he gets too far away, which lead to this small conversation between Janah and Katya.<br /> <br /> Katya: Janah! We need you to follow the frost giant!<br /> <br /> Janah: What!? No! I'll get stomped!<br /> <br /> Katya: Just be stealthy.<br /> <br /> Janah: No, not doing it.<br /> <br /> Katya: How about I give you something?<br /> <br /> Janah: Frost giant.<br /> <br /> Katya: How about I give you a snack?<br /> <br /> Janah: Frost giant!<br /> <br /> Katya: Two snacks?<br /> <br /> Janah: FROST GIANT!<br /> <br /> Katya: Three snacks?<br /> <br /> Janah: FROST! GIANT!<br /> <br /> <br /> She never did convince him. By the time they had left, Janah had bitten and peed on her. Fun times.<br /> <br /> So, they ran out the diner right as Jamie and Lad arrived. With a brief explanation, the Band began to tail the titanspawn. Thanks to Jamie, they never lost track of it. When it threw a hobo who had accidentally walked into it into a nearby wall with bones cracking, Lad declared enough was enough and attacked. <br /> <br /> The resulting two rounds of combat showed that no one remembered the rules of combat. Since we were out of time, we ended the session to right before the combat had started. My homework to the players (and myself) was to learn the rules of combat. <br /> <br /> Despite all of the chaos, people did have fun and are ready for more. The biggest lessons I've learned is that A) know the rules and B) a single page of material isn't enough for a three-hour session. I'm also considering tossing out the Legendary XP. My players are struggling with it, and I've read that it's better to just give it Legend dots at story-appropriate times. <br /> <br /> Comments or suggestions?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-22T13:49:29-07:00","id":599780,"title":"","content":"Now, while I was under-prepared for that session, I did have the end point of this first story sketched out. Thor's Belt is currently being worn by Owney Madden, a Legend 3 Aptranger, former head of the Hell\u2019s Kitchen\u2019s Gopher Gang. He is a creation of the svartalfar, who are trying to wreck NYC and kick-start Fimbulvetr. They're the ones collecting bodies and are turning them into a zombie horde in the basement of an environmental high school in Hell's Kitchen. Every night the Band fails to reach them translates into another twenty more zombies that they'll (and the NYPD) will have to deal with. If they don't find them before Yule, the horde will be unleashed. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T13:16:10-07:00","id":920525,"title":"","content":"That's hilarious, I'm re-resurrecting this game a year after my last collapse.<br /> <br /> Well, it is alive again and with two more additions.<br /> <br /> Joining the Band is a nameless Scion of Heimdall and Leithe, Scion of Freya. Last night was essentially getting everyone re-familiarized with their characters and helping the two new additions craft their characters.<br /> <br /> Leithe is fulfilling the role of Healer in the party and plays an Irish whistle that transforms into a Quarterstaff. She will also receive an Irish wolfhound, whom she's already nicknamed 'Talky' on her character sheet.<br /> <br /> The Scion of Heimdall already has a lot of interesting ideas going for him. He has all of the Perception and has a black glass eye. My wife suggested that during the Visitation, Heimdall rips out a healthy eye and replaced it with the new eye. Grisly, but that's not all. He intends to buy Shadow Mask and have the eye be the device that spews the darkness he wraps himself in.<br /> <br /> The only thing of note is now I see why most Scion games I've started in had STs start the party at Legend 3. Being limited to the first level of E.attributes and Boons allows characters to be jack-of-trades but limits their ability to distinguish themselves from their band-mates.<br /> <br /> Also, I am amused that I wrote the results of the last session here, but not in my ST notes on Word. Will have to fix that, but at least I know where everyone is at the start of the next session.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6942,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","user":"simison","date":". 06-24-2016, 06:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T20:18:17-07:00","id":920747,"title":"","content":"I've learned (I hope) a couple of things from my last failed attempt to ST. I think I understand why I quickly burn out on storytelling. While I loved doing the set-up and creating the world for my players and coming up with the sessions, I am still an introvert. Thus, the normal stress of leading a session does double the damage to me. I was also very insecure and was extra hard on myself during these sessions. I'm aiming to be more confident in myself because my players obviously were having fun if they are asking me to do it again. <br /> <br /> Another thing I've learned was that I was trying to hard to establish the characters and their personal stories as opposed developing them as a Band, which is why they kept splitting apart. <br /> <br /> The last thing I've learned or changed is furious wave of research of Norse mythology. Trying to determine who is Aesir or Vanir, learning about the Nine Worlds, and much more. There are some ideas I'd like to try, but it's too late, like combining Freya and Frigg into one goddess. Regardless, I feel like I have a much firmer understanding the world of Norse mythology, which gives me a better foundation to ST on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T22:12:55-07:00","id":920795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=920525#post920525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing of note is now I see why most Scion games I've started in had STs start the party at Legend 3. Being limited to the first level of E.attributes and Boons allows characters to be jack-of-trades but limits their ability to distinguish themselves from their band-mates.</div> </div> </div> </div>Starting at Legend 2 is really difficult in RAW to allow Scions to differentiate themselves from each other. Normally where you will see the biggest variation, and characters distinguishing themselves is through Birthrights, and their Pantheon Specific Purviews. Since I believe you are running an all Norse game, the Pantheon Specific Purviews are obviously all the same, so that takes out that method.<br /> <br /> What I generally see with Legend 2 characters I create, see others create, and in the one game I am running, is that Birthrights form the key forms of mechanical variation. However, unfortunately RAW has a sort of... weird Birthright system, so you probably don't have as much room for uniqueness in that area as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=920525#post920525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of curiosity, anybody else have this much trouble keeping the Band together? Or is this a secondary skill of Loki's kids?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Most of the games I have played in / run normally start with what you did in the first session as background, or just have some outside unification force, such as all being hired to work together, or a Deity just going, &quot;Congratulations, you're all doing what I tell you because I am vastly more important than you.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=920525#post920525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also considering tossing out the Legendary XP. My players are struggling with it, and I've read that it's better to just give it Legend dots at story-appropriate times.</div> </div> </div> </div>Giving out Dots of Legend in return for people being sufficiently Legendary (i.e. out Appearancing a Gorgon to prevent a city block from being turned to stone, beating down a Legend 4 Avatared down God at Legend 2, ect) is probably the best solution. Legendary XP is just extra book keeping. Try to keep everyone within 1 Dot of each other, and you probably never want anyone to hit a higher tier before the rest of the Band. For 4-5, and 8-9, do some sort of communal Legend Up. It just prevents a huge amount of hassle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=920525#post920525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've learned (I hope) a couple of things from my last failed attempt to ST. I think I understand why I quickly burn out on storytelling. While I loved doing the set-up and creating the world for my players and coming up with the sessions, I am still an introvert. Thus, the normal stress of leading a session does double the damage to me. I was also very insecure and was extra hard on myself during these sessions. I'm aiming to be more confident in myself because my players obviously were having fun if they are asking me to do it again.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am really introverted. Like, paralyzed by phone calls bad. Running games can be difficult sometimes, but you can get into the flow of it. What's probably the best next step for you here is to almost be less... focused? You have mentioned players doing unexpected things, or mention &quot;not being dead set on combat breaking out&quot; which is a difficult first hurdle for a lot of people. Especially in Scion more so than most RPGs.<br /> <br /> You just kinda gotta let the players do as they will. Don't plan things in too much detail, and never, ever expect something to happen. Scions are <i>incredibly</i> powerful, both through their own capacity, but also through the fact they have fully fledged Deities backing them up. Especially the Norse who have Loyalty, their Divine Parents <i>will always</i> be on their side. Heck, the entire Pantheon (- Hel) is probably always going to be backing the Band up unless they do something fundamentally abhorrent. Odin probably the lest, and Loki the most (Loki gets a bad rap modernly, but up until the Baldur-Murder, Loki is flat out the most loyal and helpful Pantheon member) likely to help if asked. These Scions are all family to the Aesir (except those related to the three Vanir in RAW, Njord, Freya, and Freyr, but even they have a family-like structure and social requirements for protection due to being political hostages) which means the Aesir are both socially, legally, and Virtue compelled to be helpful.<br /> <br /> So, don't be too worried about your Scions. They can probably face down most challenges you throw at them by hook or by crook if they think innovatively.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=920525#post920525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The last thing I've learned or changed is furious wave of research of Norse mythology. Trying to determine who is Aesir or Vanir, learning about the Nine Worlds, and much more. There are some ideas I'd like to try, but it's too late, like combining Freya and Frigg into one goddess. Regardless, I feel like I have a much firmer understanding the world of Norse mythology, which gives me a better foundation to ST on.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you're doing a purely Norse-centric game, reading up on them as much as you can is probably only going to be helpful. Just some hints though. Freya, Freyr, and their father Njord are the Vanir currently being held as political hostages by the Aesir as part of the peace pact between the two Pantheons. If you rule Frigg is Freya, she would thereby also be Vanir, but doing this creates a whole lotta chronology problems (Odin and his brothers met Frigg way, way, way before they ever meet the Vanir IIRC) but RAW Aesir are filled with chronology problems. Like, I believe Vidar isn't actually supposed to be born until after the death of Baldur during the events of Ragnarok. Also, the Nine Worlds are inconsistant, varying depending on which document you use. I'd suggest either 'canonizing' which these are, or allowing there actually be elleven (I think) Nine Worlds.<br /> <br /> Since you've offed all of the Pantheons that are not Norse, and their Titans, you also may be at a disadvantage for Titanic antagonists. A really quick and dirty list of entities you could make into Titans for the Norse are as follows.<ul><li>Jormungand - Animal or Water Realm.</li> <li>Fenrir - Animal Realm.</li> <li>Skoll and Hadi - Darkness Realm.</li> <li>Nourns - Fate Realm.</li> <li>Utgard-Loki - Illusion Realm.</li> <li>Sutr - Fire Realm.</li> <li>Sol - Light/Sun Realm.</li> <li>Mani - Celestial/Moon Realm.</li> <li>Ran - Water Realm.</li> <li>Aegur - Water Realm.</li> <li>Nidhogg - Death Realm.</li> <li>Odr - War Realm.</li> <li>Jord - Earth Realm.</li> </ul>Now, not all of these are antagonistic Titans (RAW says all Titans are antagonistic, but that's sort of complicated and hard to make work in actual mythology) with the Nourns, Sol, Mani, Ran, Aegur, Oor, and Jord all ranging from neutral to friendly to the Pantheon.<br /> <br /> If you've got any other questions, or if I missed any of yours, just let us know!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":".  Spelling issues, you know, the norm. 06-25-2016, 02:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T09:51:08-07:00","id":921001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=920795#post920795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I generally see with Legend 2 characters I create, see others create, and in the one game I am running, is that Birthrights form the key forms of mechanical variation. However, unfortunately RAW has a sort of... weird Birthright system, so you probably don't have as much room for uniqueness in that area as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed with the Birthright system being the main method. It's led to some interesting ideas taken form. Jamie's birthrights are Norse runes tattooed on her body that give her access to her purviews. I've already mentioned the glass eye of darkness. And, animals have proven to be really popular with this crowd. No one has considered a mentor or having allies at their beck and call.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=920795#post920795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Giving out Dots of Legend in return for people being sufficiently Legendary (i.e. out Appearancing a Gorgon to prevent a city block from being turned to stone, beating down a Legend 4 Avatared down God at Legend 2, ect) is probably the best solution. Legendary XP is just extra book keeping. Try to keep everyone within 1 Dot of each other, and you probably never want anyone to hit a higher tier before the rest of the Band. For 4-5, and 8-9, do some sort of communal Legend Up. It just prevents a huge amount of hassle.</div> </div> </div> </div>It didn't even occur to me to allow some scions to be on different legend levels. But I do have a concern. Jamie is our ninja, and she should be rewarded just as much legend for pulling off some epic stealth things, but legend is all about becoming more famous/infamous. If everything she's doing is in the shadows, what's my reason for rewarding her with more popularity?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=920795#post920795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You just kinda gotta let the players do as they will. Don't plan things in too much detail, and never, ever expect something to happen. Scions are <i>incredibly</i> powerful, both through their own capacity, but also through the fact they have fully fledged Deities backing them up. Especially the Norse who have Loyalty, their Divine Parents <i>will always</i> be on their side. Heck, the entire Pantheon (- Hel) is probably always going to be backing the Band up unless they do something fundamentally abhorrent. Odin probably the lest, and Loki the most (Loki gets a bad rap modernly, but up until the Baldur-Murder, Loki is flat out the most loyal and helpful Pantheon member) likely to help if asked. These Scions are all family to the Aesir (except those related to the three Vanir in RAW, Njord, Freya, and Freyr, but even they have a family-like structure and social requirements for protection due to being political hostages) which means the Aesir are both socially, legally, and Virtue compelled to be helpful.<br /> <br /> So, don't be too worried about your Scions. They can probably face down most challenges you throw at them by hook or by crook if they think innovatively.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I'm trying to do now is have all of the details of the environment but not what have a detailed idea for what's going on. I originally thought the Band was at the drop off point, and we were starting from there before I rediscovered this thread. My plan was to outline three broad paths the Band could take: social, stealth, and combat. I made sure I knew who the cultists were, their general skill set, and a solid picture of the pier. That way, I felt like I could react to most of the choices the Band took without over-planning.<br /> <br /> You do bring up an interesting point. I had forgotten about the Loyalty of the Asa, but I'm concerned. How often would they choose to help? I'm worried about having one too many Dues Ex Machinas.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=920795#post920795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're doing a purely Norse-centric game, reading up on them as much as you can is probably only going to be helpful. Just some hints though. Freya, Freyr, and their father Njord are the Vanir currently being held as political hostages by the Aesir as part of the peace pact between the two Pantheons. If you rule Frigg is Freya, she would thereby also be Vanir, but doing this creates a whole lotta chronology problems (Odin and his brothers met Frigg way, way, way before they ever meet the Vanir IIRC) but RAW Aesir are filled with chronology problems. Like, I believe Vidar isn't actually supposed to be born until after the death of Baldur during the events of Ragnarok. Also, the Nine Worlds are inconsistant, varying depending on which document you use. I'd suggest either 'canonizing' which these are, or allowing there actually be elleven (I think) Nine Worlds.<br /> <br /> Since you've offed all of the Pantheons that are not Norse, and their Titans, you also may be at a disadvantage for Titanic antagonists. A really quick and dirty list of entities you could make into Titans for the Norse are as follows.<br /> <br /> If you've got any other questions, or if I missed any of yours, just let us know!</div> </div> </div> </div>I knew about those three Vanir and chose not to combine Freya and Frigg for this game (though I may do it for a future game). So far, I think the biggest changes I've made to the pantheon is that I've officially labeled Sif &amp; Uller as Vanir, and that Odr, Freya's husband, is secretly Odin who had visited the Vanir in disguise long before the Aesir-Vanir war broke out. Oh, I've also killed off Vili and Ve via Fire and Frost giants, but the impact of that was never going to be much considering how little those two do. But I thought it added some context on why Odin obsesses so much over the pursuit of wisdom and knowledge.<br /> <br /> Are the titanrealms necessary? This is one of the few Scion concepts that has always struck me weird, and I've never made it far enough as a player for one to come up. My intent was to detail the Nine Worlds and go from there since the titanrealms are more about living concepts as opposed to just being alien lands filled with monsters and hostile deities/entities.<br /> <br /> Lastly, thank you for replying! I had just made peace with the idea that this was going to be nothing more than a ST log for myself. Certainly read, but just me speaking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T11:24:58-07:00","id":921050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=921001#post921001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed with the Birthright system being the main method. It's led to some interesting ideas taken form. Jamie's birthrights are Norse runes tattooed on her body that give her access to her purviews. I've already mentioned the glass eye of darkness. And, animals have proven to be really popular with this crowd. No one has considered a mentor or having allies at their beck and call.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's actually interesting that there are so many critters hanging around your Band. The Norse have <i>issues</i> with animals. If you notice, most of the Gods die to animals (Fenrir, Gram, Hadi, Skoll, Jormungand are the main killers) with only a few having animal servants. Thor, and Freya are the most obvious, but they very specifically have domesticated animals pulling their chariots. Gullinbursti is Freyr's boar, but it's less animal more construct I suppose. However, Odin has a <i>lot</i> of animals, including wild animals (Hunin, Munin, Geri, Freki, Sleipnir) and this actually is part of his limital role as a God between what is accepted, and what isn't. Odin really skirts that line with social acceptability. You could do something with your Band's critters, since if they're not wild, they're mostly a marker of the figure being limital like Odin is. (except without being Odin, they don't have all the political power to prevent people talking)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=921001#post921001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It didn't even occur to me to allow some scions to be on different legend levels. But I do have a concern. Jamie is our ninja, and she should be rewarded just as much legend for pulling off some epic stealth things, but legend is all about becoming more famous/infamous. If everything she's doing is in the shadows, what's my reason for rewarding her with more popularity?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, <i>that</i> thing. Okay, so, you need to invert that concept. RAW has this idea that your Legend reflects how well known you are, for good or for bad. This is <i>really bad</i> since it makes the Manipulation and other sneaky characters almost impossible to gain Legend with. What you can do instead is make having a higher Legend increase how well you are known (rather than the other way around) and have mortals start spontaneously learning of these modern myths.<br /> <br /> The <i>other</i> issue with Legend working as it does in RAW is that someone could 'give' someone else Legend. Say, for example, Baldur just drops down at Legend 12 in downtown New York and talks with one of their Scions infront of a ton of people. By RAW Legend logic, that Scion is going to raise in Legend a bunch due to the sheer social weight of Baldur with his 11 Dot Appearance and Charisma. If the world worked like this, then you have to start explaining <i>why</i> people don't do this, and it becomes a mess on top of the previous problem of the sneaky Scions not actually being able to gain Legend without being bad at what they're supposed to be good at.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=921001#post921001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You do bring up an interesting point. I had forgotten about the Loyalty of the Asa, but I'm concerned. How often would they choose to help? I'm worried about having one too many Dues Ex Machinas.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't do it all the time, obviously. The Gods won't get involved in everything. But, keep in mind, the Norse have two All Seeing people (Odin on his throne + ravens, and Heimdall who is just aware of everything all the time) so they will, without even trying, be aware of everything the Band is doing unless something powerful is trying to prevent this. (and in that case, they would then be aware someone is trying to hide things from them and it becomes a whole thing) So, Thor probably wouldn't arrive in 99.9% of situations, but if the Band was all on the verge of dying, you should consider the following.<br /> <br /> How much time and effort have their Divine Parents put into these Scions? This sort of depends on how common Scions are in your setting, but if Scions are rare, these kiddos are a Big Investment and the Divine may interject here and there. While, you can't do this all the time least all tension vanish from a story, the Gods, unless occupied by something else <i>really</i> important, will want to save their kids. Especially the Norse. Especially-especially-especially the Norse. Some good In-Myth examples of this happening can be seen all through the Iliad where Aphrodite just drags Paris (or was it Aeneas, one of the two) off the battlefield so they don't die. Or, in the Cattle Raid of Cooley, Lugh shows up and heals CuChulain a bit. (more like he knocks his son out to calm him down)<br /> <br /> But, doing this all the time removes all tension. But, what should be remembered is the Gods are not stagnant, they themselves are up to things. If Thor sees one of his kids about to be killed by a Giant, he may immediately drop everything to save them, but there must be consequences for Thor. Maybe Thor was protecting someone during this and he leaves them alone. While the Band is saved, a God dies in the Overworld as a consequence for the Band.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=921001#post921001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the titanrealms necessary? This is one of the few Scion concepts that has always struck me weird, and I've never made it far enough as a player for one to come up. My intent was to detail the Nine Worlds and go from there since the titanrealms are more about living concepts as opposed to just being alien lands filled with monsters and hostile deities/entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>I, personally, think Titanrealms are unnecessary. Also, they're mythologically problematic. For example, Atlas is just imprisoned at the edge of the world. No special place, just past Oceanus, where Helios, and Eos live as well. I just listed them there since a lot of people prefer them. You can just say Jomungard is resting at the bottom of the ocean of... Jotunheim? I can't remember where Thor fishes him up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=921001#post921001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lastly, thank you for replying! I had just made peace with the idea that this was going to be nothing more than a ST log for myself. Certainly read, but just me speaking.</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries man, I've never see this post before, sorry no one had responded sooner. Just holler if you need anything else.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T13:27:24-07:00","id":921122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=921050#post921050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's actually interesting that there are so many critters hanging around your Band. The Norse have <i>issues</i> with animals. If you notice, most of the Gods die to animals (Fenrir, Gram, Hadi, Skoll, Jormungand are the main killers) with only a few having animal servants. Thor, and Freya are the most obvious, but they very specifically have domesticated animals pulling their chariots. Gullinbursti is Freyr's boar, but it's less animal more construct I suppose. However, Odin has a <i>lot</i> of animals, including wild animals (Hunin, Munin, Geri, Freki, Sleipnir) and this actually is part of his limital role as a God between what is accepted, and what isn't. Odin really skirts that line with social acceptability. You could do something with your Band's critters, since if they're not wild, they're mostly a marker of the figure being limital like Odin is. (except without being Odin, they don't have all the political power to prevent people talking)</div> </div> </div> </div>If there's one thing I've learned in my research is just how much of a gray character Odin is. Which makes the animal connection more interesting. There's a wolf, a dog, the Gambian rat, and a ferret. I should definitely have some Norse deities ask about that. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=921050#post921050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> What you can do instead is make having a higher Legend increase how well you are known (rather than the other way around) and have mortals start spontaneously learning of these modern myths.</div> </div> </div> </div>The vague idea I had was that Odin and Heimdall would note these incidents and that somehow translate it into Legend increase. Perhaps Odin goes on trips specifically to spread the tales to increase Jaime's legend in ways that won't cause consequences to fall upon her. But your solution also sounds doable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=921050#post921050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much time and effort have their Divine Parents put into these Scions? This sort of depends on how common Scions are in your setting, but if Scions are rare, these kiddos are a Big Investment and the Divine may interject here and there. While, you can't do this all the time least all tension vanish from a story, the Gods, unless occupied by something else <i>really</i> important, will want to save their kids. Especially the Norse. Especially-especially-especially the Norse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good points. Off-hand, I wanted to avoid Riordan's take which was to have scions everywhere to the point where they could form battalions, but wanted to avoid having the Band be the only Heroes wandering around. I have plans to create a rival Band and then, eventually, a newcomers Band which could be apprenticed to the current Band. So, I'd say, perhaps a couple of dozen Scions globally at any point in time. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=921050#post921050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I, personally, think Titanrealms are unnecessary. Also, they're mythologically problematic. For example, Atlas is just imprisoned at the edge of the world. No special place, just past Oceanus, where Helios, and Eos live as well. I just listed them there since a lot of people prefer them. You can just say Jomungard is resting at the bottom of the ocean of... Jotunheim? I can't remember where Thor fishes him up.<br /> <br /> No worries man, I've never see this post before, sorry no one had responded sooner. Just holler if you need anything else.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that was in Midgard actually. Regardless, I think I'll just ditch the Titanrealms then, and focus on having the -Heims be the hostile and strange lands for the Scions to visit. That's something else I'm going to have to work out eventually: supernatural travel. Again, this is an area I've only perused in the core books, but I had a vague idea that an individual could use portals to step onto Yggdrasil, and they could travel thousands of miles in a fraction of the walk/climb it would take on the World Tree. Technically, one could eventually walk from Asgard to Jotunheim to Alfheim, but traveling across the tree is just much faster. The only exception is Midgard, which is physically cut off from the other worlds, so you would have to use the portals to leave the human realm to get to someplace more exotic. The idea is that is the 'wall' that protects Midgard from daily Jotunn raids, unlike Asgard which has a physical wall. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T14:58:47-07:00","id":921181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=921122#post921122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there's one thing I've learned in my research is just how much of a gray character Odin is. Which makes the animal connection more interesting. There's a wolf, a dog, the Gambian rat, and a ferret. I should definitely have some Norse deities ask about that.</div> </div> </div> </div>A wolf especially should raise a lot of concern. Three of the Big Antagonists of the Norse are Wolves. Four if you count Gram. If you houserule the Creature rules at Demigod (RAW Creatures sort of become more liabilities than actual helpful creatures around Legend 5. At God, they are normally flat out incapable of being direct help. The RAW Birthright system is sort of plagued with these issues) and have the Wolf continue to grow in power, it would likely raise a tremendous amount of concern. <br /> <br /> Norse Wolves also seem to be (I have not done any reading in this specific area, but, just at a glance) deeply rooted with ideas of Consumption. Fenrir will eat Odin, Hadi and Skoll will eat Mani and Sol, and Odin's two wolves are The Ravenous One, and The Greedy One. The PC's wolf could probably really easily develop a Fate like this, consuming entities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=921122#post921122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The vague idea I had was that Odin and Heimdall would note these incidents and that somehow translate it into Legend increase. Perhaps Odin goes on trips specifically to spread the tales to increase Jaime's legend in ways that won't cause consequences to fall upon her. But your solution also sounds doable.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, the only issue with that one is then Odin could just make up things and try to pump Scions Legends that way. He has Ultimate Manipulation, Mortals will believe anything he says. You could rule that Fate is the actual 'audience' instead of mortals or Deities. That's sort of how we run it. Fate observes, and those that tie themselves more deeply into the story, and become characters dancing on the strings of Wyrd (in the Norse case), their Legend increases.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=921122#post921122\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good points. Off-hand, I wanted to avoid Riordan's take which was to have scions everywhere to the point where they could form battalions, but wanted to avoid having the Band be the only Heroes wandering around. I have plans to create a rival Band and then, eventually, a newcomers Band which could be apprenticed to the current Band. So, I'd say, perhaps a couple of dozen Scions globally at any point in time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rival Bands can be fun. Might be a bit tricky in a Norse Only world though, since they will inevitably all have Loyalty (unless you have houserules for Virtues) to each other, and the PC Band as well. You could get some really good 'friendly competition' sort of stuff though. Outright antagonism could prove difficult, but, if someone does kill someone else, their Divine Parent has the right to invoke weregild, which can be a fun story. However, the killer'd get the nasty brand of 'kinslayer' which is a <i>really</i> big deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T20:04:20-07:00","id":921316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=921181#post921181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The PC's wolf could probably really easily develop a Fate like this, consuming entities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooo, that could be great character moment, learning that Fate wants to twist his companion into something malevolent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=921181#post921181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">See, the only issue with that one is then Odin could just make up things and try to pump Scions Legends that way. He has Ultimate Manipulation, Mortals will believe anything he says. You could rule that Fate is the actual 'audience' instead of mortals or Deities. That's sort of how we run it. Fate observes, and those that tie themselves more deeply into the story, and become characters dancing on the strings of Wyrd (in the Norse case), their Legend increases.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, fair points. Yeah, in that case, I'll simply go with it's Fate observing, recording, and eventually divulging. With the amount of prophecy and magic going around, it'd be pretty easy to explain how a couple of Jamie's more magically-sensitive followers could divine her past heroics despite the secrecy. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=921181#post921181\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Rival Bands can be fun. Might be a bit tricky in a Norse Only world though, since they will inevitably all have Loyalty (unless you have houserules for Virtues) to each other, and the PC Band as well. You could get some really good 'friendly competition' sort of stuff though. Outright antagonism could prove difficult, but, if someone does kill someone else, their Divine Parent has the right to invoke weregild, which can be a fun story. However, the killer'd get the nasty brand of 'kinslayer' which is a <i>really</i> big deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've really got to start adding the Virtue system to my calculations. Off-hand, I hadn't thought much of where the rivalry was going to fall on the spectrum between 'friendly' and 'malicious', but I knew envy and disgust was going to play a role between a few of the scions.<br /> <br /> Originally, I was going to have a Scion of Heimdall rival against Jamie, the Scion of Loki, but with the new player choosing Heimdall, I need to choose another deity instead. <br /> <br /> For Katya, Scion of Hel, I was debating one of the fertility deities and have settled on Sif. The primary antagonism is that Sif's Scion finds Katya's connection to the dead distressing and disgusting.<br /> <br /> For Lad, Scion of Baldur, I thought a daughter of Frigg would be fitting since Frigg requires all her scions to swear to protect Baldur. I thought about adding a personal touch that Frigg's scion is plain, while Lad is handsome, so there's some sexual tension sprinkled on top of the resentment.<br /> <br /> For Vjun, Scion of Vidar, I'm thinking either a Scion of Forseti or Tyr, either representing a more cleaner version of justice compared to Vidar's hunt for vengeance. Given Vjun is a loner who prefers the solitude of the forest over mankind (something Vidar is disappointed about), I wanted to make his rival the leader of the rival Band and a social butterfly. <br /> <br /> That leaves Jaime and the two new scions. My first impulse was to have a Scion of Thor to rival Jaime, someone who deplores Jaime's underhanded tactics. <br /> <br /> I don't know who would rival Heimdall's scion. One impulse was to bring in Sly from the core rulebooks. Leithe, the Scion of Freya, I hadn't had any thoughts about. ...nope, I'm honestly not sure who's left to face off against her. I suppose Hodr would be an interesting choice since Leithe is the team healer and Hoder is the deity of blind battle-rage.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T22:43:29-07:00","id":921359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=921316#post921316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've really got to start adding the Virtue system to my calculations. Off-hand, I hadn't thought much of where the rivalry was going to fall on the spectrum between 'friendly' and 'malicious', but I knew envy and disgust was going to play a role between a few of the scions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Virtues are really tricky a lot of the time. In our houserules, we actually allow Scions to swap one of their Virtues for any other Virtue. Our thought process is that a lot of Deities totally don't have all four of their Pantheon's Virtues. For example, Odin has Ambition (we don't use Dark Virtues as Titan corruption, as the Dark Virtue system, and Always-Evil Titans is sort of problematic), and Tezcatlipoca may have Malice but it's almost impossible to get a read on him.<br /> <br /> But, sticking with the four Virtue system, you should totally keep Virtues in mind for most Pantheon's actions. They're a handy way to sort of gently work out how they would act without spending all the time reading into legal systems of the cultures, social roles, and the like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=921316#post921316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Lad, Scion of Baldur, I thought a daughter of Frigg would be fitting since Frigg requires all her scions to swear to protect Baldur. I thought about adding a personal touch that Frigg's scion is plain, while Lad is handsome, so there's some sexual tension sprinkled on top of the resentment.</div> </div> </div> </div>That actually is an interesting little twist there at the end. The Aesir are <i>super</i> against incest, while on the other hand, the Vanir are not only cool with it, but it's a normal system of their divine tribe. The Aesir put a stop to that with their captives though, separate Njord from his sister-wife, and (probably, this is speculative and not mythologically cannon) preventing Freyr and Freya from getting married. You could do something interesting there, since if the Scion of Frigg is lusting after her nephew, Lad, there's this whole angle of social revulsion, that the Vanir may actually try to encourage (especially Njord and Freya) to spite the Aesir. If a daughter of Frigg and a son of Baldur were caught in such a relationship, there'd be a political clusterfuck where the Aesir either have to levy punishments, or allow it to carry on and give the Vanir members the capacity to return to their previous practices.<br /> <br /> Also, other random thing I remembered that makes the Freya = Frigg thing tricky. Freya and Freyr are children when she comes to Asgard after the war IIRC. But, at the same time, Norse chronology is a utter pain and inconsistent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=921316#post921316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Vjun, Scion of Vidar, I'm thinking either a Scion of Forseti or Tyr, either representing a more cleaner version of justice compared to Vidar's hunt for vengeance. Given Vjun is a loner who prefers the solitude of the forest over mankind (something Vidar is disappointed about), I wanted to make his rival the leader of the rival Band and a social butterfly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh! Another thing! Right, so, I was talking about how the Norse got <i>Issues</i> with wild animals? Forests are also problematic. Wild places outside the realm of human control. A conflict between Human (and Divine) against Nature is a big 'thing' with Norse mythology and culture IIRC.<br /> <br /> But, with Forseti or Tyr's Scions as antagonists. That could work, sure. The Norse did actually have a interesting bit of their legal system that is a branch between these two practices interestingly. The Weregild (Man-Price I think?) is a term for a payment in return for the killing, or otherwise harming of a family member. On this side, we can see the opposite of Vidar's system, Vengeance is controlled and moderated. But, if a Weregild is <i>not</i> paid, then you can just kill the other person, sometimes members of their family too I think. And, <i>that</i> bit is very much in the realm of Vidar. You could do something interesting based off that maybe.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=921316#post921316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That leaves Jaime and the two new scions. My first impulse was to have a Scion of Thor to rival Jaime, someone who deplores Jaime's underhanded tactics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now, Scions don't have to mirror their parents, not at all. In fact, some of the most interesting Scions I have seen reject (or are rejected by) their parents. But, I get the feeling you have been playing with this idea of Like Mother Like Daughter with this antag Band. If that's the case, don't use Thor as a fair fighter. Thor is not, at all. Thor's a lot like a roving murderer a lot of the time. He's going around killing Giants, but we know that not all Giants are evil (his own mother is a Giant, for example. Skadi is a Frost Giant and a member of the Pantheon. Loki's a Giant, and a staunch friend of Thor's) which makes this slightly problematic. On top of that, Thor <i>brutally</i> breaks the rules of hospitality during the whole 'Thor's in a dress pretending to be Freya to get his hammer back' myth. That sort of passes as a 'oh haha look at Thor', but actually man, breaking hospitality is a super big deal. <br /> <br /> If you want a fair fighter or the like, go with Forseti or Tyr again. Maybe check out the ritual legal combat the Norse used, that could be interesting inspiration. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=921316#post921316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know who would rival Heimdall's scion. One impulse was to bring in Sly from the core rulebooks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm. You could just use any old Scion actually, but have them be someone who has picked up Sun and have them be exceptionally panic-y about the Scion of Heimdall using Darkness. Hadi and Skoll are two big-ol' Darkness personifications, and there is no actual good Darkness entities in the Norse system. (Hod may have Darkness, but he isn't a Darkness God. It'd just be a proponent of him being a blind God. Sort of like someone having Fire for Hearth style stuff.) So, seeing someone using Darkness may set them off being suspicious. <i>Especially</i> since this Darkness Scion is, Gasp! Hanging out with someone who has a wolf. Bad portents indeed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=921316#post921316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Leithe, the Scion of Freya, I hadn't had any thoughts about. ...nope, I'm honestly not sure who's left to face off against her. I suppose Hodr would be an interesting choice since Leithe is the team healer and Hoder is the deity of blind battle-rage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Poor Hod. Baldur steals his blind brother's girlfriend and runs off with her, leaving Hod to sit alone, blind, not being able to contribute to his martial society. Always feel compelled to point that out, that Baldur's a bit of an ass despite what his Epic Charisma'll tell you.<br /> <br /> Instead of having someone opposed on thematic stuff, you could just have another healer who wants to out due the Scion of Freya. The resident Plague Deity is Hel though, and you could add another Scion of Hel and have them doing the whole sickness thing.<br /> <br /> I think both of your Magic people (and I don't think you have anyone with Prophecy) are women, but if you are looking for strife causing things, keep in mind that Magic and Prophecy are both womenly magics that is super-duper socially bad if a male practices. Just like with his wild animals, this is another way Odin is running around being a transient figure. Furthermore, I don't know if any of the PCs are gay, but the Norse have a whole <i>thing</i> about that, which can make interesting strife between Divine Parents and Scions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-26T10:24:17-07:00","id":921549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=921359#post921359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That actually is an interesting little twist there at the end. The Aesir are <i>super</i> against incest, while on the other hand, the Vanir are not only cool with it, but it's a normal system of their divine tribe. The Aesir put a stop to that with their captives though, separate Njord from his sister-wife, and (probably, this is speculative and not mythologically cannon) preventing Freyr and Freya from getting married. You could do something interesting there, since if the Scion of Frigg is lusting after her nephew, Lad, there's this whole angle of social revulsion, that the Vanir may actually try to encourage (especially Njord and Freya) to spite the Aesir. If a daughter of Frigg and a son of Baldur were caught in such a relationship, there'd be a political clusterfuck where the Aesir either have to levy punishments, or allow it to carry on and give the Vanir members the capacity to return to their previous practices.<br /> <br /> Also, other random thing I remembered that makes the Freya = Frigg thing tricky. Freya and Freyr are children when she comes to Asgard after the war IIRC. But, at the same time, Norse chronology is a utter pain and inconsistent.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not doing the Freya = Frigg thing in this game. Might do it in a different game. Do agree that the Norse mythology timeline is wacky.<br /> <br /> Now, I thought the ban against incest was only against the same members of what we call the nuclear family. Do the Norse not even allow for cousin marriage?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=921359#post921359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh! Another thing! Right, so, I was talking about how the Norse got <i>Issues</i> with wild animals? Forests are also problematic. Wild places outside the realm of human control. A conflict between Human (and Divine) against Nature is a big 'thing' with Norse mythology and culture IIRC.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good grief, my Band is turning out to be a bunch of oddballs from both mortal and Norse perspectives. This should be interesting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=921359#post921359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, with Forseti or Tyr's Scions as antagonists. That could work, sure. The Norse did actually have a interesting bit of their legal system that is a branch between these two practices interestingly. The Weregild (Man-Price I think?) is a term for a payment in return for the killing, or otherwise harming of a family member. On this side, we can see the opposite of Vidar's system, Vengeance is controlled and moderated. But, if a Weregild is <i>not</i> paid, then you can just kill the other person, sometimes members of their family too I think. And, <i>that</i> bit is very much in the realm of Vidar. You could do something interesting based off that maybe.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed! I'll keep that in mind. One idea you've given me is that the Norse gods are much more active in their scions' lives compared to the Greeks.Maybe I'll arrange for Norse culture lessons throughout the campaign to bring the Band up to speed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=921359#post921359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, Scions don't have to mirror their parents, not at all. In fact, some of the most interesting Scions I have seen reject (or are rejected by) their parents. But, I get the feeling you have been playing with this idea of Like Mother Like Daughter with this antag Band. If that's the case, don't use Thor as a fair fighter. Thor is not, at all. Thor's a lot like a roving murderer a lot of the time. He's going around killing Giants, but we know that not all Giants are evil (his own mother is a Giant, for example. Skadi is a Frost Giant and a member of the Pantheon. Loki's a Giant, and a staunch friend of Thor's) which makes this slightly problematic. On top of that, Thor <i>brutally</i> breaks the rules of hospitality during the whole 'Thor's in a dress pretending to be Freya to get his hammer back' myth. That sort of passes as a 'oh haha look at Thor', but actually man, breaking hospitality is a super big deal.<br /> <br /> If you want a fair fighter or the like, go with Forseti or Tyr again. Maybe check out the ritual legal combat the Norse used, that could be interesting inspiration.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true. We do know that if twins grow up apart, they end up like each other, but if they grow up together, they end up opposites. I think I'll play around with that concept here. Everyone starts out, mirroring their divine parent pre-Vistation. But, afterwards, now armed with that knowledge, they can choose to follow their parents' footsteps. I do plan on the PC Band having a large impact on the direction of the rival Band.<br /> <br /> Wasn't that giant guilty of theft and breaking &amp; entering in the first place? Still, I'll consider Thor or Tyr then. If a Scion of Thor, then maybe one that highlights his positive attributes. Perhaps the canon Scion of Thor from the rulebooks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=921359#post921359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm. You could just use any old Scion actually, but have them be someone who has picked up Sun and have them be exceptionally panic-y about the Scion of Heimdall using Darkness. Hadi and Skoll are two big-ol' Darkness personifications, and there is no actual good Darkness entities in the Norse system. (Hod may have Darkness, but he isn't a Darkness God. It'd just be a proponent of him being a blind God. Sort of like someone having Fire for Hearth style stuff.) So, seeing someone using Darkness may set them off being suspicious. <i>Especially</i> since this Darkness Scion is, Gasp! Hanging out with someone who has a wolf. Bad portents indeed.</div> </div> </div> </div>This has got me thinking, how do I explain all of the odd birthrights being given by the Norse deities who should know better? My first thought was to have the gifts be some kind of test. One example would be Baldur testing Lad's luck by giving him a wolf or by setting up a long-term lesson that the wolves can't be trusted. Another idea was that the Norns or Fate were forcing the Norse to give these socially-ill gifts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=921359#post921359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Poor Hod. Baldur steals his blind brother's girlfriend and runs off with her, leaving Hod to sit alone, blind, not being able to contribute to his martial society. Always feel compelled to point that out, that Baldur's a bit of an ass despite what his Epic Charisma'll tell you.<br /> <br /> Instead of having someone opposed on thematic stuff, you could just have another healer who wants to out due the Scion of Freya. The resident Plague Deity is Hel though, and you could add another Scion of Hel and have them doing the whole sickness thing.<br /> <br /> I think both of your Magic people (and I don't think you have anyone with Prophecy) are women, but if you are looking for strife causing things, keep in mind that Magic and Prophecy are both womenly magics that is super-duper socially bad if a male practices. Just like with his wild animals, this is another way Odin is running around being a transient figure. Furthermore, I don't know if any of the PCs are gay, but the Norse have a whole <i>thing</i> about that, which can make interesting strife between Divine Parents and Scions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wasn't that only in one version though?<br /> <br /> That's a good idea, have someone try to one-up their rival as oppose to being opposing in theme.<br /> <br /> I did learn during my research rampage that magic, seidr in particular, is for women only. And, I doubt homosexuality will come up in the game, but I'll keep that in mind, too.<br /> <br /> Another big running concept I'm going to have affecting the Band is Ragnorak. I'm allowing it to occur whether or not they're Heroes, Demigods, or outright Gods. What triggers it are failures on the part of the Band to keep the Devourers (catch-all term for the three kinds of giants, the monsters, and the Svart-Alfs) in check. Basically, if I count up three failures at any point, I'm going to trigger the Ragnorak sequence. Baldur could die, but the Fimbulwinter will happen regardless, and will last three years. I figure that's enough time to allow the Heroes become Demigods so that they're throwing around some kind of strength during the final sequence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6942,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","user":"simison","date":". 07-02-2016, 09:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T06:21:06-07:00","id":924865,"title":"","content":"We didn't have a session this week because my wife was in the hospital and, suffice to say, my focus was dead. Thankfully, she's doing better and will be back next week.<br /> <br /> The next session is still devoted to introducing the two new Scions: Leithe, (Scion of Freya) &amp; Elias (Scion of Heimdall).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T12:13:02-07:00","id":924978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=921549#post921549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, I thought the ban against incest was only against the same members of what we call the nuclear family. Do the Norse not even allow for cousin marriage?</div> </div> </div> </div>They wouldn't be cousins. She, being Frigg's daughter, is Baldur's brother. So, the Scion of Frigg is the Scion of Baldur's aunt. Now, cousin marriages tend not to be super big deals in the ancient world, but I can't find any mention of Nephew - Aunt. You would need to sort of extrapolate based off existing information I think. As we know the Aesir have issues with the Vanir system of marriage, and none of the Aesir are married to another member of the Aesir (if you notice, Odin's line always marries out, to Alfs, Vanir, or Giants. Never internally as far as I remember) I'd probably say it would cause a big ruckus inside the Pantheon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=921549#post921549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good grief, my Band is turning out to be a bunch of oddballs from both mortal and Norse perspectives. This should be interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sort of thing's actually one of my favorite themes to play with in Scion. Divergence and disagreements between the Scions and their ancestors. You could have a lot of fun with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=921549#post921549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed! I'll keep that in mind. One idea you've given me is that the Norse gods are much more active in their scions' lives compared to the Greeks.Maybe I'll arrange for Norse culture lessons throughout the campaign to bring the Band up to speed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Theoi are... paradoxically withdrawn, but ever-present which is a weird thing to say. For example, Theoi Scions probably have eyes kept on them by Helios, Apollo, Artemis, or others. While, at the same time, the Theoi are almost never going to interject. Mostly because Theoi Scions... tend to make the Divine annoyed with them, and die as a consequence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=921549#post921549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't that giant guilty of theft and breaking &amp; entering in the first place? Still, I'll consider Thor or Tyr then. If a Scion of Thor, then maybe one that highlights his positive attributes. Perhaps the canon Scion of Thor from the rulebooks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup! Thrym steals Mjolnir from Asgard (through an undisclosed method. A big task with Heimdall up there) but Norse hospitality is very important. Even though Thrym is a thief, he had invited Loki, and Thor (disguised as a handmaiden and Freya) giving them food and drink. They were bound under hospitality. Even though Thrym was a thief, hospitality overrides this. Thrym must treat his guests exceptionally well, and his guests must in turn do the same. Thor breaks hospitality by killing his host and his host's family (presumably they were his family as it was a wedding feast) which is an <i>exceptionally</i> bad thing. Hospitality is why Loki could stroll into Odin's hall after tricking Hod into killing Baldur, insult everyone, and leave unharmed. <br /> <br /> It's sort of hard to grasp modernly, but hospitality is pretty important in many ancient cultures since without it, diplomacy is almost impossible. If there was a chance you could be killed during a meeting, marriage, or other sort of peace-brokering deal, especially in a martial society, people would be very hesitent ever to do such things. Hospitality taboos gave a sort of social guarantee of safety to allow diplomacy and peace.<br /> <br /> Due to this, violating hospitality, even if your host or guest murdered your most beloved son/brother (in the case of Baldur), is exceptionally dangerous. If someone violates it, then <i>everyone</i> will doubt any meeting with that person again. It essentially blacklists you from ever having any diplomatic relationship with anyone outside your immediate family, and even then, your family may suffer on behalf of you violating it. So, Thor breaking hospitality is a <i>really</i> shitty thing. In a many-Pantheon game, for example, I would have the Tuatha, Theoi, and Bogovi (the closest Pantheons written geographically all happen to have big hospitality rules) all incredibly cautious of any sort of inviting Thor to a hospitality-bound situation. His sons, and daughter I'd actually extend this black mark onto.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=921549#post921549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This has got me thinking, how do I explain all of the odd birthrights being given by the Norse deities who should know better? My first thought was to have the gifts be some kind of test. One example would be Baldur testing Lad's luck by giving him a wolf or by setting up a long-term lesson that the wolves can't be trusted. Another idea was that the Norns or Fate were forcing the Norse to give these socially-ill gifts.</div> </div> </div> </div>It <i>is</i> sort of tricky. If it's been established that the Norse Gods gave these gifts personally, maybe make them tests. If they were given these through intermediaries, I'd have the animals slipped in by the Vanir. Either the three captives, or the rest living off in Vanaheim, trying to stir disruption in the Aesir. But, that's just me who prefers Pantheon-War and Pantheon Civil-Wars as stories rather than Titan Wars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=921549#post921549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wasn't that only in one version though?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of. I believe the Prose Edda never actually establishes how Baldur and Nanna met, while the Gesta Danorum humanizes the deities involved, but explains how they met. Both can exist at the same time without even needing any of the 'even contradictory things are true' stuff. Since it's pretty much the only source we have for Hod being an independent actor, I tend to prefer to use it rather than discount all the things he did in the story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=921549#post921549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another big running concept I'm going to have affecting the Band is Ragnorak. I'm allowing it to occur whether or not they're Heroes, Demigods, or outright Gods. What triggers it are failures on the part of the Band to keep the Devourers (catch-all term for the three kinds of giants, the monsters, and the Svart-Alfs) in check. Basically, if I count up three failures at any point, I'm going to trigger the Ragnorak sequence. Baldur could die, but the Fimbulwinter will happen regardless, and will last three years. I figure that's enough time to allow the Heroes become Demigods so that they're throwing around some kind of strength during the final sequence.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to do Ragnarok, my biggest piece of advise is for you to get a timeline of events. For example, work out what point Loki is fated to betray everyone (and, keep in mind, as a Prophecy it can be a bit weird. For example, Loki who tricks Hod may not be Loki-Loki. Up to that point, Loki has been the most loyal member of the Pantheon pretty much, way more than Odin in the least. Such a sudden swap into maliciousness is crazy. But... there <i>is</i> <i>another</i> Loki who isn't keen on the Aesir. It could be Utgard-Loki if you want to surprise your players.) and work out the details of different events beforehand. Maybe have the players instructed to help find Loki when he runs off and hides, or have them present for his binding.<br /> <br /> Hope your wife is doing alright!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T16:26:07-07:00","id":925090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=924978#post924978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They wouldn't be cousins. She, being Frigg's daughter, is Baldur's brother. So, the Scion of Frigg is the Scion of Baldur's aunt. Now, cousin marriages tend not to be super big deals in the ancient world, but I can't find any mention of Nephew - Aunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. Hm. Yeah, I think that would be uncomfortably close on the kin system to set off flags, but just far enough out to not warrant outright bans. At that point, if anything does come of it, there's going to be a lot of awkwardness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=924978#post924978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It <i>is</i> sort of tricky. If it's been established that the Norse Gods gave these gifts personally, maybe make them tests. If they were given these through intermediaries, I'd have the animals slipped in by the Vanir. Either the three captives, or the rest living off in Vanaheim, trying to stir disruption in the Aesir. But, that's just me who prefers Pantheon-War and Pantheon Civil-Wars as stories rather than Titan Wars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I did go with direct gifts in this game. So, testing it is. <br /> <br /> I'm not sure how much emphasis I'm going to place on the Aesir-Vanir divide. I've obviously put enough importance enough into it to mark down who's on what line of the divide, but how much of an issue it's going to be depends on the Band's actions. One vague plot hook is Delling or another Vanir encouraging the Band to distance themselves from the Aesir in an effort to save themselves (and maybe the suggestor) from Ragnorak. Exploring Vanaheim will definitely open up possibilities of establishing a new pantheon given that it's mostly overrun by the Devourers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=924978#post924978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to do Ragnarok, my biggest piece of advise is for you to get a timeline of events. For example, work out what point Loki is fated to betray everyone (and, keep in mind, as a Prophecy it can be a bit weird. For example, Loki who tricks Hod may not be Loki-Loki. Up to that point, Loki has been the most loyal member of the Pantheon pretty much, way more than Odin in the least. Such a sudden swap into maliciousness is crazy. But... there <i>is</i> <i>another</i> Loki who isn't keen on the Aesir. It could be Utgard-Loki if you want to surprise your players.) and work out the details of different events beforehand. Maybe have the players instructed to help find Loki when he runs off and hides, or have them present for his binding.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've already started to mentally map it. My biggest issue is how Snorri's version is so well-known how on earth could everyone be stupid enough to let themselves be guided into that prophecy? Granted, I suppose Fate could force them, but I'm aiming for something different. I'm going to have Snorri be correct on the major points: Loki and Hodr are responsible for Baldur's death, and it will be Loki leading the giants at the end of Fimbulvinter, but some of the details are different.<br /> <br /> Right now, my intent is that Frigg is on a continuous quest to find new elements and things and create new immunities for Baldur. Just like in the legends, she fails, but this time, the 'mistletoe' is in fact a new element created by a Dr. Mistletoe. The element is only jokingly named after him, but before it receives a proper name, it plays in the death of Baldur at the time of a spear wielded by Hodr. Unlike Snorri's version, Hodr is striking against Baldur in rage, but believed it would simply bounce off of him like everything else. What Hodr doesn't know is that Loki has created a layer of 'mistletoe' around the spear point, which allows Hodr to kill Baldur, surprising them both. Loki's motivation is his envy getting the better of him, and the hope that if Baldur dies this way instead of the Snorri version, it's enough difference to derail Fate and Ragnorak.<br /> <br /> Obviously, it doesn't. <br /> <br /> Then again, despite all of this, if the Band has managed to hold off Ragnorak for long enough to become Demigods or even Gods, they might successfully stop Baldur's death and really throwing Ragnorak and Fate for a loop.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=924978#post924978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hope your wife is doing alright!</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! We're hoping that she'll be out before next Tuesday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T20:09:11-07:00","id":925178,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The formatting for this is crazy weird, sorry about that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=925090#post925090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how much emphasis I'm going to place on the Aesir-Vanir divide. I've obviously put enough importance enough into it to mark down who's on what line of the divide, but how much of an issue it's going to be depends on the Band's actions. One vague plot hook is Delling or another Vanir encouraging the Band to distance themselves from the Aesir in an effort to save themselves (and maybe the suggestion) from Ragnarok. Exploring Vanaheim will definitely open up possibilities of establishing a new pantheon given that it's mostly overrun by the Devourers.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I don't remember the Devourers, it's been ages since I read RAW Ragnarok. The Vanir are supposed to survive Ragnarok however, and Vanaheim can be inferred to rise again as a powerful entity After The End. It is explicitly mentioned that Njord survives, and returns to Vanaheim to live with his Sister-Wife. You could do something interesting with the Band trying to tie themselves to the Vanir to survive, as only one Vanir is Fated to die. (Freyr)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=925090#post925090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've already started to mentally map it. My biggest issue is how Snorri's version is so well-known how on earth could everyone be stupid enough to let themselves be guided into that prophecy?</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So, I have a really weird way to handle this exact problem. I rule that the Norse do not know about Ragnarok. Odin does, and both Frigg and Freya might. (Frigg is supposed to know all of Odin\u2019s secrets, despite him not wanting her to, and Freya may be the Prophetess who tells Odin about part of it) The Norse knowing about Ragnarok sort of makes some things really fiddily however.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I have this effect currently built into part of my rough draft for a revised Norse PsP since Jotunblut\u2019s a bit... if you\u2019re not a physical character, you don\u2019t get a lot out of it. Also the \u2018empowering things\u2019 bit drops off as soon as you hit Demigod.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The reason I do this is because canonically, none of the Aesir (Except Odin, and the two other possibilities) actually know about Ragnarok. Now, could Odin tell them? Of course! Would Odin tell them? No. Odin\u2019s a dick, and is probably frantically scrambling to solve the problem before anyone else realises that he (throwing Loki\u2019s kids out) has brought about the end of the world. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">So, how is this done? I say that either Odin has done something (Ultimate Manipulation, or The Wyrd) to conceal the information from his Pantheon (and all other Legendary Beings from Norse Cosmology) to the extent that, if they are told about it, they will dismiss the knowledge, or forget it as soon as the Scene ends. Or I just rule that Fate\u2019s said so, so there.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Now, how to deal with the players knowing about Ragnarok, and thereby their Characters. I rule that Heroes totally manage to remember the details, but when they hit Demigod, it starts to slip away so quickly that by the time they are Legend 6, they can\u2019t remember it at all, and are affected by the aforementioned \u2018forgetting power\u2019.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">It just... really helps a lot of stuff. It also makes Odin come off as a way bigger ass, which he is in-universe. Also you can get really interesting interactions with Divine Parents.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=925090#post925090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right now, my intent is that Frigg is on a continuous quest to find new elements and things and create new immunities for Baldur. Just like in the legends, she fails, but this time, the 'mistletoe' is in fact a new element created by a Dr. Mistletoe. The element is only jokingly named after him, but before it receives a proper name, it plays in the death of Baldur at the time of a spear wielded by Hodr. Unlike Snorri's version, Hodr is striking against Baldur in rage, but believed it would simply bounce off of him like everything else. What Hodr doesn't know is that Loki has created a layer of 'mistletoe' around the spear point, which allows Hodr to kill Baldur, surprising them both. Loki's motivation is his envy getting the better of him, and the hope that if Baldur dies this way instead of the Snorri version, it's enough difference to derail Fate and Ragnorak.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">What we tend to go for is that it\u2019s all a big twisted Prophecy and Baldur dies to a missile with some sort of T.O.E acronym thing. It\u2019s fun because players don\u2019t necessarily notice it, all they know is Loki has kidnapped Hod and is doing something at a missile silo.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Why are you changing Hod\u2019s roll in the murder? Just curious, wondering if you\u2019ve got anything interesting up your sleeve there.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=925090#post925090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then again, despite all of this, if the Band has managed to hold off Ragnorak for long enough to become Demigods or even Gods, they might successfully stop Baldur's death and really throwing Ragnorak and Fate for a loop.</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One thing you may want to keep an eye on. If the Band wants to derail Ragnarok, and other Pantheons are all dead, they might be able to do it. There are some key points of the leadup to Ragnarok that can be utterly ruined with a Relic from another Pantheon. For example, getting ahold of Lugh\u2019s Spear that grants perpetual victory for the wielder, and give it to Freyr, he may survive the battle and kill Sutr. Or, go find Balor\u2019s Evil Eye and use it as a weapon. (I focus on Irish stuff if you can\u2019t tell)</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Spoiler for Pots and Pans: No Griff, Aynie, or SMP.</b></span> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"> For example, in my current game, Odin has been trying (and failing due to constantly trying to use complex chains of intermediaries) to get ahold of the fragments of The Cauldron of Rebirth from Welsh Mythology (but the fragments are in Ireland.) in order to turn his Cosmology into one with reincarnation. His plan is to bring every single human that dies back to life over and over until they die in battle so he can use them in his army. Sure, they\u2019ll be mute for most of their existence, but it might work. </div></div> </div> </div></span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T21:06:46-07:00","id":925191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=925178#post925178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The formatting for this is crazy weird, sorry about that.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><br /> <br /> No problem. Though, I'm curious how that happened. Also, I apologize if it affects my post in weird ways.<br /> <br /> </span></span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=925178#post925178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">I don't remember the Devourers, it's been ages since I read RAW Ragnarok. The Vanir are supposed to survive Ragnarok however, and Vanaheim can be inferred to rise again as a powerful entity After The End. It is explicitly mentioned that Njord survives, and returns to Vanaheim to live with his Sister-Wife. You could do something interesting with the Band trying to tie themselves to the Vanir to survive, as only one Vanir is Fated to die. (Freyr)</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>I apologize for the confusion. Devourers is what the guy over at 'Norse Mythology for Smart People' argues should be the real name for the giants. I find it as a handy way to refer to all three breeds of giants and monsters as one group. I find it more fitting than using 'titanspawn' since there's no Theoi around.<br /> <br /> Really? Didn't know Njord was fated to survive. I'll have to add that to my notes. Originally, one of the reasons that I wasn't thinking too much about it was because none of the Bandmates were Vanir kids. So, less reason for it to be introduced. But now we have a Scion of Freya, so now I have an avenue to explore this idea. Think I'll save it for a Demigod or late Hero campaign, right as the Band is finally getting comfortable in their new identities. Culture shock for the win!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=925178#post925178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">What we tend to go for is that it\u2019s all a big twisted Prophecy and Baldur dies to a missile with some sort of T.O.E acronym thing. It\u2019s fun because players don\u2019t necessarily notice it, all they know is Loki has kidnapped Hod and is doing something at a missile silo.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Why are you changing Hod\u2019s roll in the murder? Just curious, wondering if you\u2019ve got anything interesting up your sleeve there.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>A missile? Huh, didn't even consider anything that modern. Fun choice. <br /> <br /> I wanted to strike a balance between Snorri's passiveness and Saxo's action. (I think it was the Saxo Germanicus that had the other version of Baldur-Hodr incident.) And to maintain Loki's involvement. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=925178#post925178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">One thing you may want to keep an eye on. If the Band wants to derail Ragnarok, and other Pantheons are all dead, they might be able to do it. There are some key points of the leadup to Ragnarok that can be utterly ruined with a Relic from another Pantheon. For example, getting ahold of Lugh\u2019s Spear that grants perpetual victory for the wielder, and give it to Freyr, he may survive the battle and kill Sutr. Or, go find Balor\u2019s Evil Eye and use it as a weapon. (I focus on Irish stuff if you can\u2019t tell)</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>One of the players actually spotted this loophole. Well, at least the idea of treasures and relics of other pantheons to be out there for the finding. I regret this, and have already declared that everything was lost. There is no trace of the other pantheons or their enemies. Slightly unrealistic... yep.<br /> <br /> In hindsight, I wished I had just made it clear that the universe was Norse-only. <br /> <br /> Also, I find your Irish focus ironic. The Scion of Freya has an Irish theme developing. Irish wolfhound, red hair, an Irish whistle that turns into a quarterstaff, and a Celtic torc. Given the fact that she's a daughter of Freya, I planned on some raised eyebrows at this. And a few quiet whispers about Freya's past 'friendliness'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T22:42:48-07:00","id":925226,"title":"","content":"Yeah IIRC Njord goes back to the vanir when ragnarok commences. What they all do after that? I have no idea. Maybe its like lord of the rings and they all go off to whereever the elves go and give the middle finger to the realm of man.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T23:24:32-07:00","id":925238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=925191#post925191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No problem. Though, I'm curious how that happened. Also, I apologize if it affects my post in weird ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was trying to fix a buzzing sound coming over my mic before sitting down to some Stelaris with a friend while I started on the post. Had to turn my machine off to work out what was making the racket, so I took what I had written so far and threw it into a Google Doc, and moved it back over when I finished it. The forums... don't like it when you do that. The other times I've had to do similar things, I'll just transcribe what I wrote, but it was a bit much to do that this time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=925191#post925191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I apologize for the confusion. Devourers is what the guy over at 'Norse Mythology for Smart People' argues should be the real name for the giants. I find it as a handy way to refer to all three breeds of giants and monsters as one group.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, that's interesting. I've never heard of that term before. What's his argument for calling them that and not just Jotuns?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=925191#post925191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I find it more fitting than using 'titanspawn' since there's no Theoi around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Scion 1E had a bad habit of pretty much only using Greek termenology, and then not using it properly. For example, Gaia isn't a Titan, she is a Primordial. The Titans are not all antagonistic, several side with Zeus. All Scions are technically Demigods, and the entire God Template 'can go invisible' thing is ripped directly from Greek Mythology. I normally axe the term 'Titanspawn' entirely, and for other things, such as 'Titan', different Pantheons give different names on a case by case basis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=925191#post925191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Really? Didn't know Njord was fated to survive. I'll have to add that to my notes. Originally, one of the reasons that I wasn't thinking too much about it was because none of the Bandmates were Vanir kids. So, less reason for it to be introduced. But now we have a Scion of Freya, so now I have an avenue to explore this idea. Think I'll save it for a Demigod or late Hero campaign, right as the Band is finally getting comfortable in their new identities. Culture shock for the win!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, he's Fated to survive, and return home to Vanaheim to live with Nerthus (we sort of guess that's her name, we have no Norse records giving her name, just reference to Njord's Sister-Wife. I think one of the Romans mentioned Nerthus and there's some connection somewhere.) in the new world created after the fires subside. The Vanir are still living in Vanaheim though, and still kicking probably around Legend 10 - 11. I can't remember which Aesir they had captive past Murmur, but I believe they killed both of them.<br /> <br /> But, it's a good Demigod level thing. Especially since I don't think Vanaheim is ever actually given a location in the Nine Worlds. You could do something interesting with it, but, it's pretty much an Overworld in its own right. (I'd scrap the whole 'anything that's not a God can't go into an Overworld' thing. It doesn't make sense with many mythologies. The big danger of Overworlds is being around the Legend 12 Social Deities.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=925191#post925191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A missile? Huh, didn't even consider anything that modern. Fun choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's even shaped like a dart. We normally run our games with the Pantheons being crazy isolationist (with some exceptions. The Deva, for example, are still very involved but do things with a gentle touch. The Kami likely want to be involved, but the Shen probably prevent it. But, again, that's one of my Pantheon-War things.) so Frigg never thought to make Baldur immune to many new things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=925191#post925191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the players actually spotted this loophole. Well, at least the idea of treasures and relics of other pantheons to be out there for the finding. I regret this, and have already declared that everything was lost. There is no trace of the other pantheons or their enemies. Slightly unrealistic... yep.<br /> <br /> In hindsight, I wished I had just made it clear that the universe was Norse-only.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might want to ask your players if you can fiddle with that. I think all you've mentioned so far from exterior cosmologies was a Nymph / Dryad, right? That could be ret-conned into an Alf or something similar. <br /> <br /> Ragnarok is almost impossible to run in a Pan-Pantheon game, mostly because other Pantheons have ends of the world, and giving the Norse dominance in that area's weird. Also, a lot of the problems can be solved with external methods. If I ever ran a game using Ragnarok in a Pan-Pantheon setting, I'd have Midgard essentially 'separate' from the rest of Earth. All mortals in 'Norse' areas (which would require a lot of handwaving in regards to the Slavic-Norse, Celtic-Norse, and a bunch of other border mixtures) would just now be in a carbon copy of the world, except mythified. Murkwood (The Dark Forest, think it's in Ragnarok), and an impossibly large and stormy sea (I call this The Whale Road, essentially a Norse-only aquatic Dark Forest) blocking off the areas that used to be the rest of the world.<br /> <br /> This Midgard would be the world that is doomed. Back on earth, these parts of the world are just empty now. I'd probably only allow uses of The Way to move in between Midgard and Earth or something. May even do some funky things with Pantheon Specific Purviews of foreign figures who enter the Nine Worlds during this. If Tezcat brought an end to The Fifth Sun (it's not fated, but, I mean, he's the usual suspect.) or whenever the Deva reach The End, Ra blinks, or Svarog wakes up, I'd have a similar thing happen, just plucking their regions out.<br /> <br /> After the fires fade, and Balder and Hod rebuild Asgard (or after the Teotl fashion another Sun, Brahma creates it all again, Svarog shatters his leg again, ect) that part of the world would just 'slot' back in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=925191#post925191\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, I find your Irish focus ironic. The Scion of Freya has an Irish theme developing. Irish wolfhound, red hair, an Irish whistle that turns into a quarterstaff, and a Celtic torc. Given the fact that she's a daughter of Freya, I planned on some raised eyebrows at this. And a few quiet whispers about Freya's past 'friendliness'.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Aesir can get away with a lot of weird Birthrights, luckily. They went far afield, more so than even the Irish that one time they went and pestered the entire Mediterranean and stole their interesting things. It's not a leap at all for her to have those things. Dublin was a Norse stronghold for the longest time, building off a tiny backwater village I think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lyrics of War</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah IIRC Njord goes back to the vanir when ragnarok commences. What they all do after that? I have no idea. Maybe its like lord of the rings and they all go off to whereever the elves go and give the middle finger to the realm of man.</div> </div> </div> </div>This brings up something sort of interesting about the whole 'Njord goes home' scene. The authors went to all the trouble to explain what is going to happen after, who will return from the dead, how Asgard will be rebuilt, and the like. But, not a peep is given to Njord and the Vanir save that they return home, an interesting lack of detail. In reality, it's probably that whoever was recording the tale didn't think that section was important, or possibly in the original oral traditions, versions that detailed that were not popular enough to survive. But, it could totally be fluffed like Ragnarok breaks the Fated connections the Vanir have to the Aesir, and allow them to have their own story once again, rather than be resigned to being side-entities in the Aesir's tale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T10:53:47-07:00","id":925407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=925238#post925238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Huh, that's interesting. I've never heard of that term before. What's his argument for calling them that and not just Jotuns?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's his translation of Jotuns. I'll let him speak his argument in his own words...<br /> <br /> &quot;<span style=\"color:#2B2B2B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">Speakers of Old Norse called them </span></span></span><i>j\u00f6tnar</i><span style=\"color:#2B2B2B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> (singular </span></span></span><i>j\u00f6tunn</i><span style=\"color:#2B2B2B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">, pronounced roughly \u201cYO-tun\u201d) or </span></span></span><i>\u00feursar</i><span style=\"color:#2B2B2B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> (singular </span></span></span><i>\u00feurs</i><span style=\"color:#2B2B2B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">, pronounced \u201cTHURS\u201d like the first element in \u201cThursday\u201d but with a soft \u201cs\u201d at the end). </span></span></span><i>J\u00f6tunn</i><span style=\"color:#2B2B2B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> comes from the Proto-Germanic </span></span></span><i>*etunaz</i><span style=\"color:#2B2B2B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> and means \u201cdevourer.\u201d The Old English </span></span></span><i>e\u00f3ten</i><span style=\"color:#2B2B2B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> is a cognate (it means the same thing and comes from the same Proto-Germanic word).</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#2B2B2B\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">[1]</span></span></span><i>\u00deurs</i><span style=\"color:#2B2B2B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> is derived from the Proto-Germanic </span></span></span><i>*\u00feurisaz</i><span style=\"color:#2B2B2B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> and means something like \u201cpowerful and injurious one\u201d with a secondary connotation of \u201cthorn-like.\u201d The Old English</span></span></span><i>\u00f0yrs</i><span style=\"color:#2B2B2B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> and Old High German </span></span></span><i>duris</i><span style=\"color:#2B2B2B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\"> are cognates.</span></span></span><span style=\"color:#2B2B2B\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">[2]</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#2B2B2B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">How, then, did these \u201cdevourers\u201d come to be called \u201cgiants?\u201d When the Norman (French) William the Conquerer seized control of England in 1066 CE, the English language became filled with French words. Among these loanwords was the Old French <i>geant</i>, the ancestor of the modern English word \u201cgiant,\u201d which replaced the Old English <i>e\u00f3ten</i>. <i>Geant</i> referred to the Giants of Greek mythology, who were a group of spiritual beings who, like the <i>j\u00f6tnar</i> of Germanic mythology, were the enemies of the gods. The Greek ancestor of <i>geant</i>, in turn, was once used to translate a Hebrew word that denoted beings of enormous size in the Bible, and over time this connotation of \u201cgiant\u201d became the word\u2019s dominant meaning.<span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">[3]<br /> Source: </span></span>http://norse-mythology.org/gods-and-creatures/giants/</span></span></span><br /> <br /> He doesn't actually include Norse monsters in his usage, that's something I added in my own style. Figured it be easier than saying Jotun and monsters, like Fenris and Jorgumand.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=925238#post925238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup, he's Fated to survive, and return home to Vanaheim to live with Nerthus (we sort of guess that's her name, we have no Norse records giving her name, just reference to Njord's Sister-Wife. I think one of the Romans mentioned Nerthus and there's some connection somewhere.) in the new world created after the fires subside. The Vanir are still living in Vanaheim though, and still kicking probably around Legend 10 - 11. I can't remember which Aesir they had captive past Murmur, but I believe they killed both of them.<br /> <br /> But, it's a good Demigod level thing. Especially since I don't think Vanaheim is ever actually given a location in the Nine Worlds. You could do something interesting with it, but, it's pretty much an Overworld in its own right. (I'd scrap the whole 'anything that's not a God can't go into an Overworld' thing. It doesn't make sense with many mythologies. The big danger of Overworlds is being around the Legend 12 Social Deities.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, I'll have to follow that up.<br /> <br /> The only description I've found of Vanaheim is in the name itself. Midgard and Asgard are distinguished from the -heim lands because they are the bastions of civilization. What makes a place civilized? -gard says that it's a wall. So, according to this logic, Vanaheim is probably a lot like Asgard, but it isn't a walled settlement.<br /> <br /> In my game, I use this interpretation to build Vanaheim. Here, Vanaheim is in ruins. Not long after the Aesir-Vanir peace treaty, the Devourers, seeking to weaken this alliance by attacking the weaker target, assaulted Vanaheim. The Vanir city was sacked and most of the survivors have either retreated to Asgard (Sif &amp; Uller are two examples), died in the sacking, or disappeared. The lands around the city were wrecked by fire and ice, a preview of what will happen in Ragnorak. The Devourers,thinking their work done, have since left the place abandoned and desolate. Or so everyone thought. A couple of gods are still hiding in Vanaheim. I know I want Nerthus, Hoenir, and Gullveig to be three of them. I'm playing around with the idea that the Vanir deity of squirrels is there and is connected to Ratatoskr somehow. And maybe throwing in a true Norse goddess of virginity. But these other two are just potential ideas at this point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=925238#post925238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might want to ask your players if you can fiddle with that. I think all you've mentioned so far from exterior cosmologies was a Nymph / Dryad, right? That could be ret-conned into an Alf or something similar.</div> </div> </div> </div>I used 'nymph' for an easy reference, but she's a forest maiden, a skogsra, according to Scion. Although, a proper Alf would be also fitting, I need to keep that in mind next time. There are no other mythical creatures, except for the Norse.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T16:59:04-07:00","id":925564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=925407#post925407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's his translation of Jotuns. I'll let him speak his argument in his own words...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting argument of his. I don't believe his implication that the Gigantes were not supposed to be large in stature is correct, with the siege of Olympus having the invading Gigantes hurling mountains as missiles. While not Giants, the Cyclopses were definitely seen as larger than life, which can be seen through the depictions of Odysseus and Polyphemus on pottery. It is an interesting name to give them however.<br /> <br /> Actually, also, the logic of the argument doesn't make much sense. If 'Giants' gained their stature through the Norman Invasion, then the non-English speaking world, such as the Germanic principalities, and the Nordic countries, would never have gained that association. As all of our primary sources for Norse Mythology are detached from these linguistic lines he has drawn, mentions of the Jotun being larger than humans would all be valid.<br /> <br /> For example, in Beowulf, The Giant's Sword also takes a hatchet to that theory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beowulf</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then he saw mid the war-gems a weapon of victory,<br /> An ancient giant-sword, of edges a-doughty,<br /> Glory of warriors: of weapons \u2019twas choicest,<br /> <u>Only \u2019twas larger than any man else was<br /> Able to bear to the battle-encounter</u>,<br /> The good and splendid work of the giants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting idea though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=925407#post925407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He doesn't actually include Norse monsters in his usage, that's something I added in my own style. Figured it be easier than saying Jotun and monsters, like Fenris and Jorgumand.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think, by bloodline, Fenrir and Jomungand (as well as Hel) are full blooded Jotun. Both their parents are Jotun. Two of them being animals is a bit odd though. I know what you mean though, just a Norse term for Titanspawn.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=925407#post925407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only description I've found of Vanaheim is in the name itself. Midgard and Asgard are distinguished from the -heim lands because they are the bastions of civilization. What makes a place civilized? -gard says that it's a wall. So, according to this logic, Vanaheim is probably a lot like Asgard, but it isn't a walled settlement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I can follow that logic, sort of. The Jotun, and Dwarves are both shown to have some large scale infrastructure (various forges, Utgard-Loki's fortress) however, so, I'd not call their realms 'uncivilized' really. I'd probably not have Vanaheim walled due to the Vanir being non-warlike from what we can gather, where the Aesir are exceptionally martially inclined. Heck, Asgard wasn't walled for ages, even during the Aesir-Vanir war.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=925407#post925407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my game, I use this interpretation to build Vanaheim. Here, Vanaheim is in ruins. Not long after the Aesir-Vanir peace treaty, the Devourers, seeking to weaken this alliance by attacking the weaker target, assaulted Vanaheim. The Vanir city was sacked and most of the survivors have either retreated to Asgard (Sif &amp; Uller are two examples), died in the sacking, or disappeared. The lands around the city were wrecked by fire and ice, a preview of what will happen in Ragnorak. The Devourers,thinking their work done, have since left the place abandoned and desolate. Or so everyone thought. A couple of gods are still hiding in Vanaheim. I know I want Nerthus, Hoenir, and Gullveig to be three of them. I'm playing around with the idea that the Vanir deity of squirrels is there and is connected to Ratatoskr somehow. And maybe throwing in a true Norse goddess of virginity. But these other two are just potential ideas at this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, random notes. Feel totally free to ignore all of these entirely, they're really not that important, little details. Just stuff I thought I'd let you know in case it prompts any interesting ideas on your end.<br /> <br /> I'd probably not say the Aesir and Vanir are allied to each other, at all. In fact, I'd bet they <i>hate</i> each other pretty substantially. The Vanir murdered the hostages they were holding from the Aesir, which is a cataclysmically big deal. The Aesir actually come out looking good for not immediately putting Freyr, Freya, and Njord to death in response. There may have been a peace-treaty to start with, but <i>something</i> happened that caused the Vanir to snap, and murder their hostages despite knowing that the logical response from the Aesir would to kill their own captives. So, whatever caused this (we never learn IIRC) is a huge deal. The two Divine Tribes probably hold zero love for each other. So, even if Vanaheim fell, they probably would not ever go to Asgard. (As the Aesir would probably kill them for killing the Aesir hostages)<br /> <br /> Second, if a bunch of Vanir Gods and Goddesses died, then there's some conclusions your players will draw. First off, whatever killed them off are beings capable of killing Legend 9 - 12 beings who managed to fight the exceptionally warlike Aesir to an absolute standstill. Second, any of those Vanir who were Legend 12 had their Avatars explode in this area, meaning Vanaheim is probably insanely crazy. <br /> <br /> Third, that proposed Virginity Goddess. I don't know enough about the Norse to talk about if the Norse had a concept of virginity or not. I'd suggest you look into that before you create her, since virginity is a pretty big social construct. Now, I wouldn't be surprised if they had a thing about it, since almost all of the PIE cultures (except Ireland which looks like it totally purged the concept from existence there much to everyone's great confusion) but you might just want to check it out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=925407#post925407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I used 'nymph' for an easy reference, but she's a forest maiden, a skogsra, according to Scion. Although, a proper Alf would be also fitting, I need to keep that in mind next time. There are no other mythical creatures, except for the Norse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, makes total sense. And yeah, cross-cultural stuff can ruin Ragnarok pretty badly. One of the biggest derailing points is just going to one of the Omniscientient entities and asking where Freyr's sword is. If Freyr wins the conflict by having his sword (which, the lack of is explicitly spelled out to be why he fails to defeat Surtr) then the world isn't destroyed in fire. And, on top of that, then you have Freyr running around the battlefield able to help other figures as a wildcard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T18:22:05-07:00","id":925608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=925564#post925564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, random notes. Feel totally free to ignore all of these entirely, they're really not that important, little details. Just stuff I thought I'd let you know in case it prompts any interesting ideas on your end.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, this has been a really helpful discussion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=925564#post925564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd probably not say the Aesir and Vanir are allied to each other, at all. In fact, I'd bet they <i>hate</i> each other pretty substantially. The Vanir murdered the hostages they were holding from the Aesir, which is a cataclysmically big deal. The Aesir actually come out looking good for not immediately putting Freyr, Freya, and Njord to death in response. There may have been a peace-treaty to start with, but <i>something</i> happened that caused the Vanir to snap, and murder their hostages despite knowing that the logical response from the Aesir would to kill their own captives. So, whatever caused this (we never learn IIRC) is a huge deal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't it described as the Vanir getting pissed off at Hoenir's idiocy? Granted, their reaction is extreme, but there is a feeling of getting the short end of the stick in the hostage swap, and they take it out on Mimir since Hoenir is Odin's brother, supposedly. I think it's interesting how Odin never demands weregild for the murder too. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=925564#post925564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Second, any of those Vanir who were Legend 12 had their Avatars explode in this area, meaning Vanaheim is probably insanely crazy.</div> </div> </div> </div>This sounds like a Scion mechanics system that I don't know about. Would you mind expounding?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=925564#post925564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third, that proposed Virginity Goddess. I don't know enough about the Norse to talk about if the Norse had a concept of virginity or not. I'd suggest you look into that before you create her, since virginity is a pretty big social construct. Now, I wouldn't be surprised if they had a thing about it, since almost all of the PIE cultures (except Ireland which looks like it totally purged the concept from existence there much to everyone's great confusion) but you might just want to check it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>There supposedly already is a Virginity Goddess, Gefjun. But, in her one story, it ends with her having sex with a king and having a bunch of kids, which makes the title stupid. Right now, I've rolled her into Freya and simply being a different name she used when she visited the Midgard.<br /> <br /> I could leave it like that, or I could say that the sex with the king incident was simply a myth concocted by a boastful mortal, and it never happened. Or, Gefjun could be a Virginity goddess who gave away her virginity and has paid the price for breaking her legend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T22:00:52-07:00","id":925707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=925608#post925608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks, this has been a really helpful discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad to help. I really enjoy stuff like this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=925608#post925608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't it described as the Vanir getting pissed off at Hoenir's idiocy? Granted, their reaction is extreme, but there is a feeling of getting the short end of the stick in the hostage swap, and they take it out on Mimir since Hoenir is Odin's brother, supposedly. I think it's interesting how Odin never demands weregild for the murder too.</div> </div> </div> </div>It totally is. Hoenir is apparently super indecisive, and relied on Mimir for all of his decision making. The Vanir thought there was something fishy going on, and executed Mimir. This is a super weird scene, but, once again, Hospitality comes back up. Political hostages are protected under the bounds of hospitality, which may be why the Aesir don't kill their hostages (even though they likely had a right to after Mimir was killed) but I'm unsure.<br /> <br /> The fact that the Vanir sent Mimir's head back to the Aesir means they were trying to send a message. If they were being respectful, they'd send the entire body back. Instead, they only sent a severed head which was 100% dead until Odin pulled some of his rune-magic out and reanimated it. So, in the least, the Vanir were trying to insult, or threaten the Aesir. On top of that, it was a gross violation of hospitality. So, lots of social black marks, and violations of taboos.<br /> <br /> Why did Odin not demand a weregild? This enters one of the tricky bits of Scion. When we're not given explicit information about a myth, we sort of have to make logical leaps. The story of Odin demanding the blood-price for Mimir may not have been important enough to tell (i.e. people didn't find it interesting. Only the interesting stories survive in Bardic cultures unfortunately. The 'extra bits' tend to get shaved off) or perhaps it was never detailed. Knowing what we know of Odin, and Norse culture, it's out of character for him <i>not</i> to have gone after the Vanir for a blood price. So, I'd probably use that as a story hook in some way. Maybe he got something out of the Vanir in exchange.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=925608#post925608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds like a Scion mechanics system that I don't know about. Would you mind expounding?</div> </div> </div> </div>No worries. It's filed away somewhere in God in the Avatar section.<br /> <br /> So, if a Deity has any Avatar States (Rank 12 Purviews.) when they die, they sort of have a 'death throes' in the form of these Avatars running rampant. (This is another one of those things that doesn't make sense mythologically. But, it really helps the game function at God level. Killing Gods and Goddesses is very dangerous, which helps explain why the status quo has continued for so long.)<br /> <br /> For example, if Manannan mac Lir dies (not using the RAW associateds. Updated away from those to more accurate ones.) The Flood, The Trickster, The Reaper, and The Way go off in a random order. Basing this off his myths, and saying this died during a three-way re-invasion of Ireland between the Tuatha, Fomori, and The Sons of Mil (mortals in Ireland are the leading source of theocide. Don't mess with those mortals, they've got something wonky with them.) I would say the following happens.<br /> <br /> <b>The Flood</b>: Manannan's horses (which are both waves and horses at the same time. It's a weird literal metafore) tear into the scene, stampeding (read: flooding) the entire scene in a Deluge similar to Noah's Great Flood. All sides now have to deal with a potential sinking of Ireland.<br /> <br /> <b>The Trickster</b>: Riding on the backs of Manannan's horses (floating on the surging waves) comes The Isle of Man's phantom navy formed of mists. Ships of every era, from currachs, to world war two dreadnaughts, the Scene has suddenly been almost entirely blinded, with an armada arriving to defend, and return the body of Manannan to one of the Otherworldly Islands.<br /> <br /> <b>The Way</b>: A third of every force (three thirds. It'll almost always be three, seven, or nine with the Irish) suddenly finds themselves whisked away in a currach and left on a random Otherworldly island. Every four minutes that pass is equal to a day outside. Have fun getting back in time for the battle.<br /> <br /> <b>The Reaper</b>: In the colossal flood, more die than there are stars in the sky, and waves in the sea, dragged down into the depths of Donn's transitory underworld before being sent along to the afterlife.<br /> <br /> Now, the only way to resist any of these, is to use a Purview Avatar or an Ultimate Ability. So, almost everyone can't actually resist these. This will happen when any Legend 12 Deity dies (which is why killing Gods is a dangerous prospect, for the Titans, and upstart Scions alike! It really does help balance the game at God with Mutually Assured Destruction.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=925608#post925608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There supposedly already is a Virginity Goddess, Gefjun. But, in her one story, it ends with her having sex with a king and having a bunch of kids, which makes the title stupid. Right now, I've rolled her into Freya and simply being a different name she used when she visited the Midgard.<br /> <br /> I could leave it like that, or I could say that the sex with the king incident was simply a myth concocted by a boastful mortal, and it never happened. Or, Gefjun could be a Virginity goddess who gave away her virginity and has paid the price for breaking her legend.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh! That's the Proto Indo-European thing I was talking about. So, right, okay. In most (Ireland not only doesn't have it, but subverts it totally) of the Indo European Cultures, there is some sort of story relating to a Virgin, and a King. Sometimes a King becomes King due to the virginity of one of his daughters, sometimes a King becomes King by sleeping with a virgin. It's a really odd system. Best example off the top of my head is in Wales with the King who can only ever rest his feet on the back of a virgin for a complicated reason IIRC. So, right. Keep her. While she isn't a Virgin, she still is very important to a really old story of kingship predating the Pantheon itself.<br /> <br /> (Ireland inverts this by having every King / Chief enter into a marriage with the same entity. There are many names (Danu is just one of them) but they are The Land. So, right off the bat, they throw out any notions of virginity in the kingship story. Sovereignty (an easy way to refer to these Goddesses, they may or may not all be the same person, or different Goddesses wearing the mantle) tests would-be Kings by appearing as a monsterous, sometimes canabalistic woman demanding some sort of sexual action. Sometimes a kiss, but more often actual sex. He (or she, rare, but there were women Ri) who accepts this offer (almost everyone refuses) is given the authorty if Sovereignty and right to rule. Interestingly, I've found an interesting document from the early Christian period that suggests that Sovereignty may have been able to withdraw their support. Very Mandate of Heaven-y. Under Christianity, the stories would continue, but Sovereignty turned into Jesus disguised as a leper, and it was always simply a kiss.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 07-04-2016, 01:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T06:20:10-07:00","id":925854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=925707#post925707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The fact that the Vanir sent Mimir's head back to the Aesir means they were trying to send a message.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that the Scion version? Because I thought in the original myth, Odin just comes across Mimir's body and then takes the head. Which, admittedly, I'm sure there's some kind of social more being violated by that action (not to mention the coincidental timing), but that seems to be keeping in with Odin's MO of being a wanderer and dedicated to his pursuit of knowledge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=925707#post925707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, the only way to resist any of these, is to use a Purview Avatar or an Ultimate Ability. So, almost everyone can't actually resist these. This will happen when any Legend 12 Deity dies (which is why killing Gods is a dangerous prospect, for the Titans, and upstart Scions alike! It really does help balance the game at God with Mutually Assured Destruction.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yikes! *glances at all of the dead pantheons*<br /> <br /> Is there any way to contain the collateral damage? If the 'death' happens in an Overworld, does all the damage stay there or can it spill into the human realm?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=925707#post925707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh! That's the Proto Indo-European thing I was talking about. So, right, okay. In most (Ireland not only doesn't have it, but subverts it totally) of the Indo European Cultures, there is some sort of story relating to a Virgin, and a King. Sometimes a King becomes King due to the virginity of one of his daughters, sometimes a King becomes King by sleeping with a virgin. It's a really odd system.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, in that case, I'll render Gefjun back into her own character again and have her be one of the Vanir survivors.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T06:41:39-07:00","id":925865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=925854#post925854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is that the Scion version? Because I thought in the original myth, Odin just comes across Mimir's body and then takes the head. Which, admittedly, I'm sure there's some kind of social more being violated by that action (not to mention the coincidental timing), but that seems to be keeping in with Odin's MO of being a wanderer and dedicated to his pursuit of knowledge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, I can't remember actually. I hope I've not just messed up. I'll go through and check the Saga as soon as I can to check what's going on there. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=925854#post925854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yikes! *glances at all of the dead pantheons*<br /> <br /> Is there any way to contain the collateral damage? If the 'death' happens in an Overworld, does all the damage stay there or can it spill into the human realm?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, it won't spill over into the human realm. Dying in an Overworld is actually a pretty good way to contain it, but, it's messy anyways. More expensive things to break in an Overworld too from an IC perspective. The only reason I mentioned Ireland directly there is almost all conflict in Irish mythology takes place on the surface of Ireland. The Way, and The Wyrd won't be able to be contained like this, but, the rest are probably free game.<br /> <br /> Past that, combating the collateral damage of any Avatars can only be done through other Avatars, or Ultimate Attributes. So, for example, with the death of Manannan up there, this is what could be done to stem the tide. Balor of the Evil Eye could use his Ultimate Strength (epithet: Of the Strong Blows) to grab The Flood, and hold onto it. The Morrigan (though it'd actually be one of her component entities, probably Babd) could use The Reaper to counteract Manannan's The Reaper, just stating that none will perish. The Dagda could pull down the Sun to banish The Trickster with Ultimate Strength, stuff like that.<br /> <br /> Now, this <i>is</i> a very Scion-y rule in that it doesn't make sense (when, like, most of the important Tuatha died, they just died. Nothing fancy. Same with Pan, Osiris, ect) but it is exceptionally helpful for balancing the field at God. Feel free to toss it if you'd like.<br /> <br /> This also will only happen if you have Legend 12 Deities dying since you must be Legend 12 to buy an Avatar. I don't think RAW makes any Vanir except those in Asgard Legend 12, so, you could rule that the Vanir were simply mostly Legend 11 or something. It <i>is</i> a bit weird if this is the case, since the Vanir managed to hold their own against the Aesir. If Sif, Uller, and Njord (Freya and Freyr were only children when they came to Asgard, so I'm discounting them for military participation) were the only Legend 12 Deities, then they may have a hope. But, I would expect based off the way the Norse organized their society, Delling (or whoever is the Vanir Chieftian, I can't remember if we know or not. I think the Ragnarok book is fuddling my mind) probably is/was Legend 12.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T14:04:17-07:00","id":926068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=925865#post925865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, this <i>is</i> a very Scion-y rule in that it doesn't make sense (when, like, most of the important Tuatha died, they just died. Nothing fancy. Same with Pan, Osiris, ect) but it is exceptionally helpful for balancing the field at God. Feel free to toss it if you'd like.<br /> <br /> This also will only happen if you have Legend 12 Deities dying since you must be Legend 12 to buy an Avatar. I don't think RAW makes any Vanir except those in Asgard Legend 12, so, you could rule that the Vanir were simply mostly Legend 11 or something. It <i>is</i> a bit weird if this is the case, since the Vanir managed to hold their own against the Aesir. If Sif, Uller, and Njord (Freya and Freyr were only children when they came to Asgard, so I'm discounting them for military participation) were the only Legend 12 Deities, then they may have a hope. But, I would expect based off the way the Norse organized their society, Delling (or whoever is the Vanir Chieftian, I can't remember if we know or not. I think the Ragnarok book is fuddling my mind) probably is/was Legend 12.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, I'll think on this one. While we're on the subject of game mechanics, I love the concept behind Fate Binding, but I've heard that it's a mess or pointless. So, I was going to use John's version, but in the other thread it's mentioned that it's a different kind of mess. Which version should I go with? Should I just jettison it?<br /> <br /> Not sure if we're having a session this week because of work schedule (Curse you, Wal-Mart!), but I need to start bringing things together in case we do play. This next session will take place in-game time on Dec.15, 2009. The main goal of the session is to introduce the new scions: Elias and Leithe. I intend to have Freya and Heimdall to make the Visitation themselves and give their birthrights. <br /> <br /> Of the two, Elias has the much more interesting scene already set up. Instead of the single black, glass eye, he'll now have two. His player has Elias starting out as a blind man who will receive the gift of sight from his father Heimdall. Unless his eyes are physically gone, I fully intend for Elias to lose his crippled eyes by Heimdall's hands, who rips them out before inserting the new magical eyes. This Visitation's emphasis will be on duty. Heimdall is the eternal sentinel of the Bifrost, and he makes it clear that Elias will also be a watcher against the Devourers and evil. Regardless of Elias' wishes.<br /> <br /> Freya's Visitation, I'm not so sure about. Leithe is a musician whose nature is Caregiver. The bigger question is what kind of interpretation do I go with concerning Freya. I don't like Riordan's version, who I see as too simple and vain, though pleasant. Likewise, I find the Scion descriptions of her lacking and kinda confusing. Since when does Freya have authority over the valkyries? Anyway, for the Norse deities, I'm aiming for a mix of the old and the new. Scion likes to give everyone a modern makeover that I don't feel is properly fitting. A being that has existed for centuries is going to have a natural inclination to maintaining what has come before, I would imagine. Sort of like the Kindred Elders of Requiem/Masquerade. In this case, I don't want to make Freya a party girl or a simple seducer. Her command of magic adds a serious and potentially dangerous side to her that prevents her from the superficiality of Aphrodite. Maybe providing an upbeat or energetic young woman of a goddess with a dash of flirtiness and seriousness to balance each other out.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T15:29:08-07:00","id":926108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=926068#post926068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, I'll think on this one. While we're on the subject of game mechanics, I love the concept behind Fate Binding, but I've heard that it's a mess or pointless. So, I was going to use John's version, but in the other thread it's mentioned that it's a different kind of mess. Which version should I go with? Should I just jettison it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh man, okay. Fatebinding is a huge complicated thing, but you're actually <i>really</i> lucky that you're doing an Only-Norse-Exist-ish game, it lets you sidestep a huge number of problems. Technically, in a perfect world, every Pantheon would have a unique Fate system (or not have one at all in some cases) since Fate is crazy inconsistent. For example, the Deva have Fate, but due to being Deities, they have become 'beyond' Fate and are unfettered by it (or so has been explained to me. The Deva are really not a strong point for me) The Anunna flat out have a tablet that gives them control of fate in its entirety. The Irish forgot to explain theirs, but there seems to be prophecies though they're a bit different. The Aztecs have a system based on your birthday, pretty straight forward stuff. The Norse and Greeks however have flat out 'Impossible force above even the Gods that binds them' Fate.<br /> <br /> Since you're doing All Norse, this problem is solved. Fate is Wyrd, it's the 'fuck you, you do what I say' Fate, incredibly hardline with no compromises.<br /> <br /> Now, on to the systems themselves. JSR (John's Scion Resources) had an amazing Fatebinding system that found a nice common ground (it didn't work brilliantly with some of the weirder ones, but, it was a good catch-all one) between 'This controls everything' and 'You can fight fate'. It's a masterpiece of a system. However, it is absolutely insanely complex. I think John once mentioned he would spend several hours after each game working out how things had fluxuated. Since John and his players totally understood this system since they had been playing with it for years, and John designed it, it worked for them.<br /> <br /> However, it's incredibly complex nature may really frighten new players. I have wanted to try to use it before, after playing for, like... seven years now I think? But, it's arcane complexities that allow it to be so amazingly interesting and complex have left it as a system I've not been able to teach myself. If you really want to use it, go for it, but it is crazy complicated, adjusting exp costs, forcefully changing player's experience expenditures, and the like. (that bit also rubs a <i>lot</i> of players the wrong way. They can wake up one day and lose an entire Purview) I wouldn't suggest it for a first time Scion storyteller, or a first time Scion group.<br /> <br /> Now, I'd not throw out Fate all together. Fate is <i>very</i> important in Norse cosmology. The other systems mentioned in that thread work just fine (I will up front say I am one of the three people who work on Scion 2.0, so I am bias in that direction) but don't actually work perfectly for the Norse since their Fate system is just mean. If you want to be nice to your players, I'd let them develop and fight Fates with one of those two systems mentioned. If you want to be source accurate, disallow players violating any Fate that's rated 2 or 3+, and prevent anyone from ever losing or altering a Fate.<br /> <br /> The only issue, however, is that by changing Fate systems, Prophecy and Magic become incredibly... non-functional IIRC. I know JSR put up Magic and Prophecy pretty shortly before they shut their doors for the new project, so it's pretty entwined IIRC. Since you have players with Magic, this becomes tricky. I wish I could say, 'here is Magic and Prophecy for Scion 2.0!', but they are currently only completed outlines. And even then, Prophecy's outline may get an ax taken to it by myself one of these days. I'm unsure about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=926068#post926068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of the two, Elias has the much more interesting scene already set up. Instead of the single black, glass eye, he'll now have two. His player has Elias starting out as a blind man who will receive the gift of sight from his father Heimdall. Unless his eyes are physically gone, I fully intend for Elias to lose his crippled eyes by Heimdall's hands, who rips them out before inserting the new magical eyes. This Visitation's emphasis will be on duty. Heimdall is the eternal sentinel of the Bifrost, and he makes it clear that Elias will also be a watcher against the Devourers and evil. Regardless of Elias' wishes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a grumpy Deity, though, Heimdal is... pissy I guess you could call it. Sounds like a good Visitation though. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=926068#post926068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Freya's Visitation, I'm not so sure about. Leithe is a musician whose nature is Caregiver. The bigger question is what kind of interpretation do I go with concerning Freya. I don't like Riordan's version, who I see as too simple and vain, though pleasant. Likewise, I find the Scion descriptions of her lacking and kinda confusing. Since when does Freya have authority over the valkyries? Anyway, for the Norse deities, I'm aiming for a mix of the old and the new. Scion likes to give everyone a modern makeover that I don't feel is properly fitting. A being that has existed for centuries is going to have a natural inclination to maintaining what has come before, I would imagine. Sort of like the Kindred Elders of Requiem/Masquerade. In this case, I don't want to make Freya a party girl or a simple seducer. Her command of magic adds a serious and potentially dangerous side to her that prevents her from the superficiality of Aphrodite. Maybe providing an upbeat or energetic young woman of a goddess with a dash of flirtiness and seriousness to balance each other out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Valkyries thing was extrapolated off the Valkyries never having an explanation, and Freya's whole 'takes half of the dead warriors' thing. I've got no clue if the Valkyrie bit is accurate or not though, they in the least technically serve her about as much as Odin give or take a tiny bit.<br /> <br /> Freya's description's sort of all over the place, since she herself is a bit all over the place. She's got one of the two not-shit Underworlds, she's a captive, she uses sex as a tool (big no-no culturally for a woman) to get what she wants, she may have influence over Odin, was probably supposed to be married to Freyr, but is wandering the world searching for her lost husband Odr. If you want to lean more on the ancient route rather than modernize her, I'd do something like carry the PC off for a bit while Freya searches the Nine Worlds (so, give 'shots' of Jotunheim, Helheim (just don't cross the bridge), maybe pass by the mouth of Fenrir's cave. Fancy stuff like that.) for Odr in her eternal search, and have her give the PC their stuff and explain what's going on in the process.<br /> <br /> If you want to characterise Freya, there are a <i>ton</i> of ways to do it. Big main points: She always gets what she wants, mostly through sex. Her necklace is a crazy powerful appearance boosting Relic, don't have her wear it (and have her way Legended-down) during the Visitation unless you want a <i>crazy</i> uncomfortable Scion*, she is pretty demanding, and is incredibly sexual despite longing for her lost husband. She may be dangerous, but never to one of her kiddos.<br /> <br /> * So, a few years ago I needed a way to explain just how powerful Epic Appearance is, so I converted the system to the somewhat tasteless #/10 system for rating people's appearance. If a mortal with max Appearance and Presence is a 10, then each dice = 1 point. Every dice = 1/2 Success (more like .45, but I'm rounding up. The 10 = 2 makes the math weird), so every Auto = 2 points.<br /> <br /> So, a maxed out Appearance and Presence Legend 4 (pre-Demigod, Not-Greek, and Unbuffed) Scion is a 14/10. A Legend 12 Deity (not Theoi, Unbuffed) with those same rules is a 112/10 (10 Appearance, 10 Presence, 46 Automatic Successes) which Freya then compounds with her crazy powerful Necklace which boosts up her Appearance a huge amount on top of this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T19:41:31-07:00","id":926217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=926108#post926108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, on to the systems themselves. JSR (John's Scion Resources) had an amazing Fatebinding system that found a nice common ground (it didn't work brilliantly with some of the weirder ones, but, it was a good catch-all one) between 'This controls everything' and 'You can fight fate'. It's a masterpiece of a system. However, it is absolutely insanely complex. I think John once mentioned he would spend several hours after each game working out how things had fluxuated. Since John and his players totally understood this system since they had been playing with it for years, and John designed it, it worked for them.<br /> <br /> However, it's incredibly complex nature may really frighten new players. I have wanted to try to use it before, after playing for, like... seven years now I think? But, it's arcane complexities that allow it to be so amazingly interesting and complex have left it as a system I've not been able to teach myself. If you really want to use it, go for it, but it is crazy complicated, adjusting exp costs, forcefully changing player's experience expenditures, and the like. (that bit also rubs a <i>lot</i> of players the wrong way. They can wake up one day and lose an entire Purview) I wouldn't suggest it for a first time Scion storyteller, or a first time Scion group.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, I still would love to give it a try. I think the two big questions left for me to make a proper decision is (A) how much paperwork will it force on my players? If I'm the one that has to do the work, I think I can make it work. And (B) is it possible to scale the impact of the system. The disappearing Purview obviously sounds terrifying, and I'm curious if I could scale it back to something less potentially painful. I'm definitely going to read over it a couple of times in the next couple of days.<br /> <br /> Regardless of the Fate Binding system, I want a separate system to determine what Fate declares happens to the Band on Ragnorak. The idea I have is that, unknown to everyone, there is no Fate for a Scion. It is completely blank, until they try to consult prophecy. At which point, Fate now has a chance to declare what will happen to them. I want every prophecy to come with a risk for a Ragnorak prediction. How it works is that after the prophecy is issued, I roll a D10. If I roll a 1, that is an instant Doom result. That PC will die on Ragnorak. The details are left blank, but will be filled in every time that PC consults prophecy. How good or bad will be determined by subsequent die rolls. A roll of 10 is a Survival result. If Fate is left alone and the PC makes it to Ragnorak, they will survive and make it to the new pantheon post-Ragnorak.<br /> <br /> Now, the more often a PC checks prophecy, the more likely a Doom result. Say, the second time they consult prophecy, now it's a roll of 1 or 2. And it only gets worse from there.<br /> <br /> Although the PCs may be very wary of checking prophecy, their parents and the other Asa will push them in the hopes of a good Fate or breaking a prior Fate. It's one of the great weaknesses of the Norse deities, and thus the Band will have to face that pressure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=926108#post926108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like a grumpy Deity, though, Heimdal is... pissy I guess you could call it. Sounds like a good Visitation though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. I feel like, out of all the Norse, Heimdall's core personality/legend can be summed up by the word 'duty'. He is constantly watching for danger to protect his clan and guards the infamous Ragnorak horn. Since my Visitations are brief, my goal is to show the deity's biggest personality trait. Then I'll add more substance as the game goes on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=926108#post926108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Freya's description's sort of all over the place, since she herself is a bit all over the place. She's got one of the two not-shit Underworlds, she's a captive, she uses sex as a tool (big no-no culturally for a woman) to get what she wants, she may have influence over Odin, was probably supposed to be married to Freyr, but is wandering the world searching for her lost husband Odr. If you want to lean more on the ancient route rather than modernize her, I'd do something like carry the PC off for a bit while Freya searches the Nine Worlds (so, give 'shots' of Jotunheim, Helheim (just don't cross the bridge), maybe pass by the mouth of Fenrir's cave. Fancy stuff like that.) for Odr in her eternal search, and have her give the PC their stuff and explain what's going on in the process.<br /> <br /> If you want to characterise Freya, there are a <i>ton</i> of ways to do it. Big main points: She always gets what she wants, mostly through sex. Her necklace is a crazy powerful appearance boosting Relic, don't have her wear it (and have her way Legended-down) during the Visitation unless you want a <i>crazy</i> uncomfortable Scion*, she is pretty demanding, and is incredibly sexual despite longing for her lost husband. She may be dangerous, but never to one of her kiddos.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's an interesting idea, the whole jumping between worlds. I won't use it for the Visitation, but I'll definitely save that for later.<br /> <br /> Perhaps I will add a slight aggression to Freya during her Visitation whenever she's addressing anyone who isn't Leithe. Maybe a willingness to violate personal spaces, maybe some light touching. Still, I think her general demeanor is friendly and energetic to kind of show that as a goddess of fertility and power that she's almost-bursting with it.<br /> <br /> For the physical location of the Visitation, I'm tempted to use Central Park where Gridni, the forest maiden, is. To me, Central Park kind of establishes several of the themes of the story. Nature is good, so long as it's controlled by civilization. It represents a connection to the ancient surrounded by the modern, which is how the PCs must feel this early on with deities inserting themselves into their lives. And, it touches on the roles of Heimdall (control) and Freya (life).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-04T23:13:26-07:00","id":926290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=926217#post926217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, I still would love to give it a try. I think the two big questions left for me to make a proper decision is (A) how much paperwork will it force on my players? If I'm the one that has to do the work, I think I can make it work. And (B) is it possible to scale the impact of the system. The disappearing Purview obviously sounds terrifying, and I'm curious if I could scale it back to something less potentially painful. I'm definitely going to read over it a couple of times in the next couple of days.</div> </div> </div> </div>For A, I am not sure. I think all of the paperwork is Storyteller-side, but any character revisions preformed by Fate will require players to adapt to those changes. It should probably start with a very minimal amount of work, since Hero Fate stuff is pretty gentle, but as you go up in Legend it will grow to rather large heights. For B, I'm sure you could, but it may unbalance the entire system. It in the very least would mess with both Magic and Prophecy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=926217#post926217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless of the Fate Binding system, I want a separate system to determine what Fate declares happens to the Band on Ragnorak. The idea I have is that, unknown to everyone, there is no Fate for a Scion. It is completely blank, until they try to consult prophecy. At which point, Fate now has a chance to declare what will happen to them. I want every prophecy to come with a risk for a Ragnorak prediction. How it works is that after the prophecy is issued, I roll a D10. If I roll a 1, that is an instant Doom result. That PC will die on Ragnorak. The details are left blank, but will be filled in every time that PC consults prophecy. How good or bad will be determined by subsequent die rolls. A roll of 10 is a Survival result. If Fate is left alone and the PC makes it to Ragnorak, they will survive and make it to the new pantheon post-Ragnorak.<br /> <br /> Now, the more often a PC checks prophecy, the more likely a Doom result. Say, the second time they consult prophecy, now it's a roll of 1 or 2. And it only gets worse from there.<br /> <br /> Although the PCs may be very wary of checking prophecy, their parents and the other Asa will push them in the hopes of a good Fate or breaking a prior Fate. It's one of the great weaknesses of the Norse deities, and thus the Band will have to face that pressure.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since none of your PCs have Prophecy, that seems totally reasonably. However, if any of them pick up Prophecy, you may need to change this, as it would effectively be a huge limitation on that player's ability to use their character's Purview.<br /> <br /> What you'll want to remind your players though is, even if they become Fated to survive, that doesn't mean they can't die. Baldur survives Ragnarok, but dies, for example. So, if someone gets a Fated survival, they can still die. Surviving pretty much just means that they'll be alive as the world is created again.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=926217#post926217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks. I feel like, out of all the Norse, Heimdall's core personality/legend can be summed up by the word 'duty'. He is constantly watching for danger to protect his clan and guards the infamous Ragnorak horn. Since my Visitations are brief, my goal is to show the deity's biggest personality trait. Then I'll add more substance as the game goes on.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might also want to have him be incredibly impatient and rushed to get back to Asgard as he's supposed to be an eternal guardian, and this is probably his first time away from the wall in millennium. Hm, actually, him having a Scion means he's already violated his watch. Tricky. He could be an adopted Scion if you want to really play up his Duty to an exceptional degree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=926217#post926217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps I will add a slight aggression to Freya during her Visitation whenever she's addressing anyone who isn't Leithe. Maybe a willingness to violate personal spaces, maybe some light touching. Still, I think her general demeanor is friendly and energetic to kind of show that as a goddess of fertility and power that she's almost-bursting with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that makes sense for Freya. Part of my internal image of her is exceptionally aloof until someone has something she wants, in which case she's willing to do pretty much anything to get whatever it is. I'm not sure why I have that image in my head, but I think it has to do with her constantly rejecting marriage proposals from ugly entities, but then being down for anything with a handful of dwarves for several days to get her necklace. If you rule that she is the prophetess who tells Odin about Ragnarok, you might want to reign back that friendly bit though.<br /> <br /> The more I write about this, the more I think my Freya is very Ishtar-light. I really need to go over the primary documents for them properly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=926217#post926217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the physical location of the Visitation, I'm tempted to use Central Park where Gridni, the forest maiden, is. To me, Central Park kind of establishes several of the themes of the story. Nature is good, so long as it's controlled by civilization. It represents a connection to the ancient surrounded by the modern, which is how the PCs must feel this early on with deities inserting themselves into their lives. And, it touches on the roles of Heimdall (control) and Freya (life).</div> </div> </div> </div>That's brilliant, go wild with that. I know pretty much nothing about Central Park or New York, but you could do something like the more mortal society breaks down in the coming of the Wolf Time section of Ragnarok (brothers killing brothers, fathers killing sons. Likely not literal compulsive parricide or... I don't know what sibling killing is called. But, that section's more to do with saying 'our social standards are slipping hardcore as kinslaying becomes more prevalent and the social systems used to prevent it are failing') that the park begins to become overgrown, until the park begins to consume the city and an entrance to The Dark Forest opens as the continents are covered by woodland once again, and cities fall.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T07:42:13-07:00","id":926400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=926290#post926290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For A, I am not sure. I think all of the paperwork is Storyteller-side, but any character revisions preformed by Fate will require players to adapt to those changes. It should probably start with a very minimal amount of work, since Hero Fate stuff is pretty gentle, but as you go up in Legend it will grow to rather large heights. For B, I'm sure you could, but it may unbalance the entire system. It in the very least would mess with both Magic and Prophecy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I've read over it, and the answer to A is yes, most of the work is on my end. The only limitation on the players is that I can only allow them to spend their XP at the beginning of the next session, which would give me the time to do the calculations.<br /> <br /> And, I think B is doable. John's Fatebinding system can be broken down into three different sections: Dice Modifiers, Death Penalties, &amp; the XP Bank. Each section has a positive and a negative effect, thus, I could simply deactivate/ignore one or two sections to cut down on the paperwork. I've spoken to one player so far, and, though he agrees that the Shadow XP bank can be frustrating, he is very interested in seeing it in action. I'll ask the others before the next session on Friday.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=926290#post926290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since none of your PCs have Prophecy, that seems totally reasonably. However, if any of them pick up Prophecy, you may need to change this, as it would effectively be a huge limitation on that player's ability to use their character's Purview.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. I'll keep an eye on it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=926290#post926290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you'll want to remind your players though is, even if they become Fated to survive, that doesn't mean they can't die. Baldur survives Ragnarok, but dies, for example. So, if someone gets a Fated survival, they can still die. Surviving pretty much just means that they'll be alive as the world is created again.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's true. Baldur could spring them out when he leaves Hel. Actually, can a Scion become one of the einherjar? We know if a warriors dies well in battle, he can go to Valhalla or to Freya's version. Wouldn't that mean that any Scion of Freya that dies in battle automatically goes to serve their mother in her undead army? <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=926290#post926290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might also want to have him be incredibly impatient and rushed to get back to Asgard as he's supposed to be an eternal guardian, and this is probably his first time away from the wall in millennium. Hm, actually, him having a Scion means he's already violated his watch. Tricky. He could be an adopted Scion if you want to really play up his Duty to an exceptional degree.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's brilliant! I hadn't even considered adopted scions, but it makes perfect sense in this case. Elias' player was originally considering Njord as the divine parent but chose Heimdall because he didn't want to be the only one working out of the Ragnorak book. Now, I could have Heimdall be the parent, but only because of a backroom deal with Njord that Elias will have to discover himself. This also adds another hook and a twist into the Aesir-Vanir differences alongside Leithe. <br /> <br /> And now the session is really coming together in my mind's eye. The Band is currently split between two apartments. In the morning, both halves are woken up by Hugin and Munin knocking on windows, who then tell them to head to Central Park for an important meeting. The Band arrives, gets together, and heads to the Egyptian Obelisk that is located in the Park. (I saw it during my brief visit to NYC a couple of years ago, and assume it was there during 2009.) Vjun will notice Gridni watching them with keen interest, but, since she only knows Vjun, she watches from a distance. Anyone who makes a perception check can notice her and the live flower growing in her hair despite all of the snow around them. <br /> <br /> Freya will already be there standing next to the Obelisk studying it with a wry smile. There'll be some interaction between her and the Band. <br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Hugin and Munin will find Elias and Leithe and guide them to the meeting point. Once they arrive, Freya will go over to Leithe and hug her, and they'll have a quick moment, but it won't be a Visitation proper. She tells the Band that they are waiting on someone to get the ball rolling. <br /> <br /> Heimdall will arrive then, literally running to the meeting point. Once he's there, he goes straight to Elias, claim that he is Elias' father (which is true in Obi-Wan's words, 'from a certain point of view'), rip out Elias' blind eyes before inserting the glass eyes. He then makes a short speech about Elias' new duty to watch over humanity before runs off scene. <br /> <br /> Freya will take her time to gently ease Leithe into Scion-hood and spend a couple more minutes in conversation. Right before she leaves, she reminds the Band that the prophecy that brought them together also warned of a time limit, and they have less than a week to find Thor's Belt before the Devourers secure a major victory.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T14:36:36-07:00","id":926642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=926400#post926400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's true. Baldur could spring them out when he leaves Hel. Actually, can a Scion become one of the einherjar? We know if a warriors dies well in battle, he can go to Valhalla or to Freya's version. Wouldn't that mean that any Scion of Freya that dies in battle automatically goes to serve their mother in her undead army?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a tricky question. First off, I think the Einherjar are technically the warriors residing within Valhalla, while those in F\u00f3lkvangr I think go unnamed. Freya's warriors actually are not mentioned to partake in Ragnarok IIRC. But, from what we know, being taken up by the Valkyries is a thing for humans, so, as long as a Scion is a human, they should be able to be carried up to one of the halls as long as they die in battle.<br /> <br /> What I'd probably rule that as, you can be taken up to Valhalla up until you hit God and cease to be human at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=926400#post926400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heimdall will arrive then, literally running to the meeting point. Once he's there, he goes straight to Elias, claim that he is Elias' father (which is true in Obi-Wan's words, 'from a certain point of view'), rip out Elias' blind eyes before inserting the glass eyes. He then makes a short speech about Elias' new duty to watch over humanity before runs off scene.<br /> <br /> Freya will take her time to gently ease Leithe into Scion-hood and spend a couple more minutes in conversation. Right before she leaves, she reminds the Band that the prophecy that brought them together also warned of a time limit, and they have less than a week to find Thor's Belt before the Devourers secure a major victory.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heimdal would probably just do the whole 'appear' thing he can do due to The Rainbow Bridge pretty much being a colossal teleportation system. (which, interestingly, is a very rare thing mythologically) I think the Norse also had a system of wards and foster children that you could fluff into the Scion Adoption stuff if you wanted, but I'm not actually sure off the top of my head. But, that does sound good.<br /> <br /> Since you're new to running Scion, I will say be ready for the Band to utterly ruin the whole 'we can't find the belt' problem really quickly. Mystery would instantly solve it (unless something exceptionally powerful is hiding it, in which case the Scions... would probably have issues retrieving it at Legend 2) and I think Magic could help a lot if Adrianie's Thread still exists as a Spell in JSR's system.<br /> <br /> If you want to delay the Band from just getting the belt as soon as they know where it is, doing stuff like Utgard Loki's dinner could be a fun way to make them work for it. Social challenges, and the like. If they're really smart, they'll get themselves Hospitalitied by the Jotuns who have the belt, and then not be able to be harmed by them during discussion for the belt unless someone grossly breaks the taboo. (All it would take is being invited in, even if it's under false pretenses. Odin uses that a lot.)<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-05T20:30:47-07:00","id":926811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=926642#post926642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Freya's warriors actually are not mentioned to partake in Ragnarok IIRC.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's actually an interesting question. She gets half the warriors, but we have no idea what she plans for them. Odin, for once, is obvious in his intent to lead the army against Ragnorak. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=926642#post926642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heimdal would probably just do the whole 'appear' thing he can do due to The Rainbow Bridge pretty much being a colossal teleportation system. (which, interestingly, is a very rare thing mythologically).</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, he can do that? I thought that was something Marvel invented. How does it work? Would there be a rainbow, and he walks out of it?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=926642#post926642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since you're new to running Scion, I will say be ready for the Band to utterly ruin the whole 'we can't find the belt' problem really quickly. Mystery would instantly solve it (unless something exceptionally powerful is hiding it, in which case the Scions... would probably have issues retrieving it at Legend 2) and I think Magic could help a lot if Adrianie's Thread still exists as a Spell in JSR's system.<br /> <br /> If you want to delay the Band from just getting the belt as soon as they know where it is, doing stuff like Utgard Loki's dinner could be a fun way to make them work for it. Social challenges, and the like. If they're really smart, they'll get themselves Hospitalitied by the Jotuns who have the belt, and then not be able to be harmed by them during discussion for the belt unless someone grossly breaks the taboo. (All it would take is being invited in, even if it's under false pretenses. Odin uses that a lot.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, to be honest, they're taking longer than I thought they would. Right now, they have a lead to the cult they could explore, but that's all they have. Here are my old notes for where the Belt is and who's guarding it. <br /> <br /> &quot;The Belt is in the hands of a titanspawn. His name was Owney Madden, a Legend 3 Aptranger, former head of the Hell\u2019s Kitchen\u2019s Gopher Gang. It is his lack of notoriety which is the biggest shield against Odin\u2019s seeking vision. He wears the Belt to strengthen his own power and will use it if directly challenged in combat.<br /> <br /> The reason for the time limit is that if Owney unleashes the zombies on NYC, in the chaos a more powerful titanspawn will come for the belt and deliver it to Fafnir. It is Fafnir who is operating the campaign to destroy NYC and herald Fimbulvetr.<br /> <br /> Each night that passes equals to another 20 Zombies for the horde. Owney has been given a relic to make zombies without using his own powers to do so (though he does have the proper boon for it). It is a cursed scepter, created by the Dark elves. It multiplies a user\u2019s own legend so that it creates 20 zombies for the cost of one. The scepter will curse anyone alive that tries to wield it with a deadly virus that will render them a zombie.<br /> <br /> Owen and the zombies are hidden in the HS of Environmental Studies\u2019 (HSES) basement, deep within the city where they can inflict the most damage.<br /> <br /> Yet, that is not where the Dark Alfs are gathering the bodies. For that, they are meeting at Pier 91 at the docks. The bodies are picked up, hidden in a random storage container until the delivery persons leave. Only when the coast is clear do they move the bodies to the HSES.<br /> <br /> The Pier is watched over by a new titan cult called Free of Terror or FOT. Their goal is to free Humanity from the fear of the apocalypse by starting it. Although small, they are zealous. Four members watch over the pier: Liane Kroeker, Ernest Karst, George Bechtold, &amp; Christine Irving. They alternate who\u2019s watching the actual container and who\u2019s patrolling the pier.&quot;<br /> <br /> Now, I don't intend to force the Band to take on all the zombies, who now stand at 60 strong. I'll be honest, I'm not sure how much of a threat they are to the Band (I imagine well beyond them), but the idea is that they realize the danger and fall back out onto the street where cops will reinforce them periodically to the point where they can eventually handle the threat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T10:58:35-07:00","id":927169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=926811#post926811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, he can do that? I thought that was something Marvel invented. How does it work? Would there be a rainbow, and he walks out of it?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not quite as 'teleport-y' as it's shown in Marvel, but it's still insanely powerful in universe. So, The Rainbow Bridge is quite literally a bridge made out of a rainbow. Except, unlike mortal bridges only one end of the bridge is 'anchored' to Asgard. The other end appears to move as it's used to drop various figures off at various points across the Nine Worlds. Since it's a rainbow, which do not branch, it can be safely concluded that the other end of the bridge must be able to move.<br /> <br /> So, by 'teleport' I don't mean in a sci-fi transporter sort of way, but in a 'can connect any two places together' sort of way. It's also the only way into Asgard pretty much unless you physically climb the tree or fly I suppose.<br /> <br /> Heimdal wouldn't just appear in a flash like the Rainbow Bridge works in Marvel, but instead he would walk down a rainbow which is touching the ground wherever he needs to go. And, when he's finished, he just walks back up it. The other Aesir can use this too, obviously. It's pretty much just a bridge that has one end that's mobile across planes.<br /> <br /> In Pan-Pantheon games, the Bifrost is actually flat out one of the most powerful military tools the Aesir have. The Bifrost and Gugnir are incredibly powerful militarily.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=926811#post926811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, I don't intend to force the Band to take on all the zombies, who now stand at 60 strong. I'll be honest, I'm not sure how much of a threat they are to the Band (I imagine well beyond them), but the idea is that they realize the danger and fall back out onto the street where cops will reinforce them periodically to the point where they can eventually handle the threat.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a White Room scenario, a Band of Legend 2 Scions probably would have that as a death sentence. But, outside of that, it actually is pretty simple to deal with. However, I think that may be because of the years of playing Scion, having a lot of practice getting a grip on the capacity of Scions, and having a good grip on how explosives are terrifying up to Legend 5-6. There are three ways off the top of my head to deal with the problem without any difficulty, killing Owney in the process without actually fighting him since that sounds a bit dangerous.<br /> <br /> 1. Drop the building on them. Epic Manipulation or Charisma characters can convince people they have permission to do this with minimal effort. Some Knacks would be more useful than others. Epic Intelligence folks can work out where the structure should be targeted to cause an implosion collapse. Epic Social people again get explosive, or Epic Int people just make it. Epic Dex people hide it (with floor plans gained from the city, all public domain stuff, maybe sped up with Epic Socials) where the Epic Int people said to. Boom, building falls in on itself, go through and dismember anything that's animated while pinned under rubble, ect.<br /> <br /> 2. Gas main leak. Epic Int characters get their hands on the city's schematics, possibly sped up with Epic Socials. Work out just where to puncture a gas main, and by how much. Send the Epic Dex people or Epic Strength people down to go it, wait a bit (Epic Int people would be able to calculate this without even needing a roll with Math Genious) and toss a match. More collateral damage, but the problem'll be solved.<br /> <br /> 3. Sneak a series of explosives inside. Epic Int, Epic Dex, and Epic Social people pull a big ruse on the Dark Elves and stuff that day's corpses with explosives, let them be carried into the building, wait a little bit, and detonate. Boom. No problem. It would be super weird for anyone to notice this since Norse reanimation stuff doesn't need any surgery or anything. Just a simple rune slapped onto a corpse.<br /> <br /> Now, if you want to make the world aware of it, and solve it even faster, you just send the Epic Social people to the local military base and bing bang boom, problem solved. If you really don't want to let the mortals know what's up, there are also normally a big list of special ways to dispose of various mythological nasties. I don't know any off the top of my head that deals with Draugr, but, I bet there's a weird weakness somewhere like how mirrors can banish a lot of antagonistic entities for the Kami, or just having a bunch of Iron'll keep the Sidhe away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T13:00:30-07:00","id":927243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=927169#post927169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heimdal wouldn't just appear in a flash like the Rainbow Bridge works in Marvel, but instead he would walk down a rainbow which is touching the ground wherever he needs to go. And, when he's finished, he just walks back up it. The other Aesir can use this too, obviously. It's pretty much just a bridge that has one end that's mobile across planes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Much more of a dignified entrance and exit for Heimdall, I like it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=927169#post927169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In a White Room scenario, a Band of Legend 2 Scions probably would have that as a death sentence. But, outside of that, it actually is pretty simple to deal with. However, I think that may be because of the years of playing Scion, having a lot of practice getting a grip on the capacity of Scions, and having a good grip on how explosives are terrifying up to Legend 5-6. There are three ways off the top of my head to deal with the problem without any difficulty, killing Owney in the process without actually fighting him since that sounds a bit dangerous.<br /> <br /> ~~~~<br /> <br /> Now, if you want to make the world aware of it, and solve it even faster, you just send the Epic Social people to the local military base and bing bang boom, problem solved. If you really don't want to let the mortals know what's up, there are also normally a big list of special ways to dispose of various mythological nasties. I don't know any off the top of my head that deals with Draugr, but, I bet there's a weird weakness somewhere like how mirrors can banish a lot of antagonistic entities for the Kami, or just having a bunch of Iron'll keep the Sidhe away.</div> </div> </div> </div>*writes down notes* <br /> <br /> Hm, my boss fight doesn't seem nearly as epic now. <br /> <br /> I was aiming for the incident to become public and using that to explain how the Band's Legend jumps up to 3 by the start of the next session. Then, the next campaign was going to be much more socially based as it was going to focus on the Band interacting with politicians and becoming a part of the food chain of NYC's political house. (I was even going to throw in Trump for a cameo or a chance to screw around with him.) <br /> <br /> My basic campaign list was supposed to look like this. <br /> First campaign: tutorial, a little mix of everything<br /> Second: Mostly social, emphasis on Band-mortal interaction<br /> Third: Mental, deal with supernatural world, but not gods-level per se. I was going to introduce the first rival Band-mate here. <br /> Fourth: Physical, new major threat to Midgard, emphasis on god-Band interaction<br /> <br /> And then it was going to start repeating itself. Another campaign focused on interacting with mortals, then mid-level supernatural creatures, then back to gods. Rinse and repeat as vary what kind of challenges I throw at them until they hit god-hood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-06T13:36:57-07:00","id":927256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=927243#post927243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*writes down notes*<br /> <br /> Hm, my boss fight doesn't seem nearly as epic now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, your players might not do it that way. That's just the way I immediately thought to deal with the problem most efficiently. Now, if you had someone from a Valor Pantheon, or a Physical Irish Scion who wanted to make a name for themselves, it could go very differently. Valor would gravely discourage such action, and a Irish Scion who wants to get the title/role of Hero would probably try to fight them all while monologuing about their various victories and the truly impressive size of their genitals.<br /> <br /> 'Boss Fights' in Scion can be a bit tricky since combat is terrifying. I don't know if you're using RAW, or JSR's Knacks, but essentially combat comes down to some simple things. 1. Bait out the target's Skin Shedding, 2. Hit them so hard they don't have a chance to blink. It's incredibly mythic, lots of just flat out destruction, but not really a DnD-esque Dragon Fight for example.<br /> <br /> Like, if you have a lot of Legend to burn, and want to ruin someone's day, you Opening Gambit + Between the Ticks to pop out four attacks (double attacking) which you've made deal Agg damage. Toss on a bunch of Virtue Channels, and a Deed somewhere, and something's just been obliterated.<br /> <br /> If you want something similar to a Boss fight, go with a big complicated challenge. Lots of little enemies for the half-combat Scions, give the Mental Scions some sort of puzzle to figure out, give the Social Scions something to do, and then toss some big thing for the Lugh/Thor/Sun Wukong/Susano-O of your Band to have a punch up with. Absolute clusterfucks sort of work best for 'Boss fights' rather than one big fucker. Especially if you have non-Physical things going on for the other Scions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=927243#post927243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was aiming for the incident to become public and using that to explain how the Band's Legend jumps up to 3 by the start of the next session. Then, the next campaign was going to be much more socially based as it was going to focus on the Band interacting with politicians and becoming a part of the food chain of NYC's political house. (I was even going to throw in Trump for a cameo or a chance to screw around with him.)</div> </div> </div> </div>That can totally work. The explosions could totally lead to the Scions getting caught. While Legend 2 means they can probably get the problem solved, they'll be still vulnerable to being caught most likely. They could game notoriety through that.<br /> <br /> What you should remember though with Social Scions and Mortals is that by the time they hit Legend 4, they'll be The Big Players on a large scale. National, or even Internationally. They will be the trickiest, most beautiful, or most charismatic people have seen or heard of ever (since the last Scion died off. I think that would have been Ragnar, Scion of Odin way back? Either him, or Freyr's kid who became King of Sweden and started their royal line I think.) and could shake the world. At... Legend 5 we had two Greek Scions have a 16 year old boy elected to the office of President of the United States, and have a national referendem to entirely change the political system into an Empire with the new sixteen year old Emperor having total control. Some lands were given up to various Pantheons (for example, Hawaii to the Polynesian Pantheon, and some large swaths were given to the more powerful Native American Pantheons) for alliances, ect. But, the world changed in a month. I think the next month, Greece, Spain, Italy, and France (the Nemetondevos had been dealt with) were absorbed into the growing Imperial State with not a complaint from a Mortal. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=927243#post927243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My basic campaign list was supposed to look like this.<br /> First campaign: tutorial, a little mix of everything<br /> Second: Mostly social, emphasis on Band-mortal interaction<br /> Third: Mental, deal with supernatural world, but not gods-level per se. I was going to introduce the first rival Band-mate here.<br /> Fourth: Physical, new major threat to Midgard, emphasis on god-Band interaction<br /> <br /> And then it was going to start repeating itself. Another campaign focused on interacting with mortals, then mid-level supernatural creatures, then back to gods. Rinse and repeat as vary what kind of challenges I throw at them until they hit god-hood.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see that, not a bad pattern. I'd probably avoid having some stories mainly one thing or another, since that can be pretty disheartening as a player to not be very relevant for two stories. But, I can see that the pattern could work.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T08:44:25-07:00","id":927637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=927256#post927256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That can totally work. The explosions could totally lead to the Scions getting caught. While Legend 2 means they can probably get the problem solved, they'll be still vulnerable to being caught most likely. They could game notoriety through that.<br /> <br /> What you should remember though with Social Scions and Mortals is that by the time they hit Legend 4, they'll be The Big Players on a large scale. National, or even Internationally. They will be the trickiest, most beautiful, or most charismatic people have seen or heard of ever (since the last Scion died off. I think that would have been Ragnar, Scion of Odin way back? Either him, or Freyr's kid who became King of Sweden and started their royal line I think.) and could shake the world. At... Legend 5 we had two Greek Scions have a 16 year old boy elected to the office of President of the United States, and have a national referendem to entirely change the political system into an Empire with the new sixteen year old Emperor having total control. Some lands were given up to various Pantheons (for example, Hawaii to the Polynesian Pantheon, and some large swaths were given to the more powerful Native American Pantheons) for alliances, ect. But, the world changed in a month. I think the next month, Greece, Spain, Italy, and France (the Nemetondevos had been dealt with) were absorbed into the growing Imperial State with not a complaint from a Mortal.<br /> <br /> ~~~<br /> <br /> I can see that, not a bad pattern. I'd probably avoid having some stories mainly one thing or another, since that can be pretty disheartening as a player to not be very relevant for two stories. But, I can see that the pattern could work.</div> </div> </div> </div>*takes more notes* <br /> <br /> That sounds like it was a fun game!<br /> <br /> Agreed, I'm only having the spotlight be on one major area, but I intend to include other challenges so that everyone is engaged. <br /> <br /> For this first campaign, the Ragnorak strike happens if the Band fails to get to stop the zombie horde before December 21st. It'll be a bigger loss if Thor's belt is lost to the Dark Alfs, but just the zombie horde being unleashed will be enough to bring Fimbulvinter a step closer. <br /> <br /> Now, the one connection the Band has to locating the High School is the cult. One of the first cult members offered an invitation to Jamie and any of her associates for them to attend a meeting. Even if the Band doesn't go this route, they still know which Pier the bodies are going to, so they will always have a method to move the story closer, whether they interrogate the cult there or beat them up and follow the trail there. If they do go to the meeting, the invitation didn't include an address but a request to come back to Pier 91 the next night. If they do, the cult will say that this proves their interest and that the meeting will start the next day. So, if they go through with the social route, that's two days lost and another 40 zombies for the horde. <br /> <br /> The session will be tomorrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-07T10:20:09-07:00","id":927668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=927637#post927637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For this first campaign, the Ragnorak strike happens if the Band fails to get to stop the zombie horde before December 21st. It'll be a bigger loss if Thor's belt is lost to the Dark Alfs, but just the zombie horde being unleashed will be enough to bring Fimbulvinter a step closer.<br /> <br /> Now, the one connection the Band has to locating the High School is the cult. One of the first cult members offered an invitation to Jamie and any of her associates for them to attend a meeting. Even if the Band doesn't go this route, they still know which Pier the bodies are going to, so they will always have a method to move the story closer, whether they interrogate the cult there or beat them up and follow the trail there. If they do go to the meeting, the invitation didn't include an address but a request to come back to Pier 91 the next night. If they do, the cult will say that this proves their interest and that the meeting will start the next day. So, if they go through with the social route, that's two days lost and another 40 zombies for the horde.<br /> <br /> The session will be tomorrow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a plan, I'm interested to hear how it goes. The Social people may just force the cult into talking instead of waiting for the meeting, could be done through Appearance, Charisma, or Manipulation pretty well in different ways. But, that assumes they're as paranoid as I am when playing which they very well may not be. (My immediate thought would be that a meeting at a predetermined time would be an ambush, so I'd just batter them over the head with Blurt it Out, or Charmer) <br /> <br /> I hope the game goes well!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T13:43:00-07:00","id":928394,"title":"","content":"After listening to the advice in the Fatebinding thread, I've decided to scale back the system since I don't have the time to invest into binders and binders' worth of material. So, I'm going to jettison the XP bank and the death resolutions sections, leaving the dice modifier rules since this is my 'first' run of Scion and all of these players are new.<br /> <br /> I'm also junking my Legendary XP idea and just making it story-based. I'm including the epic fail house rule from John's list.<br /> <br /> Are there any other house rules (John's or otherwise) that people think are necessary? I'm thinking of adding their Relic and Knack house rules, but nothing else comes to mind.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-08T14:05:38-07:00","id":928410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=928394#post928394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any other house rules (John's or otherwise) that people think are necessary? I'm thinking of adding their Relic and Knack house rules, but nothing else comes to mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh man, okay, yeah. So, first off, grab the Knacks and Boons. RAW has really unbalanced stuff, and some of it is exceptionally game breaking (Untouchable Opponent becomes almost statistically impossible to counter IIRC) RAW Jotunblut is very... it doesn't work brilliantly the moment you get beyond Hero, and JSR has a pretty decent one for the Physical characters. It's unfortunately not as good for the Social or Mental ones however.<br /> <br /> I'd also say you'll want to use the houserules for Birthrights. Creatures, and Followers both don't really... work if you don't do that. A 5 Dot Creature will be pretty nice at Hero, and then at Demigod die like a leaf in a storm from Typhon's wings. Furthermore, the 1 - Star Dot Relics make the world more... sensible. Like, Thor's Hammer, The Spear of Victory, and Smoking Bolt couldn't possibly be 5 Dot Relics. Those are within the reach of a Legend 2 Scion, and are thereby balanced for the Heroes. But, this means at Demigod and God they become increasingly weak since they can't scale up any more in RAW which doesn't make sense. Thor without his hammer in myth is dangerously weakened, RAW Thor without his hammer is mildly inconvenienced and gains very minimal benefit from wielding it.<br /> <br /> It also lets you actually have mythic-accurate Relics in the game. For example, The Dagda's Club can kill nine people per swing it is so huge (it's also so big it needs wheels on it) which is a really substantial power depending on how you stat it. If it allows him to essentially Cleve attack 9 people at a time, that's utterly insanely powerful, but accurate to the myth. (One of) Lugh's Spear(s) gives the wielder Victory, whoever wields it becoming incapable of losing a fight, which is equally insanely powerful. Manannan's Sword is always lethal even if it only inflicts the smallest scratch (it also can cut through anything, forces people to tell the truth, and commands the winds) which is frighteningly almost broken. (The Tuatha have a crazy list of incredibly powerful Relics, I could go on for ages) Odin's Spear is a good Norse example of a Star Dot Relic, as it's like Lugh's Spear I just mentioned except is for external use. None of these Relics can actually work with the 1 - 5 scale in RAW, so I'd advise swapping to the 1 - Star system.<br /> <br /> Let's see, what else. Some people allow characters to swap one of their Virtues out for another, but since you're past Chargen that may be a bit difficult. Changing how you use Boons is also pretty popular. Moving from an Epic + Ability to Purview Rank + Ability using the number of Dots in the Purview to give Autos on the Epic Attribute Scale. (This prevents things like all Fire Gods needing to be Manipulative unless they're content with being terrible with their Purview, ect)<br /> <br /> If you want the houserules I use, they can be found <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/home\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. They are not complete, with the three of us working on the rules locked in a battle dancing between nasty sickness, and University, but the core systems are present. I've not been knocked down for the count this summer yet though! It's normally one of our specters slowing things. You'd need to supplement some Purviews and the like from other sources like JSR or the like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T07:21:11-07:00","id":928723,"title":"","content":"Alright, we had our session yesterday. My players told me it was fun, but there were a couple of problems.<br /> <br /> On the mechanics-side, I did what I said I was going to do in my last post. And, as advised, I went ahead and completely switch out the boons and knacks from the core rulebook for John's set. This led to a mini-session after playing where I went through the list and tried to figure out what changes were necessary. Some knacks like Untouchable Opponent (which was a popular one) were replaced by their precursors. I don't think I eliminated any outright, but I had trouble finding one or two and intend to do a complete sweep during the time before the next session. Because everyone is still Legend 2, thankfully this is a good time to make the change since nobody has an easy list to modify. Although, Elias' player is using the opportunity to rebuild Elias from the ground up with the new system, but keeping much of his character's lore the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-09T14:33:51-07:00","id":928907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=928723#post928723\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, we had our session yesterday. My players told me it was fun, but there were a couple of problems.<br /> <br /> On the mechanics-side, I did what I said I was going to do in my last post. And, as advised, I went ahead and completely switch out the boons and knacks from the core rulebook for John's set. This led to a mini-session after playing where I went through the list and tried to figure out what changes were necessary. Some knacks like Untouchable Opponent (which was a popular one) were replaced by their precursors. I don't think I eliminated any outright, but I had trouble finding one or two and intend to do a complete sweep during the time before the next session. Because everyone is still Legend 2, thankfully this is a good time to make the change since nobody has an easy list to modify. Although, Elias' player is using the opportunity to rebuild Elias from the ground up with the new system, but keeping much of his character's lore the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, entirely a good plan to do it as early as possible if you're going to do it. Which ones have you had trouble finding alternatives to? If the names changed, I might know where they went, or if they were removed entirely, I may be able to explain why if they were one of the more problematic powers. Obviously, I can't speak for John and Anne, but you might be able to email them and possibly get some questions answered if you want their thoughts.<br /> <br /> Do you know how Elias player is changing their character around? I might be able to offer suggestions for your, or their end if anything is needed.<br /> <br /> If you've got any other houserule-y questions, or the like, more than happy to answer to the best of my abilities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T08:41:23-07:00","id":929755,"title":"","content":"Boy has life been busy. <br /> <br /> Mark (Elias' player) realized that his PC was overlapping with Jamie and wanted to use John's houserules to distinguish the two of them. For starter's, he's changed from two glass eyes to one. He's moving from a subterfuge character to a much more intellectual one, which would be good since I don't think we have a Mental powerhouse. <br /> <br /> The only power that's given me issue is that I can't find the 'peaceful meeting' boon from Ragnorak in the houserules. I admit, I've only taken a quick look since the session, so that might resolve itself.<br /> <br /> The last problem I had was volume. The guys in this circle of friends are loud, while the gals are kinda quiet. Because the guys were sitting next to me, the gals could hardly hear me throughout the entire session. Next time, I plan on the gals sitting next to me and having the guys at the other end of the table. <br /> <br /> Now for a quick recap: the Band successfully watched the two Visitations. I think I stumbled a little bit here and there, and Freya came off as way too nice, but it was done. Elias got a little jealous that Freya doted on Leithe (there was a hug), while Heimdall was brusque. From there, the Band chatted a little bit before they went back to the Pier and contacted that cultist, who told them about the meeting. The rest of the session was in downtime for the rest of the day. Lad, Jamie, Katya, and Elias did some investigating to see what they could come up with the names of the cultists, location of the meeting point, and anything else. Vjun went back to Central Park and spent some time with Gridni and beat up a hoodlum who was spray-painting in the park.<br /> <br /> And, we now seem to have all varieties of animal communication. The Irish wolfhound speaks English, the rat speaks to Katya because he's a ghost, while Vjun can speak 'ferret'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T12:06:04-07:00","id":929879,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=929755#post929755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Boy has life been busy.<br /> <br /> Mark (Elias' player) realized that his PC was overlapping with Jamie and wanted to use John's houserules to distinguish the two of them. For starter's, he's changed from two glass eyes to one. He's moving from a subterfuge character to a much more intellectual one, which would be good since I don't think we have a Mental powerhouse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Having a Mental powerhouse is probably a really good addition. Mental is a silent killer in the sheer amount of stuff it can do when coupled with people skilled in the other areas. I a lot of game I've seen, the first Story has a clause allowing people to alter their characters for the first session or two to make sure they work as the player intended for situations just like this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=929755#post929755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only power that's given me issue is that I can't find the 'peaceful meeting' boon from Ragnorak in the houserules. I admit, I've only taken a quick look since the session, so that might resolve itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah! Peaceful Meeting. So, Peaceful Meeting is a great idea for a Boon, really awesome, totally Mythic, and works within many ancient Societies, especially the Norse. (All that Hospitality stuff I've been going on about) The only problem is that it is an amazing <i>Justice</i> Boon, not a Magic Boon. It is exceptionally tangentially related to Magic, while it is exactly within Justice's realm of control. Enforcing the social rules of Hospitality with powers is more of a Tyr thing than a Freya thing (or, Zeus than Hermes, Nuada than Manannan, Amaterasu than Hotei, ect) for example.<br /> <br /> It can be really nicely retooled into a Justice Boon though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=929755#post929755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The last problem I had was volume. The guys in this circle of friends are loud, while the gals are kinda quiet. Because the guys were sitting next to me, the gals could hardly hear me throughout the entire session. Next time, I plan on the gals sitting next to me and having the guys at the other end of the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately, I've got no experience on that one. I play online, and I've not ST'd or played in person for ages. Best I could probably suggest is telling the lads that people're having problems hearing and if they'd mind, quieting down while you're explaining things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=929755#post929755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now for a quick recap: the Band successfully watched the two Visitations. I think I stumbled a little bit here and there, and Freya came off as way too nice, but it was done. Elias got a little jealous that Freya doted on Leithe (there was a hug), while Heimdall was brusque. From there, the Band chatted a little bit before they went back to the Pier and contacted that cultist, who told them about the meeting. The rest of the session was in downtime for the rest of the day. Lad, Jamie, Katya, and Elias did some investigating to see what they could come up with the names of the cultists, location of the meeting point, and anything else. Vjun went back to Central Park and spent some time with Gridni and beat up a hoodlum who was spray-painting in the park.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't sound too bad. If you want to make Freya scarier next time people run into her, check out the human sacrifice stuff the Norse practiced. I can't remember the exact details of who it was for, but that sort of thing always makes modern characters a bit cautious. I know there is suspected Odin sacrifice to do with hanging, or the strangulation of the corpses we keep turning up in the Nordic Bogs.<br /> <br /> Checking Wikipedia (which I normally suggest people be cautious with, but it's a good spot to find your primary sources), it looks like Adam of Bremen wrote about the Swedish royal line preforming human sacrifice. Since they trace their descent from Freyr, you could do some fun stuff with Freya about that. If you want to surprise your players, if Fimbulwinter kicks off, you could show them that there's a rash of kidnappings through the hemisphere centered on NYC. They could suspect Titan Cult, kick down the doors, and find Freya and Freyr overseeing a monumental series of human sacrifices trying to restore fertility to the land and hold back Fimbulwinter. (which is one of the first steps in bringing about the death of Freyr) This would all be above board to the Aesir, and Odin would probably be encouraging it in his attempts to hold back The End as much as possible. Blood, sex, fertility, all that could easily work together to severe the players out on the topic of Freya, and make them realize the Gods and Goddesses do not hold to their children's morality in the slightest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T12:01:27-07:00","id":930965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=929879#post929879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah! Peaceful Meeting. It can be really nicely retooled into a Justice Boon though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, it was originally listed as a Magic boon. For this game, I'll allow it to stand, but for future reference you think it should be Justice? What level?<br /> <br /> And, boy, does my prep time feel like it's fading fast. The game is going to be tomorrow (the gang had always wanted it to be on Thursdays) after my shift. So, I have only a day left to get ready. Now, we're picking it up on the 16th, and the Band is going to go to the home of the cultist they met the other day. I plan on her, another cultist, and the leader, Uhry, to be there. The cultists are going to try to enlist the Band for their cause. Of the cultists, only Uhry knows where the bodies are going, and, in fact, doesn't know what's happening to them. Although charismatic, Uhry is ultimately just a greedy guy who's being paid in gold by the Svart-alfs. The other cultists are orphans, social outcasts, and the like who feel like they now have a purpose in following Uhry.<br /> <br /> Again, the Band could just simply beat up Uhry for the info. He'll talk if he truly thinks he's about to die. (Physical)<br /> <br /> If they kill him before getting the info, searching his body will lead them to his uptown apartment which will have enough clues for the Band to find the location of the zombie basement. (Mental)<br /> <br /> Or they could try to out-bribe the Svart-alfs. If they can't do that, they won't be able to persuade Uhry to give up the location without using Social powers. (I wonder if I should allow seduction as one option). And, they could faux-join for more info. That option is the one I'm most wary of. (Social)<br /> <br /> Are there any other paths they could take that I missed?<br /> <br /> And, I was considering two last, huge, house-rules. We all know how the auto-successes start multiplying the more god-like a scion gets. Well, what if instead of it multiplying like it does, it always sticks to sequential order? Instead of 1-2-4-7-11, it'd be 1-2-3-4-5 and so on. Because I've heard that god-level games get ridiculously unbalanced.<br /> <br /> The other houserule is to have only the most famous/infamous deities be Level 12. So, unlike Ragnorak where even Forseti and Uller are Legend 12, only Odin, Thor, and Loki would be Legend 12 because they have best stood the test of time. Is that reasonable or a bad idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-13T13:46:35-07:00","id":931011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=930965#post930965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, it was originally listed as a Magic boon. For this game, I'll allow it to stand, but for future reference you think it should be Justice? What level?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Magic is kind of infamous for having powers that should be in other Purviews. Mostly because the RAW Fatebinding system was so... ineffective, Magic couldn't really interact like it as you would expect the Purview would, so it stole a bunch of stuff from other Purview's areas of influence. Let's see if I can make a list...<br /> <br /> Scion Adoption Rite should be a Justice power. Complex systems of adoption (or similar things) are present in many ancient cultures and have nothing at all to do with Fate. In the very least, if Magic can do this, Justice should be allowed to do it as well. But, in my mind, it should just be for Justice.<br /> <br /> Transient Visitation should be Psychopomp or Illusion. Magic has nothing to do with dreams. Sure, you're giving a Visitation through dreams, but Morpheus for example should be able to do that without buying up a bunch of Magic and instead just use his existing dream powers.<br /> <br /> Illwind Cures from Ragnarok should be in Health since it's causing someone's body to do something. If it is to be kept in Magic it should just cause people to keep making or causing minor Social faux pas which <i>would</i> be in the realm of Fate.<br /> <br /> Demand a Labor is just Justice again. &quot;Do XYZ for me because I'm King/Queen/A God.&quot; Magic has nothing to do with the functioning of this unless Fate is shoehorned in. It doesn't even compel someone to do things as part of their Fate. It's just a Justice Boon.<br /> <br /> Peaceful Meeting itself works just fine at the same rank as it is in Magic, just make it a Justice Boon. Maybe swap the roll to Charisma + Academics/Occult/Command.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=930965#post930965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, boy, does my prep time feel like it's fading fast. The game is going to be tomorrow (the gang had always wanted it to be on Thursdays) after my shift. So, I have only a day left to get ready. Now, we're picking it up on the 16th, and the Band is going to go to the home of the cultist they met the other day. I plan on her, another cultist, and the leader, Uhry, to be there. The cultists are going to try to enlist the Band for their cause. Of the cultists, only Uhry knows where the bodies are going, and, in fact, doesn't know what's happening to them. Although charismatic, Uhry is ultimately just a greedy guy who's being paid in gold by the Svart-alfs. The other cultists are orphans, social outcasts, and the like who feel like they now have a purpose in following Uhry.<br /> <br /> Again, the Band could just simply beat up Uhry for the info. He'll talk if he truly thinks he's about to die. (Physical)<br /> <br /> If they kill him before getting the info, searching his body will lead them to his uptown apartment which will have enough clues for the Band to find the location of the zombie basement. (Mental)<br /> <br /> Or they could try to out-bribe the Svart-alfs. If they can't do that, they won't be able to persuade Uhry to give up the location without using Social powers. (I wonder if I should allow seduction as one option). And, they could faux-join for more info. That option is the one I'm most wary of. (Social)<br /> <br /> Are there any other paths they could take that I missed?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm...<br /> <br /> For Physical, they could just shadow Uhry everywhere (Dexterity) until they learn the location.<br /> <br /> For Mental, they could go all Holmes on it, examine their shoes, clothes, ect to work out where in the city this was happening (Int, Perception, and Wits all possible).<br /> <br /> For Social, they could do a huge amount of things since this is sort of Social's place to shine. They could seduce him (Appearance), make him enamored with them (Appearance or Charisma), intimidate him (Appearance or Charisma), trick him to let it slip (Manipulation), pretend to be a cultist who needs information (Manipulation), befriend him (Charisma), a bunch of stuff. Blurt it Out (Manipulation), and Charmer (Charisma) are the two easiest ways just to force him to talk to the Band and spill the beans.<br /> <br /> Edit: Something I didn't notice was you mentioning they'd <i>need</i> to bribe him. I'd probably throw that out the window, it's a limitation being put onto Social for no real reason. Physical and Mental neither have a limiter like that. Keep in mind that Social Scions are above and beyond mortals. Humans can convince other people to do what they want, despite bribes or even death on the line of they didn't. Now, Scions are even better then that. Giving an alternate to the bribe could help, but I wouldn't require it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=930965#post930965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And, I was considering two last, huge, house-rules. We all know how the auto-successes start multiplying the more god-like a scion gets. Well, what if instead of it multiplying like it does, it always sticks to sequential order? Instead of 1-2-4-7-11, it'd be 1-2-3-4-5 and so on. Because I've heard that god-level games get ridiculously unbalanced.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to alter how Epics work, you need to go through and edit how many powers (Bona Fortuna, Animal Aspect, and that one Animal Boon where you eat animal bits to gain dice IIRC) to balance them with this new scale. Furthermore, you need to nerf how armor, and weapons work, along with Untouchable Opponent (As now it would work exactly as it did pre-previous nerf, and Body Armor) and you would need to nerf Self-Healing and Regeneration least they just become the staple of combat. Do Not Want from Appearance too IIRC would make everything a bit wonky.<br /> <br /> Additionally, all Deities become incredibly weak. Here, I'll give you a breakdown of... The Dagda (legend 12) and CuChulain (Legend 4) fighting.<br /> <br /> The Dagda's Dodge at Legend 12: <b>12</b> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">(10 Athletics + 5 Dexterity = 15 / 2 = 8 [rounded up]. + Epic Dexterity 4 = 12)</span><br /> The Dagda's Lethal Soak at Legend 12: <b>20</b> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">(10 Stamina = 10. + Epic Stamina 10 = 20.)</span><br /> The Dagda's Agg Soak at Legend 12: <b>10</b> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">(Epic Stamina 10)</span><br /> The Dagda's Hit with Club at Legend 12: 14 dice + 4 Autos = <b>11 average</b>. <span style=\"font-size:9px\">(10 Melee + 5 Dexterity -1 club (Using Quauhololli template) = 14. + Epic Dexterity 4)</span><br /> The Dagda's Damage with Club at Legend 12: 27 dice + 10 Autos = <b>24 average</b>. <span style=\"font-size:9px\">(10 Melee + 10 Strength + 7 Club (Using Quauhololli template) = 27 dice. +10 Epic Strength Autos)</span><br /> <br /> CuChulain's Parry DV at Legend 4: <b>9</b> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">(5 Melee + 5 Dexterity + 1 Mundane Spear [Naginata template] = 11 / 2 = 6 [rounded up] + 3 = 9.)</span><br /> CuChulain's Lethal Soak at Legend 4: <b>8</b> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">(5 Stamina = 5. + Epic Stamina 3 =8)</span><br /> CuChulain's Agg Soak at Legend 4: <b>3</b> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">(3 Epic Stamina)</span><br /> CuChulain's Hit with mundane Spear at Legend 4: 11 dice + 3 autos = <b>9 average</b> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">(5 Melee + 5 Dexterity + 1 Mundane Spear [Naginata template] = 11. +3 Automatic Successes from Epic Dex 3)</span><br /> CuChulain's Damage with mundane Spear at Legend 4: 14 dice + 3 autos = <b>10 average</b> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">(5 Melee + 5 Strength + 4 Mundane Spear [Naginata template] = 14. +3 Automatic Successes from Epic Strength 3)</span><br /> <br /> What we can see with this is, without using any buffs, a Legend 12 primarily Physical God and a Legend 4 primarily Physical Scion are <i>incredibly</i> close in several areas. The sheer power of weapons adding some dice is also apparent. The Dagda would only need a slightly below average roll (-3 successes from average) and be unable to hit CuChulain who is 8 Legend below him for example. Add in various other dice adders, armor, and Stunts and a Hero could easily throw down with a God who doesn't have Animal for example. (In total, Animal could be giving someone +30 extra dice on any of these rolls between Animal Aspect and the eating one I think at Legend 12, which makes Animal even more powerful.<br /> <br /> It also really nerfs Socials too in a round about way. I can't remember the exact details of JSR's social resist stuff, but it would make things even more funky than they start with.<br /> <br /> So, feel free to make that change, but you'll have to change a whole lot of things. Additionally, your players will be far less distinct from each other (Someone who has 2 Epic Dex and someone with 5 Epic Dex are only 3 Successes apart) and they will be comparatively way more powerful. Also, actually, Mortals become <i>hugely</i> powerful. I think some of the explosives in Companion could easily kill The Dagda up there.<br /> <br /> God Level games are <i>crazy</i> unbalanced, but that's sort of the point. Scion is essentially a game of hyper-specialization. Honestly, God level stuff is more problematic because of Avatars, Ultimates, and Pantheon Politics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=930965#post930965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other houserule is to have only the most famous/infamous deities be Level 12. So, unlike Ragnorak where even Forseti and Uller are Legend 12, only Odin, Thor, and Loki would be Legend 12 because they have best stood the test of time. Is that reasonable or a bad idea?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, changing how RAW assigns Legend is probably a good idea. Generally, I wouldn't do it quite so simplistically based off how much we remember them since that unfairly shafts pre-literate cultures. We normally examine Legend based on three areas. Cult Presence, Persistence into Modernity, and In-Universe Power. So, while you may have a Deity with like 0 cult worship, they single handedly slapped a Titan back into its prison. That means they're probably pretty high up there for example.<br /> <br /> But yeah, Forseti and Uller are probably Legend 10. Loki, Thor, Odin, Tyr, Sif, Frigg, Baldur, Freya, Freyr, Njord, Heimdal and Hel are probably all Legend 12 off the top of my head. I might be missing someone though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 07-13-2016, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T08:12:35-07:00","id":931364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=931011#post931011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm...<br /> <br /> For Physical, they could just shadow Uhry everywhere (Dexterity) until they learn the location.<br /> <br /> For Mental, they could go all Holmes on it, examine their shoes, clothes, ect to work out where in the city this was happening (Int, Perception, and Wits all possible).<br /> <br /> For Social, they could do a huge amount of things since this is sort of Social's place to shine. They could seduce him (Appearance), make him enamored with them (Appearance or Charisma), intimidate him (Appearance or Charisma), trick him to let it slip (Manipulation), pretend to be a cultist who needs information (Manipulation), befriend him (Charisma), a bunch of stuff. Blurt it Out (Manipulation), and Charmer (Charisma) are the two easiest ways just to force him to talk to the Band and spill the beans.<br /> <br /> Edit: Something I didn't notice was you mentioning they'd <i>need</i> to bribe him. I'd probably throw that out the window, it's a limitation being put onto Social for no real reason. Physical and Mental neither have a limiter like that. Keep in mind that Social Scions are above and beyond mortals. Humans can convince other people to do what they want, despite bribes or even death on the line of they didn't. Now, Scions are even better then that. Giving an alternate to the bribe could help, but I wouldn't require it.</div> </div> </div> </div>*jots down notes* I forgot that they could simply shadow him. Alright, I have the basic concepts down, now I need to work on the actual details.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=931011#post931011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you want to alter how Epics work, you need to go through and edit how many powers (Bona Fortuna, Animal Aspect, and that one Animal Boon where you eat animal bits to gain dice IIRC) to balance them with this new scale. <br /> <br /> ~snip~ <br /> <br /> God Level games are <i>crazy</i> unbalanced, but that's sort of the point. Scion is essentially a game of hyper-specialization. Honestly, God level stuff is more problematic because of Avatars, Ultimates, and Pantheon Politics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hm, that does sound too harsh (and too much paperwork) at this point. I still have time to work with it, but maybe a different curve. All Heroes get +1 to their Autos, Demigods get +3s, and Gods get +5s?<br /> <br /> I'd imagine that reducing the number of Legend 12 deities would help reign in the Avatar &amp; Ultimate problems. How does Pantheon Politics screw things up? I would think that would add an awesome avenue of storytelling. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T12:05:17-07:00","id":931502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=931364#post931364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hm, that does sound too harsh (and too much paperwork) at this point. I still have time to work with it, but maybe a different curve. All Heroes get +1 to their Autos, Demigods get +3s, and Gods get +5s?</div> </div> </div> </div>So, it would be this scale? Epic 1 = 1, Epic 2 = 2, Epic 3 = 3, Epic 4 = 12, Epic 5 = 15, ect? That would actually result in even higher numbers than normal, with the 10th Dot giving +50 Autos instead of +46. If you mean, Epic 1 @ Hero = 1 and Epic 1 @ God = 5, that might work still? It may make a weird world where Gods are always better than humans at everything even if it's an area they're toss at, but if that's the sort of universe you want to run, go for it!<br /> <br /> So, those suggested changes are less problematic since it scales things slightly better. It does mean however that people in the same tier are very close. So, for example, Heracles at Legend 9 has +40 Successes to his Strength rolls, while Atlas at Legend 12 only has +10 more. It makes Major and Minor Gods far closer in power. If you want to do that however, this is a reasonable hack for the system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=931364#post931364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd imagine that reducing the number of Legend 12 deities would help reign in the Avatar &amp; Ultimate problems. How does Pantheon Politics screw things up? I would think that would add an awesome avenue of storytelling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reducing the number of Legend 12 Gods actually probably makes Avatars and Ultimates problematic in a different way. Essentially, think of Avatars and Ultimates as Nukes. No one uses Nukes because then everyone would be using Nukes. So, having a large number of figures with Avatars/Ultimates actually prevents people from using them. Reducing this number would reduce the amount of 'policing' that could happen. While you would be dealing with <i>less</i> nukes, the people with the nukes would be more likely to use them.<br /> <br /> Pantheon Politics is the key feature of God. In fact, Pantheon Politics is essentially the entire God Tier. The way the game is designed with Avatars and Ultimates means everything is in a perpetual state of cold war enforced by MAD. So, when no one can act against someone else, be they a Titan, another Pantheon, or another God, everything becomes <i>super</i> diplomatic. Talking becomes way, way, way more relevent than hitting stuff.<br /> <br /> If you want to get something done, you can't <i>take</i> it unless you want everything to go to hell in a hand cart. So, let's use Odin wanting Cronus' Sickle for some reason. Odin <i>could</i> do three things to get it. He could a) steal it by force or trickery, b) take it by conquest, or c) ask for it.<br /> <br /> If a) Odin is blocked by one of the Ultimate Perception Theoi without even using their Ultimate Perception. There is only one Odin, and there are several Theoi with this, so statistically, one will notice. (not even counting Arete which means they'd actually all notice due to having a way bigger dice pool) Odin is now caught red handed. Zeus smacks Odin with Justice because he broke one of Zeus' laws.<br /> <br /> Now, back in Asgard, the Aesir are torn. They are loyal to Odin, but Odin <i>did</i> break the law. So, the Aesir now have to decide to either use force, trickery, or diplomacy to get Odin back. Force and Trickery are both contested by the Theoi who are equally powerful. This can get out of hand, someone uses an Avatar, and suddenly you have upwards of thirty Avatars going off and the allied Greek Titans are showing up to throw down to help their younger cousins. Gods Die. This is a bad thing.<br /> <br /> If b) Odin rolls up with his army and the other Martial Gods. The Theoi knew about this ahead of time because of their All-Seeing figures, but also their Prophecy people. Odin's army drops into Olympus via the Rainbow Bridge, and Odin throws his spear on his side meaning they will win. But, wait, hold on, Nike is hanging out with Zeus, so that means the Theoi will win. Paradox. (I'd probably rule in favor of the Theoi there since they're in a Theoi dominated space) Zeus hurls his Thunderbolt, Thor throws his Hammer, Athena runs rampant as Apollo and Artemis rip things up. Odin fights Ares (and probably wins because Ares is a terrible fighter) and someone dies. If Major God, Avatars go off. If Minor God, the Theoi or Aesir have Vengeance or Loyalty, statistically, someone fails a roll, and an Avatar goes off. Back where we were before, we now have upwards of 30 Avatars throwing down, all the Minor Gods are instantly obliterated unless someone is specifically trying to protect them (and even then, if people gang up on them, they will fail even in their Avatar state) and the Theoi allied Titans show up to throw down.<br /> <br /> Gods Die. This is a bad thing.<br /> <br /> And then, c) Odin goes to Olympus as a honored guest protected under Hospitality. Odin explains why he needs Cronus' Sickle, and Zeus thinks about it. While Odin has Ultimate Manipulation and can get Zeus to agree with him, Zeus has Ultimate Charisma so Odin doesn't want to rip Zeus off. Zeus agrees that Odin can use the Sickle for some time, and Odin offers to give Zeus his spear as collateral. Zeus thinks that's a lovely offer, and both of them Pantheon Head it up and complain about things. Odin and Zeus both decide to seal this pact between them (As they now both are best buds due to both of their Epic Socials) and Odin sends Hugin and Munin out to fetch some Scion of theirs. Zeus yells for Hermes until he shows up, and sends Hermes off to gather up one of their Scions.<br /> <br /> Both Scions get dragged, confused, to Olympus to see two probably a bit tipsy Pantheon Heads (who have been arguing with each other about the superiority of beer or wine) who tell them they're getting married. Hera is pulled up from somewhere (as Zeus is the host, their traditions) and the two Scions are married to each other to seal the pact despite any of their comments otherwise.<br /> <br /> Now the Pantheons are allied, no one died, the two Pantheon Heads now expect babies soon to intertwine their lines, and Odin got what he wanted.<br /> <br /> Fighting is a terrible, terrible idea at God, talking things out is king flatly due to the MAD that Gods embody. That is how Pantheon Diplomacy makes God Games super complicated. Now, what I described above in section c) isn't even as complicated as it could be, since now there's fallout to the Aesir running around with a Primordial Neutering weapon, and the Greeks are playing with something that guarentees their victory. (which they can double up on with Nike) Some Gods may be insulted <i>their</i> Scions were not picked for the marriage, some hearts may be broken from the marriage, the couple may hate each other but forced to keep up appearances least the Theoi sick Eros on them to obliterate their opinions and make them whole heartedly in love with each other. ect.<br /> <br /> Edit: And, just to further explain why no one wants outright conflict, everyone's Ultimate Intelligence Gods and Goddesses can explain that this will be the outcome of Pantheons clashing. The same is true even for antagonistic Titans. If the Titan is ever out of the Titanrealm, the Pantheon is instantly aware due to all-seeing figues. Someone uses The Way, and the entire Pantheon ganks the lone Titan. So, Titans are themselves forced to use diplomacy (Except for the more bestial ones like Apep who are not really concerned with talking and more concerned about eating that tasty tasty sun)<br /> <br /> Edit#2: Oh yeah, I forgot to also mention that a lot of the time you don't <i>want</i> to fight each other due to the Epic Social people. No one wants to hurt Baldur because everyone loves Baldur. No one wants to go against Zeus because Zeus Is King. No one wants to spurn Aphrodite because she's the most beautiful thing ever ever ever. No one wants to make... well, actually, Apollo is pretty frequently shit on so much so that he's got some sort of weird Fate about his Socials being terrible. But, you get my point. Epic Socials make you want to make love not war, because even your generals with Epic Charisma are calmed by other people with Epic Charisma and don't <i>really</i> want to hurt them.<br /> <br /> Edit#3: Forgot to explain why Pantheon Politics beaks things. Pantheon Politics becomes the only game in town, that's how it breaks things. Avatars make <i>doing</i> thing so dangerous that no one wants to do them, so everything becomes diplomacy and discussion. It's a big whiplash effect coming from Hero and Demigod where you're out there fighting monsters, when at God it's, 'Hey, so, we're going to a meeting with the Netjer about loaning them Apollo to try to deal with Apep in exchange for a marriage between Apollo and Isis since she's widowed technically. Isis really isn't into it, and Horus is up to something, but Hera is super into it since Apollo doesn't want to marry Isis and she's taking out her spite on him again' or 'So, we're going to need you to go and talk to Ouranos about if he can tell us where Prometheus is hiding.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","user":"Watcher","date":". 07-14-2016, 03:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T12:36:28-07:00","id":931519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=931502#post931502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, it would be this scale? Epic 1 = 1, Epic 2 = 2, Epic 3 = 3, Epic 4 = 12, Epic 5 = 15, ect?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's like <br /> <br /> Epic 1-3 = 1-3<br /> <br /> Demi-hood<br /> <br /> Epic 4 = 7<br /> Epic 5 = 10<br /> Epic 6 = 13<br /> Epic 7 = 16<br /> <br /> God-hood<br /> <br /> Epic 8 = 21<br /> Epic 9 = 26<br /> Epic 10 = 31<br /> Epic 11 = 36<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=931502#post931502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reducing the number of Legend 12 Gods actually probably makes Avatars and Ultimates problematic in a different way. Essentially, think of Avatars and Ultimates as Nukes. No one uses Nukes because then everyone would be using Nukes. So, having a large number of figures with Avatars/Ultimates actually prevents people from using them. Reducing this number would reduce the amount of 'policing' that could happen. While you would be dealing with <i>less</i> nukes, the people with the nukes would be more likely to use them.<br /> <br /> Pantheon Politics is the key feature of God. In fact, Pantheon Politics is essentially the entire God Tier. The way the game is designed with Avatars and Ultimates means everything is in a perpetual state of cold war enforced by MAD. So, when no one can act against someone else, be they a Titan, another Pantheon, or another God, everything becomes <i>super</i> diplomatic. Talking becomes way, way, way more relevent than hitting stuff.<br /> <br /> ~~~<br /> <br /> Both Scions get dragged, confused, to Olympus to see two probably a bit tipsy Pantheon Heads (who have been arguing with each other about the superiority of beer or wine) who tell them they're getting married. Hera is pulled up from somewhere (as Zeus is the host, their traditions) and the two Scions are married to each other to seal the pact despite any of their comments otherwise.<br /> <br /> ~~~<br /> <br /> Edit#3: Forgot to explain why Pantheon Politics beaks things. Pantheon Politics becomes the only game in town, that's how it breaks things. Avatars make <i>doing</i> thing so dangerous that no one wants to do them, so everything becomes diplomacy and discussion. It's a big whiplash effect coming from Hero and Demigod where you're out there fighting monsters, when at God it's, 'Hey, so, we're going to a meeting with the Netjer about loaning them Apollo to try to deal with Apep in exchange for a marriage between Apollo and Isis since she's widowed technically. Isis really isn't into it, and Horus is up to something, but Hera is super into it since Apollo doesn't want to marry Isis and she's taking out her spite on him again' or 'So, we're going to need you to go and talk to Ouranos about if he can tell us where Prometheus is hiding.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Those poor Scions. <br /> <br /> Hm, yeah. I pity the War gods who must feel so useless in these situations, forced to do nothing for ages before they have a real chance to fight.<br /> <br /> It does sound fascinating as a huge Social game, but, given the limitations, has anyone ever thought of just dropping Avatars and Ultimates?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T14:35:40-07:00","id":931596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=931519#post931519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those poor Scions.<br /> <br /> Hm, yeah. I pity the War gods who must feel so useless in these situations, forced to do nothing for ages before they have a real chance to fight.<br /> <br /> It does sound fascinating as a huge Social game, but, given the limitations, has anyone ever thought of just dropping Avatars and Ultimates?</div> </div> </div> </div>That sort of thing's the standard fate of Scions really. Getting married off for alliances is pretty standard in the ancient world for the children of royalty/leadership, with the kiddos of Gods and Goddesses, it's even more common.<br /> <br /> War Gods do seem to have a harder time, but what's good about them is that when something <i>does</i> happen, when the terrible happens, the War Gods are hands down the greatest. They can end wars by demanding champion combat, outmanover anyone, even lay Titans low. The War Gods are a brilliant trump card. They may rarely get involved, but when they do the world shakes.<br /> <br /> But, removing Avatars and Ultimates brings a host of problems with it. Firstly, there's a lot of stuff that's not possible RAW IIRC without Avatars. Bringing the dead back to life for example can't be done without an Avatar or Ultimate. A huge amount of myths don't really make sense as well, since Creation Myths pretty much require Avatars to have happened. What did you do, use Create Earth about five thousand times? Then spend several billion years using Shaping? That's just to build the foundation. Or you can pop The Maker and forge a continent. The Deluge myths can't really work without The Flood too, or when The Dagda held the sun in place for nine months, it's hard to do that without Ultimate Strength. Tezcatlipoca knocking the sun from the sky as a colossal jaguar is difficult without The Beast, ect. The Narrative function of Avatars allows very easy solution to these problems.<br /> <br /> On top of <i>those</i> problems comes the fact you need to find a way to award the Legend 12 Gods and Goddesses something that the Legend 11 Deities don't have. A Legend 11 Goddess can have Rank 10 Epics, the same as a Legend 12 Goddess. What makes the Legend 12 Goddess more powerful is their capacity to use Avatars and Ultimates.<br /> <br /> And then, if Titans don't have Ultimates or Purview Avatars, a lot of their threat is removed. You can just beat them down without any real difficulty. But, if they retain Ultimates and Avatars, the Pantheons have no capacity to compete with them. A Titan of Death could just go, &quot;You all die&quot; to a Pantheon, and without access to Avatars or Ultimates themselves, they have no capacity to resist this.<br /> <br /> A lot of new storytellers are freaked out by the sheer power of Avatars and Ultimates, but they fill a good nieche in the story, and makes the Major Gods terrifying in power. It also helps create the MAD system. (Also, without Avatars, whichever Pantheon has more Gods could steamroll other Pantheons. The Deva, the Shen, and the Theoi are good examples of this. They have so many Legend 9 - 10 figures that they could crush the Aesir, Tuatha, Orisha, Teotl, without any of those Pantheons really able to stop them.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-14T21:43:03-07:00","id":931807,"title":"","content":"The other thing is, this is a game about GODS. If you nerf them so that they can't pull Ultimates and Avatars, or cut down the automatic successes, you remove what makes them Godly. They are supposed to be able to crack the world, toss ships into space, and change the course of rivers - they aren't just glorified adventurers once they get past Hero level. Humans are ants to them. So are most Scions. The only other things they respect are other Gods and the Titans. Playing and running a Scion game means thinking big, which means big rules to cover big deeds. Sometimes those rules are inelegant or flawed [hence all the house rules], but without them, you take the larger-than-life elements out of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5627,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","user":"Purple Snit","date":".  Edited a typo. 07-15-2016, 12:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T08:11:52-07:00","id":932016,"title":"","content":"And Scion (as is) doesn't even have to wait to God, Ultimates and Avatars,; it can START at Hero with concepts that would over-the-top in other games. For example, how about an astronaut Scion of Apollo whose Visitation involved keeping a space shuttle from crashing into Manhattan? At the start of the game, he's America's Shining Son, the Hero Saved the Big Apple... Capitalize on that with a few Social Knacks and some bush league Boons... <br /> <br /> You can think small if you want to and have characters who are neurotic mechanics with daddy issues, but you don't HAVE to do that. After all, not every mythic child of a god/mortal cross has to recapitulate a rags-to-riches story. That's just one mythic path... For every Theseus who has to live in poverty the true ID of his sorta-father is revealed (since he's variously Aegus, Zeus or Poseidon's son...), there'a s Heracles strangling magic serpent demons in his crib....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-15T09:54:56-07:00","id":932064,"title":"","content":"Definitely food for thought.<br /> <br /> We had another session last night. It wasn't much of one since I was coming straight off work, and it was late. Most of it was devoted for transferring over to the JSR boon and knack system. The night before I reviewed everyone's character sheets and identified which ones needed to be traded out since some of them were now part of trees, like Untouchable Opponent. I wrote down what the starting knacks were for each tree and offered them as suggestions. Half my players accepted my recommendations. The other half took the opportunity to completely review the new stuff and changed accordingly. Jamie is becoming quite the sniper, while Elias now has a dozen knacks to work with (his player loves them). <br /> <br /> We managed to move the story forward a little bit. It's now the next morning and was essentially a chance for everyone to do a little role-playing. Leithe is now struggling to balance her divine duties with her career as a musician. Elias called his in-laws in Canada to let them know he was going to be in the US for a lot longer. Vjun &amp; Katya fed their respective pets.<br /> <br /> By far, the most interesting part is when Jamie and Lad interacted. As a quick reminder, Lad is a hero cop, while Jamie is a criminal consultant. They are currently sharing Lad's apartment during this quest. So, in the middle of the night, she stole some of his models (think Warhammer 40,000) and then pelted him with is own models when he left his bedroom. Cue a couple of DEX rolls as they bickered, while Lad tried to re-unite the Band at a diner near the cult meeting point at 7 am. Leithe cussed him out for waking her that early, but they all agreed.<br /> <br /> We ended the session with the Band arriving at the diner with Leithe purposefully running late. Next session should be pure story and with a lot more available time than a quick two hour session.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T12:08:17-07:00","id":932589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=932064#post932064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Definitely food for thought.<br /> <br /> We had another session last night. It wasn't much of one since I was coming straight off work, and it was late. Most of it was devoted for transferring over to the JSR boon and knack system. The night before I reviewed everyone's character sheets and identified which ones needed to be traded out since some of them were now part of trees, like Untouchable Opponent. I wrote down what the starting knacks were for each tree and offered them as suggestions. Half my players accepted my recommendations. The other half took the opportunity to completely review the new stuff and changed accordingly. Jamie is becoming quite the sniper, while Elias now has a dozen knacks to work with (his player loves them).<br /> <br /> We managed to move the story forward a little bit. It's now the next morning and was essentially a chance for everyone to do a little role-playing. Leithe is now struggling to balance her divine duties with her career as a musician. Elias called his in-laws in Canada to let them know he was going to be in the US for a lot longer. Vjun &amp; Katya fed their respective pets.<br /> <br /> By far, the most interesting part is when Jamie and Lad interacted. As a quick reminder, Lad is a hero cop, while Jamie is a criminal consultant. They are currently sharing Lad's apartment during this quest. So, in the middle of the night, she stole some of his models (think Warhammer 40,000) and then pelted him with is own models when he left his bedroom. Cue a couple of DEX rolls as they bickered, while Lad tried to re-unite the Band at a diner near the cult meeting point at 7 am. Leithe cussed him out for waking her that early, but they all agreed.<br /> <br /> We ended the session with the Band arriving at the diner with Leithe purposefully running late. Next session should be pure story and with a lot more available time than a quick two hour session.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a good Session! All of that sounds totally sorted. I'm glad your players seem to be enjoying themselves!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-16T13:41:24-07:00","id":932615,"title":"","content":"Morning, December 15, 2009...<br /> <br /> Snow welcomes the Big Apple as a new day arrives, minus one frost giant. The Band slowly rouse themselves in the morning, unaware that Fate decreed that today will mark a major change for all of them. Jamie 'Moriarty' ends another fitful night sleeping on a cop's couch, lazily pushing the blanket away as she sits up. Before she makes much progress, a clattering at the window draws her attention. Glancing toward the window, she spots a large raven who is pecking at the glass, flapping the snow off his coat. After a moment, Jamie reaches down and grabs her trusty Remington and proceeds to aim the rifle at the offending creature. The moment the barrel swings in its direction, the raven lets loose a loud cry as it flies out of sight. A few seconds pass by with Jamie patiently waiting for proof that the raven was gone.<br /> <br /> Instead, the raven carefully peers back into view, caws again before disappearing back behind the wall.<br /> <br /> With a sigh, Jamie leaves her warm spot on the couch and walks over to the window. She unlocks it before pushing open. The raven flies in with a speed, landing on the couch. It shakes off the snow collected on its feathers before shoots an offended glare at the child of Loki. &quot;How dare you point that thing at me!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> [I'll try to get these done when I can, but, as a writer, making these pieces help build the world in my mind's eye, and, hopefully, entertains y'all.]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6942,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","user":"simison","date":". 07-16-2016, 11:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T20:09:06-07:00","id":935906,"title":"","content":"Another session tonight. I thought it went really well, which is a far cry from my usual anxiety after a night.<br /> <br /> Quick summary: The Band met at the diner, except for Vjun, whose player was absent this night. We had him hang out outside with the animals since they weren't allowed inside. The Band had food and got to know each other a little bit. They agreed that they would meet together twenty minutes before the meeting half a block away. My goal for the diner scene and the in-between time was to emphasize how they were supernatural now. Scions with Cat's Grace noticed how they could walk on ice without issue. Leithe's new powerful hearing allowed her to catch mistakes and played better than ever. Elias had a moment where his glass eye briefly saw in electromagnetic waves, alerting him to his new Perception knacks. Jamie's Frost Immunity (which her player just bought) discovered the cold no longer bothered her. Katya spoke with Amanda, the young woman who was stabbed to death in Central Park a few days ago and is demanding vengeance. <br /> <br /> At the meeting point, they gathered and then headed for the apartment for the actual meeting. Now, the Band had put Elias at the rear to keep an eye out. So, I had the idea that one of the Dark Alf was watching the Band to give Elias a chance to roll. I intended for him to merely notice eyes on him without seeing the Alf. I jokingly thought if he made 10 successes, I'd actually give him a glimpse. To my shock, he rolled 11. So, I gave him a peak at the Alf, who was completely clothed from the sun. Then, to add to my surprise, Elias used his ability to see infrared at him.<br /> <br /> Now, I said there was a little more heat than normal around the Alf's head, a subtle hint about the lengthened ears. Then, I said that the Alf had less body heat than a human's. I thought that this might be the case since Dark Alfs are subterranean creatures and, thus, they operate with less body heat than the average human.<br /> <br /> From there, they went into the meeting. The first half went as expected. They chit-chatted with the two cultists until the leader, William, showed up. He gave a friendly greeting and moved into a speech about how the Band was here for 'change' and that his group/cult was trying to stop the End Times. He explained that he was under divine orders, charged by an angel. They needed to gather the bodies to burn them. To prove himself, he used a ring that was enchanted to have a single fire creation spell. He activated it with the Old Norse word for fire and then deactivated it. After all of that, he offered an official invitation to join him.<br /> <br /> The Band asked for a moment to think, which the cult obliged, leaving them alone in the apartment for a few minutes. During this time, the Band decided to continue playing along, but any actual evil actions were off the table. So, Lad goes out and tells the cult to come back in. And, this is the moment where everything was nearly derailed. Jamie decides to do two things. One, she uses the Unlidded Eye to check out Will's ring. She successfully identifies the ring as a simple relic with the single fire spell, and that all three cultists were mortals. That was fine. The second thing she does is use Overt Order: &quot;Tell me what deity you serve.&quot;<br /> <br /> Will answers, &quot;There is no deity.&quot;<br /> <br /> Confusion abounds with the other two cultists, while the Band immediately jumps on Will's admission. The cult leader immediately defends himself by accusing Jamie of tricks. After a moment of arguing, Will decides to get out and takes his cultists, Ernest &amp; Christine, with him. Lad almost starts combat by physically trying to stop them from leaving. However, Leithe halts them with a combination of Charmer and some comforting words. After successfully preventing them from running out, Leithe fumbles for a bit (her player's anxiety was getting the better of her), but Lad swoops in with Center of Attention. Christine, the female cultist, is hooked, while Earnest and Will are slowly being eased back down. At this point, Will still wants some explanation for what Jamie did to him and why Jamie 'Moriarty' is working with a hero cop. It's here that Lad explains that he doesn't know about the power, but that Jamie is trustworthy because she is secretly a double agent for the cops. Lad wins the roll, so the cultists believe him. (I totally want that to become part of Jamie's legend.) Jamie slides behind them without being noticed and guards the door. By this point, the cultists have been calmed down enough to resume business. The Band accepts the invitation, and Will makes arrangements to add them to guarding the bodies at the Pier, though not to let them deliver the bodies, and to bring in more bodies. <br /> <br /> The session ends there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T19:52:20-07:00","id":937888,"title":"","content":"Alright, I've finished the basic faction lists. It's not completely thorough, but it's enough to work off of.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>The Aesir</u></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Odin</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The All-Father is the only one who is aware of how accurate Snorri was and how close Ragnorak is. Is secretly Freya\u2019s missing husband, Odr. Fated to die at Ragnorak</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Mimir</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Former hostage of Vanir. Decapitated b/c Vanir didn\u2019t want to decapitate Hoenir. Kept alive by Odin\u2019s magic and rests in a well of wisdom and knowledge.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Hoenir</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Handsome yet empty-headed brother of Odin. Hostage to Vanir. Eventually stupidity discovered.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Frigg</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Goddess of Magic. Has nine handmaidens. Rejected Lytir and Vanir to be married to Odin. Final fate unknown.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Baldur</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Son of Odin and Frigg, a bright force yet a warrior consummate. Fated to die before Ragnorak, and return afterward to become the new pantheon head. Father of Lad.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Nanna</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Wife to Baldur. Dies on the same day from grief.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Jord</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Mother of Thor. Earth giantess. Final fate unknown.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Meili</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Brother of Thor. Blank slate.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Hermod</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Son of Odin, one of the first Scions. Fate unknown.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Vali</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Use Scion version, fated to survive Ragnorak.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Hodr</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Blind war god of indiscriminate rage, son of Odin. Fated to slay Baldur by Loki or by himself? Fated to die by Vali\u2019s hand.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Thor</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Plus Hammer, butts heads with Odin, even though he is his son. Fated to die at Ragnorak.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Thrud</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Daughter of Sif and Thor. Fate Unknown.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Magni</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Son of Thor and Jarnsaxa, helped Thor when only three days old. Has the horse Gold-Mane. Fated to survive Ragnorak.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Modi</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Brother of Magni, same lineage, patron of berserkers. Fated to survive Ragnorak.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Heimdall</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Son of the Nine Mothers. Will slay and be slayed by Loki at Ragnorak.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Loki</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Trickster. Fated to die at Ragnorak.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Hel</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Underworld Manager. Survives Ragnorak.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Tyr</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Former ruler of the Aesir. Lost his throne to Odin during the Aesir-Vanir War. Son of Hymir, who was slain by Thor. Fated to slay and be slain by the hellhound Garm.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Zisa</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Wife to Tyr. Fate unknown.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Vidar</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Father of Vjun. Fated to survive Ragnorak.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Bragi</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Poet. Fate unknown.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Idun</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Keeper of the Golden Apples. Has unknown brother who was murdered, Loki accused her of sleeping with her brother\u2019s killer. Fate unknown.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Forseti</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Fair Judge, Son of Baldur and Nanna. Fate unknown.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Sigyn</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Wife of Loki. Will die during Ragnorak.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Vili/Lodurr</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Brother of Odin, helped create man? Slain by Fire Giants.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Dellingr</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">God of the dawn. Fate unknown.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>The Vanir</u></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Lytir</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Head of the Vanir, god of Prophecy, bested Tyr in war, leading to Odin\u2019s ascension. Father of Njord.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Elli</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Lytir\u2019s wife. Goddess of old age. Fate unknown.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Njord</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">God of the seas, temporary husband to Skadi. Fated to survive Ragnorak and return to Vanaheim.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Nerthus</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Earth goddess, former wife to Njord, mother of Freyr &amp; Freya. Chose to divorce Njord instead of joining him with the Aesir, who did not look kindly upon their relationship.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Sif</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Fertility goddess. Fate unknown.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Uller</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Son of Sif by not-Thor, was once incredibly prominent (married to Skadi, after she left Odin). Fate unknown.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Freya (Gefjun)</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Goddess of Fertility, Promiscuous, and Magic. Fate unknown.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Freyr</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">God of Fertility. Ruler of Alfheim. Fated to be slain by Surt.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Skirnir</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Servant of Freyr. Fate unknown.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Gullveig/Heidr</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Goddess of Gold, Magic, &amp; Greed. Survived the Aesir-Vanir War but never agreed to the peace. Wanders the world, causing discord by \u2018empowering\u2019 women.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>The Giants/Devourers</u></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Aegir</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">King of the Oceans, friendly towards the Aesir.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Ran</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Wife of Aegir. More sinister, willing to drown men. Still friendly to the Aesir. Has nine daughters.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Gerd</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Wife to Freyr. Fate unknown.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Fire Giants</u></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Surt</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">King of the Fire Giants, seeks to burn the Nine Worlds. Unlike the Jotuns and Frost Giants who regularly attack Midgard &amp; Asgard, Surt is biding his time, strengthening his forces for the final assault.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Sinmara</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Surt\u2019s wife.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Ice Giants</u></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Skadi</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Avenger, married to Njord, it failed. Had children with Odin before then marrying Uller. Frost giantess.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Monsters</u></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Fenris</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Odin\u2019s killer, Vidar\u2019s target.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Jormungand</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">World serpent. Fated to die by Thor at Ragnorak.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Garm</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Hound of Hel</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><u>Nidhogg</u></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Constantly eating at the World Tree\u2019s roots</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> [Next is to figure out Legend levels for most of the deities.]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6942,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","user":"simison","date":". 07-26-2016, 11:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-26T23:25:26-07:00","id":937954,"title":"","content":"Looks like that was an interesting session! I will be intrigued to see what move your Band makes next.<br /> <br /> Neat list! I don't know how accurate bits and pieces of it are, like Hel's survival or Lytir's defeat of Tyr (thought the whole Tyr-Odin thing was an academic theory not strictly fact) but I expect this is you expanding and fleshing out Norse Cannon for your game?<br /> <br /> Some stated Fate based things I'd add is that Hod is, like Baldur, going to return to life and help reorder the world After The End. I also don't know about Nerthus divorcing Njord, but I'm not great at Norse cannon in such fine detail. Since Njord is returning to Vanaheim and his sister-wife, I would have presumed she was inferred to survive Ragnarok, and for them to become a couple again. Fenris is also Fated to die, I think. I mean, I don't know if it's explicitly mentioned, but it's head gets torn in two.<br /> <br /> And as a random, fun note. Jormungand and Fenris are both probably technically by law members of the Aesir. Now, Jormungand never shows any signs of higher thought, but Fenris does and IIRC is even capable of speech. It can be fun to point out to Scions that they actually <i>do</i> have familial Loyalty to the pair of them. What's great about this is it makes Odin casting them out even more dickish, since Odin is throwing out his blood brother's children from his hall for no actual action of theirs. Fenris, Hel, and Jormungand are three of my favorite characters in Norse Mythology flatly because they are monsters made by Odin out of his attempts to break Wyrd. Fenris and Hel in the very least are shown to be people, who are shaped by Odin's betrayal. Jormungand... well, honestly, he might just be a really big snake, but both of his siblings are capable of higher thought, so he might too.<br /> <br /> Oh, also, another interesting thing. Uller has been Pantheon Head in the past. It's mentioned that one time, Odin was gone for so long people assumed him gone for good, and Uller took over until Odin came back and I think Odin either banished him, or Uller ran off.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T11:25:54-07:00","id":938231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=937954#post937954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Looks like that was an interesting session! I will be intrigued to see what move your Band makes next.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, they're dead set on the social/infiltration route so far. As much as I hate to admit it, they're probably going to get split up in the next session since the cult only uses 4 guards at a time. I'm tempted to have the Band come in conflict with police or some other do-gooders at the Pier for some conflict. If not, then maybe some gangs attack because they've heard about all of this money coming out of the place. We haven't had a combat session since I've restarted the campaign.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=937954#post937954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Neat list! I don't know how accurate bits and pieces of it are, like Hel's survival or Lytir's defeat of Tyr (thought the whole Tyr-Odin thing was an academic theory not strictly fact) but I expect this is you expanding and fleshing out Norse Cannon for your game?<br /> <br /> Some stated Fate based things I'd add is that Hod is, like Baldur, going to return to life and help reorder the world After The End. I also don't know about Nerthus divorcing Njord, but I'm not great at Norse cannon in such fine detail. Since Njord is returning to Vanaheim and his sister-wife, I would have presumed she was inferred to survive Ragnarok, and for them to become a couple again. Fenris is also Fated to die, I think. I mean, I don't know if it's explicitly mentioned, but it's head gets torn in two.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, most of it is from the original myths, other bits were added to make the over mythology more cohesive and original for my campaign. Tyr's fall from grace is one example and is more influenced by the historical data we have as opposed to what the myths present. Once this Band's journey is complete, I'll hang onto this list for other Scion games so I already have the Norse squared away, while my players explore other pantheons.<br /> <br /> And there are a few holes. I forgot to fill in Fenris' doom bit, along with a couple of other things like Nerthus' survival. But, the important point is that I'm no longer going on expeditions throughout the internet, trying to get obscure info. This list forms the core of my Norse Mythology, and what I'll develop upon.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=937954#post937954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And as a random, fun note. Jormungand and Fenris are both probably technically by law members of the Aesir. Now, Jormungand never shows any signs of higher thought, but Fenris does and IIRC is even capable of speech. It can be fun to point out to Scions that they actually <i>do</i> have familial Loyalty to the pair of them. What's great about this is it makes Odin casting them out even more dickish, since Odin is throwing out his blood brother's children from his hall for no actual action of theirs. Fenris, Hel, and Jormungand are three of my favorite characters in Norse Mythology flatly because they are monsters made by Odin out of his attempts to break Wyrd. Fenris and Hel in the very least are shown to be people, who are shaped by Odin's betrayal. Jormungand... well, honestly, he might just be a really big snake, but both of his siblings are capable of higher thought, so he might too.</div> </div> </div> </div>That connection is interesting and will have it make some impact, but I think I'll avoid the revisionism elsewhere.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Watcher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=937954#post937954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, also, another interesting thing. Uller has been Pantheon Head in the past. It's mentioned that one time, Odin was gone for so long people assumed him gone for good, and Uller took over until Odin came back and I think Odin either banished him, or Uller ran off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? I'll double-check that. Off-hand, I'm reminded of Skadi and how she leaves Njord and either goes to Odin or Uller. That might be a holdover fragment from when Uller was in charge.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Found it. Looks like he was temporarily in charge during one of Odin's absences. As such, he really was a deity of great power (or loyalty) at one point. I'll remember to add that to his bio.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6942,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","user":"simison","date":". 07-27-2016, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T09:13:33-07:00","id":938892,"title":"","content":"I've come up with my basic Legend list.<br /> <br /> <u>Legend 12</u><br /> Odin<br /> Frigg<br /> Baldur<br /> Hermod<br /> Thor <br /> Heimdall<br /> Hel<br /> Tyr<br /> Bragi<br /> Njord<br /> Uller<br /> Freya <br /> Freyr<br /> <br /> <u>Legend 11</u><br /> Hodr<br /> Thrud<br /> Magni<br /> Vidar<br /> Idun<br /> Lytir<br /> Elli<br /> Nerthus<br /> Sif<br /> Skirnir<br /> <br /> <u>Legend 10</u><br /> Mimir<br /> Hoenir<br /> Nanna<br /> Modi<br /> Forseti<br /> Sigyn<br /> Dellingr<br /> Gullveig<br /> <br /> <u>Legend 9</u><br /> Jord<br /> Meili<br /> Zisa<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-29T17:12:53-07:00","id":939861,"title":"","content":"<b>Session Results - </b>After successfully becoming part of the cult, the Band prepared to take a shift guarding the Pier. Now, the cult only uses 4 people at one time, and the Band chose not to buckle the rules. So, while the majority of the Band went to the Pier at 4 in the morning, Jamie &amp; Lad tried to procure some more bodies. Katya &amp; Leithe guarded the actual drop-off cargo container, while Vjun &amp; Elias patrolled the perimeter.<br /> <br /> Now, the whole point of this session was to have a big round of combat since they're a big step closer to finding Thor's belt. So, Jamie &amp; Lad are chasing a lead down with a Bloods gang in an abandoned apartment when they get ambushed. At the same time, the Pier is assaulted by another gang. Because of how the turns went, Jamie and Lad finished the apartment showdown before the Pier Assault truly started combat. <br /> <br /> I threw 6 thugs at Jamie &amp; Lad, armed with switchblades, a couple of handguns, and one shotgun. I quickly learned that the book's standard thug profile is woefully inadequate as a challenge against Scions. Three were slaughtered before Lad used his Appearance + Presence to intimidate the rest into surrendering, one thug botching and throwing himself to the floor, begging to be allowed to live.<br /> <br /> 18 thugs are attacking the 4 scions at the Pier, and I have no idea if they'll do any damage. The Band's dodge values are high enough that the thugs don't normally hit without a positive modifier. Other than that, it's all about learning combat rules and powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T00:27:43-07:00","id":939984,"title":"","content":"Yeah you will find that Mortals mean next to nothing when coming up against Scions. You could try to do something to make them more threatening for your next encounter, but you could instead use this as a showcase for your players on how powerful they are. They are unquestionably mighty. <br /> <br /> For example, your Perception Scion who got 11 Successes on a roll? Best possible mortal dice pool for that would be 15 (5 Perception + 5 Awareness + 5 Tool) which is the absolute peak of mortal capacity, with probably a small handful of people with such high ratings. Average roll by someone that amazing, stupendous, and randomly carrying one of the world's greatest pair of binoculars, would be 8 Successes. Your Perception Scion beat them by three Successes, which is pretty big at Hero.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-30T09:01:53-07:00","id":940101,"title":"","content":"Well, the next big combat planned is the zombie invasion in Hell's Kitchen. Even if the zombies provide not much more of a challenge, their sheer numbers should be enough to push the Band out of the basement and onto the streets where they can do some havoc. <br /> <br /> At the very least, I have the fluff reasons for these gang attacks. The Bloods in the apartment were trying to ambush Jamie and Lad and then sell their corpses to create a bigger foothold in the city. The gang attacking the Pier is one of the few that isn't influenced by the Dark Alfs who trick them into attacking to both weaken the Band and the rival gang.<br /> <br /> If there is a combat between this fight and the final battle, I'm definitely using more veteran, combat-oriented thugs to provide some kind of challenge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-11T17:45:19-07:00","id":948963,"title":"","content":"So, we've had to cancel the last two weeks. For once, it's not because of my failing confidence in my ST abilities, like it has been the last two times. This time, it's my players. There was some drama, which can be bad enough on its own, but out of my six players, only one of them doesn't have any kind of mental illness. So, it's acting like a multiplier, and we've needed room for people to cool down before I can bring them together. <br /> <br /> But, I have yet to give up on the game and will try to get a session going next week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-16T21:04:02-07:00","id":952265,"title":"","content":"Sorry about the silence! Was just finishing up a Semester.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=948963#post948963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the next big combat planned is the zombie invasion in Hell's Kitchen. Even if the zombies provide not much more of a challenge, their sheer numbers should be enough to push the Band out of the basement and onto the streets where they can do some havoc. <br /> <br /> At the very least, I have the fluff reasons for these gang attacks. The Bloods in the apartment were trying to ambush Jamie and Lad and then sell their corpses to create a bigger foothold in the city. The gang attacking the Pier is one of the few that isn't influenced by the Dark Alfs who trick them into attacking to both weaken the Band and the rival gang.<br /> <br /> If there is a combat between this fight and the final battle, I'm definitely using more veteran, combat-oriented thugs to provide some kind of challenge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, should be cool! Sheer numbers totally might push them back, but they might also go London Bridge on you and hold a choke point in a very Heroic act echoing that unknown Norseman who held the bridge. Firearms make that sort of thing sort of tricky, but if they can manage to fiddle with Purviews and break some things with Epics, they might hold the line! It might shuffle things up, but it would certainly be a very Norse solution, to simply hold. The Courage and Endurance would help too!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=948963#post948963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, I have yet to give up on the game and will try to get a session going next week.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope everything works out! If not, you have in the very least gotten some Scion experience under your belt, and might be able to try again with a smaller player pool or the like if that makes it easier.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T16:26:28-07:00","id":957909,"title":"","content":"We are having a session tonight! But, minus one player. The drama became too much for them, and Vjun will be disappearing, i.e. Vidar will kidnap him for his own purposes. For the STs out there, how do you handle the characters of dropped players usually? Throw them in a fridge in case of later or give them to the guillotine or something else?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T17:45:34-07:00","id":957952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=957909#post957909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are having a session tonight! But, minus one player. The drama became too much for them, and Vjun will be disappearing, i.e. Vidar will kidnap him for his own purposes. For the STs out there, how do you handle the characters of dropped players usually? Throw them in a fridge in case of later or give them to the guillotine or something else?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would normally just put them on a bus for the time being. Killing a Scion can cause weird story repercussions with player Virtues and the like. It also gives you a familiar NPC to tap into now if need be!<br /> <br /> Hope the session goes well!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T19:20:10-07:00","id":958003,"title":"","content":"It did! Most of it was just learning all of the nuances of Scion combat, and the Band was able to dominate. Which, I think my players needed to help them get back into the game after that long absence.<br /> <br /> I have a question, though. Why would anyone not use double attack per RAW? Even with the -4 penalty to the second attack, it's still a free attack that can do massive damage with a good roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-25T20:11:15-07:00","id":958018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=958003#post958003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It did! Most of it was just learning all of the nuances of Scion combat, and the Band was able to dominate. Which, I think my players needed to help them get back into the game after that long absence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome! Glad to hear it went well for them and yourself!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=958003#post958003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a question, though. Why would anyone not use double attack per RAW? Even with the -4 penalty to the second attack, it's still a free attack that can do massive damage with a good roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would anyone not use a double attack? They forget to, pretty much. That's the biggest reason, especially at higher legends where -4 dice means... nothing at all really. You can't do it if you're doing 'other stuff', like no driving and double attacking IIRC, or making a social roll and hacking someone's arm off. But, there's no real reason not to double attack most of the time. I tend to just forget about it since I play combat characters so rarely.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T15:19:52-07:00","id":972157,"title":"","content":"I'm back...again! Good gravy, I feel cursed the way things have been going on for the past couple of months. Most of it is due to going back to college and one of the players starting a new job. It's played havoc with our scheduling, but I dropped out of a club, so now we can reliably meet on Tuesday.<br /> <br /> But, I still lost another player. This time it was Hel's daughter, so the next session, I'm going to have the ground open up beneath her and have her drop with Hel warning the Band not to pursue. <br /> <br /> Then I'll wrap up the loose ends of that night, and hopefully get the Band closer to the next day. I believe they are trying to interrogate the gang members for info. Sucks to be those guys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T11:48:14-07:00","id":973265,"title":"","content":"Plotting for tonight. It occurs to me, looking over my notes, that this might be a really good opportunity to emphasize the nature of prophecies among the Aesir. The two Scions I have to remove were part of the original prophecy which triggered this campaign. After the interrogations are done (which won't take long, I'm guessing), I'm going to try to get the Band together and have one of the Norse deities visit them. Actually, this could be the first of the Norse culture lessons I was planning. <br /> <br /> The question is, who do I send? I could either send one of the parents and help strengthen an existing parent-child relationship, or I could send someone new, which would help flesh out the pantheon.<br /> <br /> If it's a parent, Heimdall is not a choice, since he's already stretched out his free time. That leaves Baldur, Loki, or Freya. Heh, I see now that I have an even number of 'nice' and 'troublesome' parents. <br /> <br /> Anyway, if it's someone new, the obvious path is to go with someone highly concerned with Fate. Frigg would be a good candidate. If Odin himself showed up, it'd also be a chance to punish the Band for constantly threatening Hugin and Munin, so double bonus. Lastly, maybe it's a good chance to introduce Lytir, former head of the Vanir and god of prophecy. He could plant the Aesir v. Vanir seed.<br /> <br /> So many good choices...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T15:22:27-07:00","id":973432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>simison</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/592622-norse-and-nerves?p=973265#post973265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plotting for tonight. It occurs to me, looking over my notes, that this might be a really good opportunity to emphasize the nature of prophecies among the Aesir. The two Scions I have to remove were part of the original prophecy which triggered this campaign. After the interrogations are done (which won't take long, I'm guessing), I'm going to try to get the Band together and have one of the Norse deities visit them. Actually, this could be the first of the Norse culture lessons I was planning.<br /> <br /> The question is, who do I send? I could either send one of the parents and help strengthen an existing parent-child relationship, or I could send someone new, which would help flesh out the pantheon.<br /> <br /> If it's a parent, Heimdall is not a choice, since he's already stretched out his free time. That leaves Baldur, Loki, or Freya. Heh, I see now that I have an even number of 'nice' and 'troublesome' parents.<br /> <br /> Anyway, if it's someone new, the obvious path is to go with someone highly concerned with Fate. Frigg would be a good candidate. If Odin himself showed up, it'd also be a chance to punish the Band for constantly threatening Hugin and Munin, so double bonus. Lastly, maybe it's a good chance to introduce Lytir, former head of the Vanir and god of prophecy. He could plant the Aesir v. Vanir seed.<br /> <br /> So many good choices...</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are planning to give them some sort of Prophecy, using a God is very tricky. Due to the heavy duty taboos regarding the use of Seidr, any God preforming it is going to be super-super looked down upon. It's an effeminate thing, and the Norse take their gender systems <i>super</i> seriously, at least in the realms of Masculinity. So, while Odin is accused of practicing Seidr, he can't really show up to give Scions a Prophecy, it would be <i>really</i> bad.<br /> <br /> Freya can work pretty well, but you've already had her show up which unless you want her to be very involved, I might not do. Frigg could as you said be a good choice, but she's busy a lot dealing with Odin as the pair of them... like, compete with each other? They have an odd relationship.<br /> <br /> You might want to use a mortal magician of some sort to relay the message, or fall back onto the Ravens. If you want them to take it more seriously, possibly send Odin's Wolves, Geri and Freki, both of whom should be very focused around Greed and Hunger if you want to play them up as characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T16:12:27-07:00","id":973465,"title":"","content":"Oh, not a new prophecy, but discussing the original prophecy. Mainly because two of the originally mentioned Scions have been pulled off the quest, some of the Aesir are getting nervous about Thor's chances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-20T16:21:46-07:00","id":973475,"title":"","content":"Ah, right! Then one of the Deities showing up makes total sense! If you want to give the PCs some help, if one of the War Deities swings by, they could leave some resources such as mercenaries behind for the Band to use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T08:08:01-07:00","id":974421,"title":"","content":"I went with Odin and completely forgot to mention the ravens. Dang it, will save that for next time if Jamie keeps threatening them. Not sure if I talked long enough about prophecy either. I think I should start actively practicing for monologues and speeches from NPCs, not so great at being verbally impromptu. <br /> <br /> Anyway, the Band turned in the (intact) bodies of the gang members who tried to kill them and earned another $50k. I don't think my players understand how many options they have because there was an attempt to persuade the leader to allow them to transport the bodies, which would lead to the final battle. But, William (Cult Leader) argued that it was too soon, and was only negotiated to allowing them to see it in 4 days. Which would be right on the day that everything is supposed to go down. <br /> <br /> None of my players have come up with the idea of taking the sneaky, investigative route. Or beating the crap out of the cult for answers. Wait, Heimdall's kid, Elias, came up with the idea that Lad should seduce the one cultist who has the hots for him. Very big on the social route, now that I think about it. The cultist in question, Christine, does know where the bodies go, even if she's never been in the actual basement with the zombies. So, it's viable. <br /> <br /> Elias' player also mentioned to expect plenty of combat in the next few days. I wasn't planning on it, but it would make sense from a Fate-viewpoint. Especially for a Norse game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T08:16:34-07:00","id":982700,"title":"","content":"Had another session a couple of days ago. <br /> <br /> So, the 5 minute version:<br /> <br /> After finishing their shift at the pier, the two female scions (Jamie and Leithe), who neither have Epic Stamina, had to sleep to prevent dice penalties. Which left the guys awake. So, I had originally had all of this material planned how they would either talk/seduce or sneak their way to the high school where the zombies, the Belt, and the boss is. I was so confident that I was ready for them, only to be derailed by this 'down time'. In hindsight, I should have just jumped to the point where everybody was awake, but I try to let my players do what they want to do. <br /> <br /> So, Elias ended up trailing a tabloid lead about a city of dwarves beneath the city in an abandoned subway tunnel. Although I wasn't planning on it, I decided to take mercy on Elias and allowed him to follow up the trail to a subway area where he could 'feel' something there. Basically, and I'm not sure if this is how it supposed to work, Elias has stumbled upon a Terra Incognita, one that connects to Svartheim, home of the dwarves. He found a rune put on a hidden rock that said dwarves, and, after waiting a couple of hours, found a dwarf walking out. After calming him down, Elias introduced himself, and learned that the dwarf is named Garik. From there, they chatted, establishing a cordial relationship. I didn't intend to explain this this early, but Garik explained that the dark alfs were active in NYC. Ah well.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Lad followed up with the female cultist who had the hots for him. Now, I had planned that this was one of the potential leads to finding the high school and zombies, but Lad said he was not going to try, merely establish a rapport with Christina the cultist. Well, he was successful, successful to the point where the neighbors complained about the racket.<br /> <br /> The session ended with the Band about to regroup with the ladies awake. <br /> <br /> Now, the biggest problem from the session I had was that two of my players feel like the Band has no direction and are frustrated. It's both of my female players, and to further muddle things, one of the male players feels like everything is going fine. <br /> <br /> Therefore, I'm confused. Is it just player activity imbalance? Or am I really too open-ended and need to make a couple of rails for my players?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T21:51:26-07:00","id":983148,"title":"","content":"It sounds like you are too open-ended. When planning a game, I try to have the beginning and end planned out, motivations for the bad guys, and the <i>general</i> plot-line mapped, but leave &quot;wiggle-room&quot; for the PCs to improvise, poke around, and not feel railroaded. But they HAVE to have an idea where things are supposed to be going, or its just &quot;Saturday Night in Toledo, Ohio&quot;, and everyone gets bored, or makes their own trouble. They need to know why they are together, and have a basic clue as to the crisis/problem/whatever that is driving the story, whether it's &quot;Hey, did anyone else see the Zombies on the news?&quot;, or &quot;Why did the Titanspawn try to eat our faces, guys? And why are they all wearing turquoise?&quot; They don't need to play out nap-time, dinner at the greasy spoon, or the train ride to Pocatello, unless something that drives the game is going to happen when they are there. And if they don't get the clues [&quot;I don't watch the news - it depresses me&quot;], then you may have to hit them with a hint brick [&quot;You get a message on your phone from your best friend - something about Zombies trying to eat everyone at the sorority mixer. There is a lot of screaming, and then the phone goes dead.&quot;]. It takes a bit of juggling, but players need to be motivated and guided - they won't usually go looking for the trouble on their own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T22:13:27-07:00","id":983157,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Purple Snit hit the nail on the head. That looks like you played that Session far too open ended. Strict rails are not great, but having 'stuff' planned to throw at the players is a good idea. Making sure there is a healthy supply of hints and clues coming right at them is important when running something 'mystery-esque' as you are doing. You need to keep the players engaged, give them clues, and hints where to go next in-universe. Always make sure they a) have a goal, and b) know some steps to take to move towards that goal.<br /> <br /> Now, don't make it really blatant like one of the Ravens showing up and telling them to do X or go to Y, unless that itself is a clue or something out of the ordinary that will leave them asking questions. Leave hints here and there, have NPCs interact with them. The best thing to do is use these things as rewards or prizes for doing something particularly amazingly well. For example, in the ruined remnants of an ancient Gaulish spring I had left a strange, almost completely worn away painting on the wall. I had been leaving these strange, hint-ridden paintings in all of the underground locations my players had gone into through several stories.<br /> <br /> In this instance, one of my players used a Boon from a houseruled Purview that worked with Art, and Tools, and managed to repair the entire painting from almost nothing due to throwing down something like thirty successes at Legend 4. I retconned my own notes, and made this painting substantially more valuable a clue to make this reward more potent, giving the players a complete depiction of the Gaulish Pantheon, giving them a clue towards the function of the Gundestrup Cauldron which is a large plot point, and revealed to them the identity of a amnesiac NPC they kept meeting multiple different 'shards' of. With this, the players clarified their situation, and had a better grasp on 'what next', giving them information about different situations that could arise in their underground odyssey.<br /> <br /> And, possibly some of the best ST advice I have gotten from Iry is the idea of &quot;Suddenly Ninjas!&quot; which you don't need to use literally. If things ever stall, throw a new problem into the mix. Make things chaotic, dramatic, and throw an infusion into the situation. Your players are sitting around not sure what to do about the cult? When Christina and Lad were meeting up, you could have had the other players catch wind of a hit squad being sent by the cult to kill Christina and Lad both for posing a threat / Christina moving away from the cult's values. This accomplishes bringing PCs back into the same Scene, and then Christina can reveal more plot information in return for being saved. Or, if they fail to save her and Lad, they can overhear the assassins talking about the cult, they can trail the van back, ect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T11:36:24-07:00","id":983429,"title":"","content":"Well, on the plus side, my confidence isn't shattering, so that's good.<br /> <br /> Alright, need more direction. I was thinking about the next session. To solve the immediate problem, I was going to let the Band discuss for a bit about their next step. If it still seems they are unsure of what to do, I was going to have a cultist text Jamie. Previously, Lad and Jamie killed the gang members after them, but then split the bodies (and profit) with the cultist clean-up crew that came to help them. So, I was thinking that one of those cultists would be eager for some money and would try to strike a deal with Jamie. The cultist knows that she wants to see where the bodies are being delivered, so he'll give the location for $100,000. Jamie has already collected $170,000 from previous 'donations', so they have the means. <br /> <br /> How does that sound?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T17:24:08-07:00","id":983623,"title":"","content":"Definitely not trying to shatter your confidence!<br /> I know you can't tell too much here, in case someone from your group reads the storyline, but what's relevant isn't necessarily what the players want to do - they aren't the Storytellers. What's relevant is, what is the story you are trying to write and tell? There needs to be an agreement between ST and players, which is, the ST agrees to provides a fun adventure, and the players agree to play characters that get involved. If they aren't really into playing Scion, then you can't fix that. And if they are, then they need to try to be engaged by the storyline and DO stuff. <br /> Ask yourself: what do you want/need them to do to advance the plot? And how can you make it so that they want to do that? Will the phone call engage them? Will it make it clear why they should be investigating this mystery/situation? If yes, go for it. If no, then you may need to throw a bigger hint brick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5627-purple-snit","name":"Purple Snit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5627_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"309"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T17:45:13-07:00","id":983642,"title":"","content":"Oh, sorry, didn't mean to suggest that you would. As Watcher knows, my first few runs as a ST crashed because my confidence was very shaky and easy to knock over. So, it's nice that I've gotten enough experience that I don't fall into a heap at the first sign of trouble. <br /> <br /> I think it'll work. What I need to do is get them the high school location and get them to stumble onto the zombie horde. That's what they're trying to do is figure out where the bodies are going to. When the Band defeats the aptranger and his zombie horde, they have finished the first campaign. <br /> <br /> And, don't worry, none of them know about this forum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T14:43:17-07:00","id":1103288,"title":"","content":"No, I'm not dead, and no I didn't end the game because my morale broke. Simply put, school become too much of a priority and my players' schedules become increasingly chaotic. So, we had to shut things down. <br /> <br /> However, the game was saved from oblivion by Lad's player. He's been feeling an RPG itch and suggested we get back into things. And, quite bluntly, I refuse to play a different RPG until we finish this campaign. That and seeing Wonder Woman has also put me into a kind of Scion mood. <br /> <br /> So, we've agreed to get the game restarted in the first week of July. The player line-up has shifted again. <br /> <br /> Leithe and Elias are out, while Vjun and (hopefully) Katya is back.<br /> <br /> In other words, the original team is back this time, including the Gambian rat. <br /> <br /> ...I just realized something. I had those two characters get kidnapped by their divine parents to remove them from play. I really should do a couple of individual sessions to bring them up to speed and let them catch up in experience points. <br /> <br /> At the same time, I need to remove Leithe and Elias. I'm tempted to hit the retcon button, but I'll resist that temptation. Maybe I should take over one or both of them. I still think it's really weird when a Band/DM group has the DM/ST playing as one of the companions. But, it'd be an easy way to provide guidance without just throwing random NPCs at the Band. Ideally, this campaign will be concluded in two or three sessions. All they need to do is find the zombie horde, end it, and retrieve the belt, and I'm about to give them a big help for them to get to the right place that I doubt they'll resist. <br /> <br /> As to why Leithe's and Elias' players are gone, well, they had a bad tendency to cause a bunch of drama. So, at the request of a couple of my other players, we're not letting them know about the Scion game. Which, I suspect, is half the reason Vjun's player is returning. <br /> <br /> Thinking on it, I feel like I should do a dream sequence with the Band as a whole and use that as an excuse to relearn the mechanics again. Is that a good idea or a waste of time?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T21:24:59-07:00","id":1103376,"title":"","content":"Hey Simison, no worries, don't be hard on yourself about calling a game due to education stuff. School first is one of the main rules in our groups. It's good you want to finish things up though!<br /> <br /> You could totally do some individual sessions with the pair of them, but, if the scheduling can't work out, you could also sit down with the players shortly before game and just go over things in rough detail with them. Totally bump their exp up to the same as the rest of the group though, having stuff like that not balanced across characters can be tricky for you as the ST as well as be a bit of a downer for the players.<br /> <br /> If you think your players need that little refresher course in the system, totally go with the dream sequence. But you could also give them some little cheat sheets for, &quot;Roll X + Y + D to make an attack,&quot; and &quot;You have X Knacks/Boons, they do Y.&quot; That sort of thing can really help people quickly get back into the swing of things I find. You could even just ease them into things slowly if you don't want to 'waste' time with a dream sequence.<br /> <br /> If there are only a handful of sessions left in your mind, I would just keep the players who left around as DMPCs, it will just make your life easier than having to try to write them out or something similar. I'm normally not very big on DMPCs, but this isn't a bad situation for them to come up.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-14T08:11:56-07:00","id":1103499,"title":"","content":"Alright, I guess it'll be a good chance to learn how to play as DMPCs. They'll also improve the Band's chances at containing the zombie horde. <br /> <br /> And hopefully I'll be able to get those sessions in. I already have one arranged for Vjun who's player is coming over tonight. <br /> <br /> I distinctly remember creating a Scion Cheat sheet, so, if I can find it, I will definitely print out some copies for the game. Fairly certain it's on my laptop.<br /> <br /> The only new addition I want to add to the saga affects Jaime. Jaime's player is my wife, and she loves thunderstorms. So, I have a strong urge to have it that Jaime was originally Thor's daughter, but bargains were made and Loki was allowed to adopt her. Now, I know this won't affect Jaime's skill set, but I think it offers a rich story opportunity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T11:42:35-07:00","id":1104393,"title":"","content":"Reviewed my notes. Vjun needs at least two sessions, and Katya needs at least one. I'll work on that in the next two weeks before the actual game starts. <br /> <br /> I did find my cheat sheet on my laptop. I'll do a more thorough review of it to see if I need to add anything before the sessions.<br /> <br /> I'm also going over my mythology. Does anyone know what happened to the earliest members, like Buri, Bor, and Bergelmir? When the Band does get higher-powered, I want them to at least know that they have the potential to start their own new pantheon. And I think meeting some of these ancients could help with that since they transcend the titles of Vanir and Aesir. I'm imagining Odin having the Band try to find Buri as he becomes desperate for anything to stop or overcome Ragnorak. The Band find Buri, but he doesn't care and then puts the idea of them starting their own pantheon to save their own hides.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T16:15:19-07:00","id":1104521,"title":"","content":"Buri and Bor seem like prime Titan Avatar material to me. They're both older figures who are directly descended from Ymir (definitely an Avatar) and don't do much beyond being the ancestors of the 'modern' Aesir. They're certainly never given more than a couple lines in what sources we have about Norse myth.<br /> <br /> Back when JSR was still a thing I asked about hypothetical Norse Avatars for their Creation Titanrealm and they suggested Buri, possibly representing parthenogenesis since he was created by one parent and went on to create a son (Bor) without a mother being mentioned. And being Ymir's son (according to at least one source) he could also fit into a Frost Titanrealm as well.<br /> <br /> If anything Bor has even less information about him than Buri, only being referenced in part of the Prose Edda and never again. So basically you can do whatever you want with him and unless you go really crazy you can probably justify it.<br /> <br /> Bergelmir on the other hand is a frost giant and, given that he's Ymir's grandson, he's probably one of the older ones. If you don't want to make him an Avatar you could probably call him a leader among the giants, maybe a bit stronger than an average one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4010-thenotorioussmp","name":"TheNotoriousSMP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-22T10:44:53-07:00","id":1106637,"title":"","content":"I keep forgetting that Titans are weird in Scion. Regardless, thanks for the suggestions. I might save Buri for when the Band becomes demigods and get promoted to fighting the more serious threats in Scion. Bor might be introduced earlier since I'll treat him like a deity as opposed to a titan avatar, though I'll need to come up with an idea of what he's been up to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-27T17:49:04-07:00","id":1108571,"title":"","content":"Had a solo session with Vjun. Given how weird his departure from the Band was, it was a little disjointed. The scenario is that Vidar has temporarily abducted his son to teach him his powers and, more importantly, his duty in dispensing justice. Vidar transports Vjun in front of an abandoned warehouse. Vidar tells his son that there are two kidnappers inside, and their murdered kidnapee. Vidar charges Vjun to figure out which of the two actually killed the young woman and to avenge her upon her killer. <br /> <br /> I took the chance to show off Vjun's new empowered senses thanks to his Epic Perception. He advanced inward and came to a partition wall dividing the warehouse in half. Vjun hears the kidnappers, one of them panicking while the other regretful he didn't get a chance to rape his victim. Unable to figure out who did the deed through eavesdropping, Vjun has his pet ferret, Dar, spy over the wall before making his entrance. <br /> <br /> The two kidnappers are confused but none too happy to see him and make threats. Mr. Panick denies the kidnapping, but Vjun obviously doesn't buy it. Mr. Regret promptly attacks with his knife. With a good roll, Vjun not only disarms him, but kicks him crashing into the partition wall. Unnerved by how easily his companion goes down, Mr. Panic doesn't even try to fight, allowing Vjun to continue his investigation. Mr. Regret does get back up, but is covering his bleeding head with his main hand.<br /> <br /> After a bit of talk, Vjun has Dar check the body, who tells him that the body was stabbed. Vjun notes Mr. Regret's knife and the old blood on his hand. Utilizing his Justice power Judgement, Vjun accuses and verifies that Mr. Regret did murder the young girl. <br /> <br /> Vjun promptly tackles and kills Mr. Regret with his own knife. Mr. Panic tries to make a run for it, but Vjun shoots an arrow into the man's thigh. Vjun takes a moment to make sure Mr. Panic wasn't working for anyone else (he wasn't) before heading for the exit, ready to call the police. <br /> <br /> Waiting for him at the warehouse's entrance is Vidar, who is pleased with his son's actions. There is now a mahogany table in front of the exit doors with two goblets on it. Vidar offers his son a celebratory drink but warns him that one of the goblets is poisoned. Vjun has his ferret smell the drinks, and Dar warns him that the left drink smells foul. Trusting in his divine lineage, Vjun promptly drinks the foul drink. Vidar is very happy with this decision, explaining that both goblets were poisoned but Vjun is immune. <br /> <br /> Vjun's last trial is to move the table out of the way. Now, the goal was to have Vjun learn and use his uplifting might knack. Instead, Vjun slams his fist against the table again and again, until he breaks it apart. Vidar gives Vjun the warehouse's address to give to the police. Vjun makes the call, and the session ends. <br /> <br /> Overall, I am very pleased with how the session went. Even though Vjun is a Loner, he did show concern for his Bandmates at a couple of points during the session. More importantly, given the way that Vjun handled his tasks, Vidar is now very pleased with his son instead of being disappointed with him before. Vjun earned back a Willpower dot because of his nature. Thinking on it, Vjun might have done so well that Vidar might give a small gift to his son. I'll have to think on it.<br /> <br /> Now, one thing that came up that I wasn't ready for was the ancient Norse attitude toward rape and how ancient justice relates to it. I'm not sure off-hand, and will take a look before the next session but does anyone know?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-28T07:30:03-07:00","id":1108753,"title":"","content":"I've done some research since then. There are essentially two kinds of rape: rape against non-Norse and Norse. Against Norse, it's a crime complete with punishments and social ostracization. Against anyone else, it's a free-for-all.<br /> <br /> So, in the previous case, had Mr. Panic raped his victim before Mr. Regret killed her, either Vidar would brush it off as 'outside his jurisdiction'. Or Mr. Panic would be expected to pay a huge fine, the victim's father would have the right to proscribe the punishment, or Vjun, as the 'judge', could inflict whatever consequence he believed fitting.<br /> <br /> Actually, since I specifically put the victim and one kidnapper into Vjun's 'jurisdiction', then that first option wouldn't have applied.<br /> <br /> Also, I am actually really happy with my decision to make Tyr the original King of the Aesir. It adds a new dynamic between him and Odin. Tyr is secretly resentful of Odin supplanting him, but, as a god of justice, Tyr would never let his emotions to cloud his responsibilities even as he yearns for his old position. And, it adds another layer of nuance to Odin's rule because Thor is also frustrated with Odin. So, with two Legend 12 deities frowning at him, Odin's position is not completely ironclad.<br /> <br /> Furthermore, I found a solution to Garm. My research indicates that Garm seems to be nothing more than a different name for Fenris, which is why Garm attacks Tyr during Ragnorak. I actually support how WW handled it by making Garm the first of the Fenrir, which explains why he attacks Tyr. It's to avenge his father's imprisonment.<br /> <br /> ~~~<br /> <br /> Some thoughts on how the kids are influencing their parents:<br /> <br /> Baldur - He would love nothing more than to add a new son to his family and Forseti finally having another surviving sibling. To that end, Baldur is keeping an eye out for ways to safeguard Lad through Ragnorak, but isn't sure what the best method is. Purposely triggering Ragnorak is off the table because there are no guarantees either Forseti or Lad would survive, and it would guarantee the death of his beloved wife Nanna. But invoking Prophecy and Fate to secure Lad's fate is like playing the lottery. Sure, there's a chance it'll work out this time, but much more likely death is in the works. Thus, Baldur remains alert but uncertain.<br /> <br /> Vidar - While no one is sure how Ragnorak will occur, the fact that Vidar knows he will survive has given him a very forward-thinking perspective. He's actively trying to shape the new pantheon that will survive Ragnorak. Truth be told, he would love to replace Baldur as the new pantheon's head, but he doesn't want to challenge fate, until after Ragnorak has passed. In this line of thought, Vidar sees Vjun as an opportunity to further cement Vidar's future status. If he can't be king, he will be something else that is powerful and influential.<br /> <br /> Hel - Katya is another piece, nothing more. Hel thinks of herself as truly eternal. She will survive Ragnorak, she will survive anything, she simply will be. <br /> <br /> Loki - He has always danced the line between mischief and evil. But as Ragnorak approaches, he is slowly losing the battle as he falls toward evil. Adopting Jaime is yet another ploy to save himself from death and to re-establish himself as something more honourable. Yet, for all of his cunning, he is as clueless as Baldur on how he can achieve his goals. Worse, Sly also exists in this game and will be indirectly nudging Loki toward his doomed fate. <br /> <br /> ~~~<br /> <br /> I've also decided that Leithe and Elias will leave after the zombie outbreak and will join the rival band, which will include Eric from the core series. After some thought, I'm leaning towards Vali being the fourth member of that band. Emphasis is on rivalry and not villainy, so Sly might end up with his own Band of questionable Aesir kids.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6942,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","user":"simison","date":".  More thinking. 06-28-2017, 02:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-19T12:35:49-07:00","id":1220307,"title":"","content":"Truly, this is the game that never dies. So, after another hiatus (in which I have completed my education), the game returns. And promptly zoomed to the finish line. My original idea to kick the plot into action worked extremely well.<br /> <br /> One of the cult members, Earnest contacts the Scion of Loki, Jamie. For $100k, he offers the location of where the bodies have been disappearing too. After consulting the Band, Jamie agrees to meet him to haggle. Haggling is Manipulation and Presence, right? They meet in a schwarma shop, the haggling occurs, and they get the info for $40k. The bodies are going to a high school of environmental sciences. They spend the next half an hour (in-game time), scouting the place out and avoiding suspicion. Vjun climbs up to the roof, Katya's pet rat is sent into the sewers, and Jamie looks for a way to sneak in. Lad stays with the cars (his player is absent) and Shauna (formerly Leithe) returns and supports Jamie's attempts.<br /> <br /> They locate a door in the back to get into after the rat fails to find a sewer infiltration. (I honestly could not think of a reason a street sewer grate could lead into a dry entrance into the building.)<br /> <br /> After some stealth and lockpick rolls, the three ladies enter the door, which leads to the basement. And promptly get a couple of warning signs of evil lurking at the bottom of the stairs. They hold to allow Vjun to catch up before stealthing down the stairs. Down there, they promptly find a zombie horde of 91, the last zombie being created right before their eyes by the campaign boss, a Legend 3 Aptranger. Although I rolled contested rolls, the boss fails to notice them. Seeing Thor's belt on him, the Band, in true Norse fashion, open fire.<br /> <br /> Thus begins combat that I'm not really prepared for, but we powered through anyway. Hiccups include forgetting about the Onslaught penalty, forgetting that certain actions lower DV, multi-action in combat, and people can move and action. Thankfully, the zombies, despite being tough, weren't able to do much damage to the Band. The boss, caught thoroughly off-guard, wasn't doing much either. Yet, neither was the Band doing much damage to the horde.<br /> <br /> Finally, Jamie sets up a plan to set fire to the basement through the use of a couple of Chaos boons and a lighter. Vjun and Katya wrestle the belt away from the boss, while Shauna runs to set off the fire alarm to get the civilians to run. The session ends wit the the Band escaping the basement, where everything is now on fire.<br /> <br /> Here's my dilemma. According to the rules, the zombies appear able to simply ignore the fire damage with soak without penalty. Which means that horde is about to spill out into the streets of NYC. Am I reading this right?<br /> <br /> EDIT: To expand on this (while I clean up a few errors, man do I hate typing one-handed), a zombie has a natural soak of 5L. The game suggests that standing in a bonfire will cause 4L/action. And it is explicitly stated that environmental damages are soakable.<br /> <br /> My current solution is to essentially reduce a zombie's soak down to 1B/1L to represent the fire eating away at their defenses, blaming necromancy magic as the reason that they're not slowing burning away.<br /> <br /> I like this solution for two reasons. One, it does not simply ignore what Jamie did during the last session. She has crippled the entire zombie horde. However, by letting the horde survive the flames, it still leads to a potential massive battle on the streets where the World can see the Band fighting the horde. After all, this is what I intend to be the big event that triggers the Scions being promoted to Legend 3. Also, I want Lad a chance to shine in combat.<br /> <br /> The only other mechanic I might introduce is the zombies slowly being damaged by the fire. Say, 1 Bashing damage every 6 ticks. I'm not sure this is necessary. Because, while the Band might be overwhelmed, if the fighting does hit the streets, I will throw in the NYPD to back-up the Band. Not sure, I think I need to roll a few practice rounds to get a good feel for what's necessary.<br /> <br /> Another question, does a single-die stunt also give a Legend point? If so, do Scions ever run out of LP?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6942,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","user":"simison","date":". 05-20-2018, 02:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-25T21:13:14-07:00","id":1222162,"title":"","content":"It took almost three years, but I've completed my first campaign as a Storyteller. <br /> <br /> When it became clear that the fire alone wouldn't be enough to put an end to the zombie horde, Jamie, Daughter of Loki, reacted quickly. She had Lad, Son of Baldur, barricade the back entrance with a car as they secured Thor's belt. Pulling off a drift and reverse, Lad got his car into position in seconds. At the basement's other entrance, the door was closed and guarded by Shauna, Daughter of Freya, and Elias, Son of Heimdall (who's player returned for this final session).<br /> <br /> With the fire alarm tripped last session, the high school was slowly being evacuated while the Band tried to keep the horde contained. The big struggle happened at the rear entrance where the boss made his way to the door. As an Aptranger with Epic Strength 2, he began pounding away at the metal door to break it open. The Band responded swiftly after a couple of good Awareness rolls, leaving Katya, Daughter of Hel, and Vjun, Son of Vidar, to guard this entrance (both of their players were absent at this time). Jame took fire support with her sniper rifle, while Shauna shepherded the students and adults to safety. Most of the action was on Lad and Elias as they tried to counter the boss' strength. <br /> <br /> Discovering the power of uplifting might, Lad stopped the Aptranger's progress by stacking a car on his own SUV, just as Elias botched a roll that saw him crush the SUV instead of holding it against the door. For a brief moment, the boss was almost able to escape until Lad dropped the second car down, throwing the boss back into the basement. Not content with this, Lad would add two more dumpsters to this barricade. Unable to counter, the Aptranger gave up and headed to the other entrance and began breaking down that door. <br /> <br /> Jamie and Elias went to Katya's and Vjun's aid, while Lad went to speed up the evacuation. After some contested strength rolls, the door was about to collapse between the forces hammering at it. At this stage, Jamie decided that it would be better to secure the belt with Lad coming to guard her. For the first time, I got to see Virtue in action as Courage yelled at them to stay in the fight. With willpower spent, they fled the scene with Norse ichor angry at them. <br /> <br /> Yet, the situation was far more in the Band's control. After 20 minutes of being on fire, the zombie horde was skinless and burning through muscle. In another 10 minutes, they'd be reduced to immobile bones. When the boss finally broke open the door, his health had been consumed by the blaze. He tore open the door only for Elias to falcon punch his skull into oblivion. The boss was dead. Containment continued as zombies attempted to move through the new hole in the door. However, as equally worn down by the flames, they were easy prey to Vjun's arrows and Katya's scythe. When the sound of police sirens reached the Band, they decided it was time to leave. Stacking two vending machines in front of the broken entrance, they also resisted the call of Courage to flee the scene.<br /> <br /> Combat over, Hugin and Munin contacted the Band and directed them to the Egyptian obelisk in Central Park. There, they met Magni, Son of Thor, on his horse. After giving the belt to him (with quite a bit of suspicion on Jamie's party), Magni rode out before the Bifrost grabbed him. Left with a small crowd of onlookers, the Band attempted to explain this away, Huginn warned them to step away from the crowd and prepare for a trip.<br /> <br /> In a moment, the Band was engulfed in the Bifrost and sped past Yggdrasil before arriving before Heimdall's hall. There, they could hear the sounds of battle as the Jotuns battled outside the walls of Asgard. With not much time, the parent of each Scion greeted and expressed praise (or as much praise as they were willing). Told they had earned a boon, they were sent back to the safety of Midgard. Dropping right back in front of the crowd of onlookers. The campaign ended with most of them launching into a pose with a big, 'TA-DA!' <br /> <br /> With that, the Band became Legend 3.<br /> <br /> ~~~<br /> <br /> Now, I'm not sure if this was a good idea or not, but I ruled that since the Band found the belt and saved Thor, they had earned 5 dots worth in birthrights. One of them immediately upgraded his bow to fire infinite arrows and could magically conceal itself. Another one wants to turn her scythe into a gun scythe, a la RWBY. <br /> <br /> The others need more time to decide what gifts they have earned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-19T21:11:43-07:00","id":1255648,"title":"","content":"After changing jobs, my and my friends are getting back into the swing of RPGs. We have three lined up: a BESM anime campaign, Vampire the Masquerade, and then the second round of my Scion campaign. My new job allows quite a bit of thinking time, which has swung toward the Scion campaign. <br /> <br /> The broad strokes is that the cult is now trying to assassinate the Mayor of NYC. Since they know they can't go toe-to-toe with the Band, they are hiding behind a powerful patron. So, I'm aiming for a more Social campaign with less combat. I intend this to be the most human campaign of this game. After this, I'm just going to slowly up the weird/supernatural factor. It's also a chance for the Band to practice politics on a city stage before cutting their teeth on god politics. (And let me practice that as a DM).<br /> <br /> Not to say there won't be combat. Mid-way through the campaign, I'm going to introduce who I've nicknamed the Scion Reaver. It's a Daughter of Hodr, who is actively trying to start Ragnorak. Since her father is fated to return after Ragnorak, she believes she's guaranteed to survive as well. Since she isn't that powerful (I'm trying to make her just a little stronger than the entire Player Band as a miniboss), she is hunting other Scions. I'm using her to introduce the Rival Band ( who is hunting the Reaver) and get the Band thinking about their own Ragnarok fates. <br /> <br /> I'm going to have two Ragnorak strikes: if the Mayor is assassinated and if the Scion Reaver kills one Scion from either Band.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6942-simison","name":"simison","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6942_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}